<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Abstract</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We introduce Adaptive Filter Attention (AFA), a novel attention mechanism that incorporates a learnable dynamics model directly into the computation of attention weights. Rather than comparing queries and keys directly, we model the input sequence as discrete observations of a linear stochastic differential equation (SDE). By imposing a linear dynamics model with simultaneously diagonalizable state matrices and noise covariances, we can make use of a closed-form solution to the differential Lyapunov equation to efficiently propagate pairwise uncertainties through the dynamics. Attention naturally arises as the maximum likelihood solution for this linear SDE, with attention weights corresponding to robust residual-based reweightings of the propagated pairwise precisions. Imposing an additional constraint on the state matrix’s eigenvalues leads to a simplified variant with the same computational and memory complexity as standard attention. In the limit of vanishing dynamics and process noise, and using a small-angle approximation, we recover ordinary dot-product attention.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Self-attention has become the dominant paradigm for sequence modeling due to its parallelism and scalability. However, this parallelism comes at the cost of losing the recursive structure that RNNs naturally impose, which provides an implicit temporal regularization that encourages consistency over time. State space models (SSMs) offer a complementary approach: they retain temporal structure through shared linear dynamics while supporting parallel training via convolutional implementations. However, most SSMs assume deterministic dynamics, limiting their ability to capture stochasticity and uncertainty. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Our goal is to bridge these two paradigms. We view self-attention as a form of filtering: it selectively averages across inputs, denoising by pooling information from similar states. However, unlike Kalman Filtering, standard attention does not explicitly propagate states through time. This motivates incorporating explicit temporal structure—through known or learned dynamics—into attention, restoring the inductive bias that standard attention loses by forgoing recurrence. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">This technical report is structured as follows: 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminaries ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold">Section <span class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></span>: Preliminaries</a> 
<br class="ltx_break">We introduce the model setup and review standard results for propagating covariances through linear SDEs. We then discuss the batch maximum likelihood estimator and its connection to the Kalman Filter. Next, we derive a closed-form solution of the differential Lyapunov equation for diagonalizable systems with simultaneously diagonalizable process and measurement noise covariances. Finally, we discuss an adaptively reweighted MLE that reweights propagated covariances using the pair-wise residuals, and its relationship to the iteratively reweighted least squares (IRLS) algorithm and a robustified form of the Kalman Filter. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><a href="#S3" title="3 Adaptive Filter Attention ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold">Section <span class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></span>: Adaptive Filter Attention</a> 
<br class="ltx_break">We generalize the robustified MLE to a tensor form of attention, and briefly analyze its time and memory complexity. We show that the algorithm can be simplified to a form with the same time and memory complexity as standard attention, through the use of convolutional kernels for the (diagonalized) matrix exponential and pair-wise propagated covariances, and by imposing additional structure on the linear SDE. We show that this formulation reduces to a complex-valued variant of standard attention in the case of a skew-symmetric state matrix and normalized inputs. We then describe an implementation of this algorithm, and an unrolled, recursive approximation for inference. We describe basic experiments on simple simulated linear dynamical systems. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><a href="#S4" title="4 Radial-Tangential Model ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold">Section <span class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></span>: Radial-Tangential Model</a> 
<br class="ltx_break">We generalize the SDE model from <a href="#S3" title="3 Adaptive Filter Attention ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref">Section <span class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></span></a>, which assumed isotropic noise, to allow for separate noise covariances in the tangential and radial directions. We show that the propagated covariances in this case can be written in closed-form for the case of diagonal plus rank-1 covariances that co-rotate with the dynamics. We derive a form of attention that solves the MLE while respecting the geometric constraints imposed by the assumed dynamics model, and compare it to the standard Transformer architecture. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><a href="#S5" title="5 Related Work ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold">Section <span class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></span>: Related Work</a> 
<br class="ltx_break">We overview related work, including classical methods for filtering and adaptive filtering; the use of neural networks for modeling and filtering dynamical systems; neural state space models; connections between attention and structured state space models; related architectures; and various other topics. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><a href="#S6" title="6 Discussion and Conclusion ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold">Section <span class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></span>: Discussion and Conclusion</a> 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Background ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix A</span></a><span id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">: Background</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">We briefly overview basic background on linear systems, stochastic processes, the Kalman Filter, adaptive filtering, the attention mechanism, and neural state space models. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Additional Material ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix B</span></a><span id="S1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">: Additional Material</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">We cover some additional topics, including a separable approximation of the propagated precision kernel, discussion of normal plus rank-1 noise covariance, and the expressivity of our structured SDE model.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">
<span id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="S1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Note:</span> This technical report describes ongoing work. Evaluation on real-world datasets is in progress and will be reported in future work.</span>
</span></p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Preliminaries</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We review standard results on vector SDEs and linear Gaussian filtering. The reader familiar with these topics may skip to <a href="#S3" title="3 Adaptive Filter Attention ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref">Section <span class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></span></a>. Additional background material can be found in <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Background ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix A</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Model Setup and Definitions</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a linear time-invariant (LTI) Itô stochastic differential equation (SDE):</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}(t)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}(t)dt+\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(t),\quad\mathbf{z}(t_{k})=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}(t_{k})+\mathbf{v}(t_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}(t)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}(t)dt+\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(t),\quad\mathbf{z}(t_{k})=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}(t_{k})+\mathbf{v}(t_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the latent state, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>th measurement, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is the state matrix, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> is the input matrix, and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐂</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is the output matrix, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{w}(t)\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I}dt)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{w}(t)\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I}dt)</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard Wiener process (Brownian motion), <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}:=\mathbf{B}\mathbf{B}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>𝐁𝐁</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}:=\mathbf{B}\mathbf{B}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the continuous-time process noise covariance, and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}(t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}(t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> is zero-mean Gaussian measurement noise with covariance <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}(t_{k})\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}(t_{k})\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{R})</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">With initial condition <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, the state at a later time <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}&gt;t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}&gt;t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written explicitly using the matrix exponential and an Itô integral:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{j}-t_{i})}\mathbf{x}(t_{i})+\int_{t_{i}}^{t_{j}}e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{j}-s)}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(s)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{j}-t_{i})}\mathbf{x}(t_{i})+\int_{t_{i}}^{t_{j}}e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{j}-s)}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=s-t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=s-t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, this is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{i})+\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{\mathbf{A}(\Delta t_{ij}-\tau)}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{i})+\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{\mathbf{A}(\Delta t_{ij}-\tau)}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t_{ij}=t_{j}-t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t_{ij}=t_{j}-t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Given <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can estimate <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> using the matrix exponential:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j}):=e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j}):=e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Likewise, if we measure <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the measurement matrix <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐂</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is square and invertible, we can estimate the latent state <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, or equivalently <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{C}(t_{i}):=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{C}(t_{i}):=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, by computing a “pulled-back” or "pulled-forward" measurement:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{i}(t_{j}):=\mathbf{C}e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{C}^{-1}\mathbf{z}(t_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{i}(t_{j}):=\mathbf{C}e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{C}^{-1}\mathbf{z}(t_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Propagation of Uncertainty</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that the state at time <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{i})+\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}\,d\mathbf{w}(\tau)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{i})+\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}\,d\mathbf{w}(\tau)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The covariance of the integral term is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t_{ij}):=\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\left(\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau_{1}}\mathbf{B}\,d\mathbf{w}(\tau_{1})\right)\left(\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau_{2}}\mathbf{B}\,d\mathbf{w}(\tau_{2})\right)^{\top}\Bigg]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t_{ij}):=\mathbb{E}\Bigg[\left(\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau_{1}}\mathbf{B}\,d\mathbf{w}(\tau_{1})\right)\left(\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau_{2}}\mathbf{B}\,d\mathbf{w}(\tau_{2})\right)^{\top}\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{Q}e^{-\mathbf{A}^{\top}\tau}\,d\tau,\quad\mathbf{Q}=\mathbf{B}\mathbf{B}^{\top}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐁𝐁</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{Q}e^{-\mathbf{A}^{\top}\tau}\,d\tau,\quad\mathbf{Q}=\mathbf{B}\mathbf{B}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We will refer to this as the backward-propagated state covariance. As the system evolves, the state distribution evolves as:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}_{F}(\Delta t_{ij})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}_{F}(\Delta t_{ij})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where the forward-propagated state covariance is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{F}(\Delta t_{ij})=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t_{ij})e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}\Delta t_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{F}(\Delta t_{ij})=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t_{ij})e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}\Delta t_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\left[\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{Q}e^{-\mathbf{A}^{\top}\tau}\,d\tau\right]e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}\Delta t_{ij}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\left[\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{Q}e^{-\mathbf{A}^{\top}\tau}\,d\tau\right]e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}\Delta t_{ij}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{\mathbf{A}(\Delta t_{ij}-\tau)}\mathbf{Q}e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}(\Delta t_{ij}-\tau)}\,d\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{\mathbf{A}(\Delta t_{ij}-\tau)}\mathbf{Q}e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}(\Delta t_{ij}-\tau)}\,d\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Using the change of variables <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\Delta t_{ij}-\tau\implies ds=-d\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\Delta t_{ij}-\tau\implies ds=-d\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and flipping the limits, we get:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{F}(\Delta t_{ij})=\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{\mathbf{A}s}\mathbf{Q}e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}s}\,ds." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{F}(\Delta t_{ij})=\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{\mathbf{A}s}\mathbf{Q}e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}s}\,ds.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which is a solution of the <span id="S2.SS2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">differential Lyapunov equation</span>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{ds}\mathbf{V}_{F}(s)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}_{F}(s)+\mathbf{V}_{F}(s)\mathbf{A}^{\top}+\mathbf{Q}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐐</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{ds}\mathbf{V}_{F}(s)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}_{F}(s)+\mathbf{V}_{F}(s)\mathbf{A}^{\top}+\mathbf{Q},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">with initial condition <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{F}(0)=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{F}(0)=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Recall that the estimate of the state is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j}):=e^{\mathbf{-A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=\mathbf{x}(t_{i})+\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j}):=e^{\mathbf{-A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=\mathbf{x}(t_{i})+\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Hence, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t_{ij})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t_{ij})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where:
<math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies the uncertainty of the estimate <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> of the state <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> at an earlier time <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, given the state <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> at a later time <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Conversely, if we observe the state at an earlier time <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and wish to quantify our uncertainty about an estimate of its state at a later time <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. the causal case), we can switch indices <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> and solve for <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{i})=e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{i}-t_{j})}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})+\int_{t_{j}}^{t_{i}}e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{i}-\tau)}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{i})=e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{i}-t_{j})}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})+\int_{t_{j}}^{t_{i}}e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{i}-\tau)}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{j})+\int_{0}^{-\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{j})+\int_{0}^{-\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{i})-\int_{0}^{-\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{i})-\int_{0}^{-\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.9" class="ltx_p">So:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}_{B}(-\Delta t_{ij})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}_{B}(-\Delta t_{ij})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.10" class="ltx_p">(Note that, according to our definition, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t_{ij}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t_{ij}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> in the causal case, so <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\Delta t_{ij}=|\Delta t_{ij}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\Delta t_{ij}=|\Delta t_{ij}|</annotation></semantics></math>.) 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Hence, in an LTI with Gaussian noise, the covariance of the state propagated forward in time under <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the covariance of the state propagated backward in time under <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We again form an estimate:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})=e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=\mathbf{x}(t_{i})-e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\int_{0}^{-\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})=e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})=\mathbf{x}(t_{i})-e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\int_{0}^{-\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.11" class="ltx_p">which has distribution: <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, 
<br class="ltx_break">where <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{V}_{B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{-\mathbf{A}^{\top}\Delta t_{ij}}=e^{\mathbf{A}|\Delta t_{ij}|}\mathbf{V}_{B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}|\Delta t_{ij}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{V}_{B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{-\mathbf{A}^{\top}\Delta t_{ij}}=e^{\mathbf{A}|\Delta t_{ij}|}\mathbf{V}_{B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}|\Delta t_{ij}|}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">So, in general, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>,
where the <span id="S2.SS2.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">propagated state covariance</span> is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})=\begin{cases}\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t_{ij})&amp;\Delta t_{ij}&gt;0\quad\text{(non-causal case)}\\
\mathbf{V}_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)&amp;\Delta t_{ij}\leq 0\quad\text{(causal case)}\\
\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(non-causal case)</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(causal case)</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})=\begin{cases}\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t_{ij})&amp;\Delta t_{ij}&gt;0\quad\text{(non-causal case)}\\
\mathbf{V}_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)&amp;\Delta t_{ij}\leq 0\quad\text{(causal case)}\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.12" class="ltx_p">Recall that the measurement at time <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}(t_{j})=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{i})+\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)\right)+\mathbf{v}(t_{j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}(t_{j})=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{i})+\int_{0}^{\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)\right)+\mathbf{v}(t_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.13" class="ltx_p">The measurement process is distributed as:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{C}\mathbf{V}_{F}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{C}^{\top}+\mathbf{R}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐑</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{i}),\mathbf{C}\mathbf{V}_{F}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{C}^{\top}+\mathbf{R}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.14" class="ltx_p">Recall that our "pulled-forward" estimated measurement is defined as:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{i}(t_{j}):=\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{z}(t_{j})\quad\text{where}\quad\mathbf{M}(\Delta t):=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{-A}\Delta t}\mathbf{C}^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{i}(t_{j}):=\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{z}(t_{j})\quad\text{where}\quad\mathbf{M}(\Delta t):=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{-A}\Delta t}\mathbf{C}^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.15" class="ltx_p">In terms of the "pulled-forward" state estimate, this is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{i}(t_{j})=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{-A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})+\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{-A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{C}^{-1}\mathbf{v}(t_{j})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{i}(t_{j})=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{-A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})+\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{-A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{C}^{-1}\mathbf{v}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})+\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{v}(t_{j})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})+\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{v}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.16" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="S2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{i}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{z}^{C}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{i}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{z}^{C}(t_{i}),\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.17" class="ltx_p">where the <span id="S2.SS2.p1.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">propagated measurement covariance</span> is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{C}^{\top}+\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{R}\mathbf{M}^{\top}(\Delta t_{ij})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐑𝐌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{C}^{\top}+\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{R}\mathbf{M}^{\top}(\Delta t_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.18" class="ltx_p">We can also define a propagated state precision matrix <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}(\Delta t_{ij})=\big(\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})\big)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}(\Delta t_{ij})=\big(\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})\big)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and a propagated measurement precision matrix <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\big(\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\big)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\big(\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\big)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math> and their inverses are positive definite (PD) and symmetric for all <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>, provided that <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q},\mathbf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐑</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q},\mathbf{R}</annotation></semantics></math> are PD and symmetric.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Batch Maximum Likelihood Trajectory Estimation</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We wish to estimate the trajectory of the system from <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> measurements taken at times <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{1},...,t_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{1},...,t_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we denote <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{z}(t_{1}),...,\mathbf{z}(t_{m})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{z}(t_{1}),...,\mathbf{z}(t_{m})\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can do so by solving a separate maximum likelihood estimation (MLE) problem for each <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Let <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}=\mathbf{x}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}=\mathbf{x}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{ij}=\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{ij}=\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{i}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{ij}=\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{ij}=\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math>. The log-likelihood is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=-\frac{d_{x}m}{2}\log(2 \pi)-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\log|\det(\mathbf{V}_{ij})|-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\left(\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{ij}-\mathbf{x}_{i}\right)^{\top}\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{-1}\left(\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{ij}-\mathbf{x}_{i}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>det</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=-\frac{d_{x}m}{2}\log(2 \pi)-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\log|\det(\mathbf{V}_{ij})|-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\left(\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{ij}-\mathbf{x}_{i}\right)^{\top}\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{-1}\left(\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{ij}-\mathbf{x}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Taking the derivative with respect to <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\ell}{\partial\mathbf{x}_{i}}=\sum_{j}\left(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{\top}\left(\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{-1}+\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{-\top}\right)-2\left(\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{-1}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{ij}\right)^{\top}\right)=\mathbf{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\ell}{\partial\mathbf{x}_{i}}=\sum_{j}\left(\mathbf{x}_{i}^{\top}\left(\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{-1}+\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{-\top}\right)-2\left(\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{-1}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{ij}\right)^{\top}\right)=\mathbf{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Defining a precision matrix <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{ij}=\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{ij}=\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the MLE solution for <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is a precision-weighted estimator:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{x}}_{i}:=\left(\sum_{j}\mathbf{P}_{ij}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j}\mathbf{P}_{ij}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{ij}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{x}}_{i}:=\left(\sum_{j}\mathbf{P}_{ij}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j}\mathbf{P}_{ij}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{z}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{z}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{i}(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{i}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{C}_{ij}=\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{C}_{ij}=\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math>, and repeating the above with the PDF for <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, the MLE solution for <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{C}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{C}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}:=\left(\sum_{j}\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j}\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij},\quad\text{where}\quad\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}=\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{C-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}:=\left(\sum_{j}\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j}\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij},\quad\text{where}\quad\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}=\mathbf{V}_{ij}^{C-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">For the causal case:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}:=\left(\sum_{j\leq i}\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j\leq i}\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}:=\left(\sum_{j\leq i}\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j\leq i}\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Repeating this computation for all <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> produces an estimate of the full trajectory. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">After estimating <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can predict the next measurement <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}(t_{i+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}(t_{i+1})</annotation></semantics></math> using the system dynamics:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}(t_{i+1})=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t}\mathbf{C}^{-1}\mathbf{z}^{C}(t_{i})+\mathbf{C}\int_{0}^{\Delta t}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)+\mathbf{v}(t_{i+1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}(t_{i+1})=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t}\mathbf{C}^{-1}\mathbf{z}^{C}(t_{i})+\mathbf{C}\int_{0}^{\Delta t}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}d\mathbf{w}(\tau)+\mathbf{v}(t_{i+1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=t_{i+1}-t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=t_{i+1}-t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the noise terms are zero mean and independent, the minimum mean squared error (MMSE) prediction given <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{\mathrm{pred}}(t_{i+1}):=\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{z}(t_{i+1})\mid\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}]=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t}\mathbf{C}^{-1}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>pred</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{\mathrm{pred}}(t_{i+1}):=\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{z}(t_{i+1})\mid\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}]=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t}\mathbf{C}^{-1}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">which matches the standard approach in Kalman Filtering of propagating the current estimate forward through the deterministic part of the dynamics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.4 </span>Recursive (Kalman Filter) Formulation</h3>

<div id="S2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We can express the batch MLE for a trajectory in a recursive (information-form) manner, while accounting for the dynamics of the system. Consider estimating the state <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{C}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{C}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> given all measurements <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{z}(t_{j})\}_{j\leq i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{z}(t_{j})\}_{j\leq i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prediction (Propagate Prior Through Dynamics).</h5>

<div id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose we have already incorporated measurements up to time <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the posterior at <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i-1}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i-1}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with covariance <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and precision <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i-1}^{+}=(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i-1}^{+}=(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Propagating through the linear dynamics:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{z}_{i-1}+\mathbf{q}_{i-1},\quad\mathbf{q}_{i-1}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{Q})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{z}_{i-1}+\mathbf{q}_{i-1},\quad\mathbf{q}_{i-1}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{Q}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">the prior for time <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i-1}^{+},\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-}=\mathbf{A}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+}\mathbf{A}^{\top}+\mathbf{Q},\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}=(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-})^{-1},\quad\bm{\eta}_{i}^{-}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}\,\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐐</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜼</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i-1}^{+},\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-}=\mathbf{A}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+}\mathbf{A}^{\top}+\mathbf{Q},\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}=(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-})^{-1},\quad\bm{\eta}_{i}^{-}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}\,\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Update (Incorporate Measurement).</h5>

<div id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now include the measurement at <math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with measurement model:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{z}^{-}_{i}+\mathbf{r}_{i},\quad\mathbf{r}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{R})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐂𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{z}^{-}_{i}+\mathbf{r}_{i},\quad\mathbf{r}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{R}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and define the information-form measurement contribution:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ii}=\mathbf{C}^{\top}\mathbf{R}^{-1}\mathbf{C},\qquad\mathbf{b}_{i}=\mathbf{C}^{\top}\mathbf{R}^{-1}\mathbf{z}_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ii}=\mathbf{C}^{\top}\mathbf{R}^{-1}\mathbf{C},\qquad\mathbf{b}_{i}=\mathbf{C}^{\top}\mathbf{R}^{-1}\mathbf{z}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The posterior precision and information vector are then:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}+\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ii},\qquad\bm{\eta}_{i}^{+}=\bm{\eta}_{i}^{-}+\mathbf{b}_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜼</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜼</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}+\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ii},\qquad\bm{\eta}_{i}^{+}=\bm{\eta}_{i}^{-}+\mathbf{b}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and the posterior mean (MAP estimate) is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{+}=(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+})^{-1}\bm{\eta}_{i}^{+}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜼</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{+}=(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+})^{-1}\bm{\eta}_{i}^{+}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, in the standard Kalman Filter (covariance) form:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}_{i}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-}\mathbf{C}^{\top}(\mathbf{C}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-}\mathbf{C}^{\top}+\mathbf{R})^{-1},\quad\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{+}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}+\mathbf{K}_{i}(\mathbf{z}_{i}-\mathbf{C}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}),\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{+}=(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{K}_{i}\mathbf{C})\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐑</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}_{i}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-}\mathbf{C}^{\top}(\mathbf{C}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-}\mathbf{C}^{\top}+\mathbf{R})^{-1},\quad\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{+}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}+\mathbf{K}_{i}(\mathbf{z}_{i}-\mathbf{C}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}),\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{+}=(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{K}_{i}\mathbf{C})\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.5 </span>Closed-form Precision Matrix Calculation for Diagonalizable Matrices</h3>

<div id="S2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The estimation procedure above requires computing <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is generally expensive, as it involves integration and matrix inversion. However, if we assume that <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonalizable, that is we can write it in the form <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{S}^{-1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{S}^{-1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagonal matrix and <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> an invertible matrix, the backward-propagated covariance becomes:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t)=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t|}e^{\mathbf{-A}\tau}\mathbf{Q}e^{\mathbf{-A}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{B}(\Delta t)=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t|}e^{\mathbf{-A}\tau}\mathbf{Q}e^{\mathbf{-A}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\mathbf{S}\left(\int_{0}^{|\Delta t|}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}(\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau\right)\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐐𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>†</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\mathbf{S}\left(\int_{0}^{|\Delta t|}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}(\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau\right)\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}:=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐐𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>†</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}:=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(\Delta t):=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t|}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}(\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐐𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>†</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(\Delta t):=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t|}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}(\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Note that <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(e^{-\bm{\Lambda}t}\mathbf{G}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}t})_{kl}=\mathbf{G}_{kl}e^{-\lambda_{k}t}e^{-\bar{\lambda}_{l}t}=\mathbf{G}_{kl}e^{-(\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l})t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐆</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(e^{-\bm{\Lambda}t}\mathbf{G}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}t})_{kl}=\mathbf{G}_{kl}e^{-\lambda_{k}t}e^{-\bar{\lambda}_{l}t}=\mathbf{G}_{kl}e^{-(\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l})t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="kl" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">kl</annotation></semantics></math>th component of <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(\Delta t)_{kl}=\mathbf{G}_{kl}\int_{0}^{|\Delta t|}e^{-(\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l})\tau}d\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(\Delta t)_{kl}=\mathbf{G}_{kl}\int_{0}^{|\Delta t|}e^{-(\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l})\tau}d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\begin{cases}\mathbf{G}_{kl}\,\dfrac{1-e^{-(\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l})|\Delta t|}}{\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l}},&amp;\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l}\neq 0\\[5.69054pt]
\mathbf{G}_{kl}\,|\Delta t|,&amp;\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l}=0\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐆</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\begin{cases}\mathbf{G}_{kl}\,\dfrac{1-e^{-(\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l})|\Delta t|}}{\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l}},&amp;\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l}\neq 0\\[5.69054pt]
\mathbf{G}_{kl}\,|\Delta t|,&amp;\lambda_{k}+\bar{\lambda}_{l}=0\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">If we assume that <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. that the process noise acts independently along the decoupled modes of the system, then <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}=\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}=\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes diagonal:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}-\mathbf{I}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}-\mathbf{I}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where division is taken element-wise (ignoring, for now, the case <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{k})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{k})=0</annotation></semantics></math>). 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">For the causal case, the forward-propagated covariance is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=e^{\mathbf{A}|\Delta t_{ij}|}\mathbf{V}_{B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}|\Delta t_{ij}|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=e^{\mathbf{A}|\Delta t_{ij}|}\mathbf{V}_{B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}|\Delta t_{ij}|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\mathbf{S}e^{\bm{\Lambda}|\Delta t_{ij}|}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}|\Delta t_{ij}|}\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\mathbf{S}e^{\bm{\Lambda}|\Delta t_{ij}|}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}|\Delta t_{ij}|}\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\mathbf{S}e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}\left(\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}-\mathbf{I}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}\right)\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\mathbf{S}e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}\left(\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}-\mathbf{I}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}\right)\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="S2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{\mathbf{I}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{\mathbf{I}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.SS5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semi-definite provided <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\geq\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\geq\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (which is true by definition). (Here, the inequalities are applied element-wise.) 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The propagated precision matrix <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> can be easily obtained by inverting <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math> element-wise: <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}(\Delta t)=\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}(\Delta t)\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>†</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}(\Delta t)=\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}(\Delta t)\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}(\Delta t)=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}(\Delta t)=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">To include the measurement model, recall that the propagated measurement covariance is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{C}^{\dagger}+\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{R}\mathbf{M}^{\dagger}(\Delta t_{ij}),\quad\text{where}\quad\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{-A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{C}^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐑𝐌</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{V}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{C}^{\dagger}+\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{R}\mathbf{M}^{\dagger}(\Delta t_{ij}),\quad\text{where}\quad\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{C}e^{\mathbf{-A}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{C}^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.7" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{C}\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{C}\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, this becomes: <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{C}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{-1}\mathbf{S}=\mathbf{S}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{C}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{-1}\mathbf{S}=\mathbf{S}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. If, in addition, <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐑</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>, then:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{C}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t_{ij})\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{\dagger}\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}+\mathbf{S}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{C}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t_{ij})\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{\dagger}\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}+\mathbf{S}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.8" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t_{ij})+e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t_{ij})+e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{\mathbf{I}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}+e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{\mathbf{I}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}+e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})|\Delta t_{ij}|}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.9" class="ltx_p">(Stable dynamics attenuate the effect of measurement noise.) 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Finally, <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>†</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Letting <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}_{i}}=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}_{i}}=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}:=e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}:=e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}j}</annotation></semantics></math>, the MLE is now tractable:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}=\mathbf{S}\left[\left(\sum_{j\leq i}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\right)^{-1}\sum_{j\leq i}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}\right]\mathbf{S}^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}=\mathbf{S}\left[\left(\sum_{j\leq i}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\right)^{-1}\sum_{j\leq i}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}\right]\mathbf{S}^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.10" class="ltx_p">For the non-causal case,</p>
<table id="S2.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t)=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(\Delta t)=\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t}-\mathbf{I}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t)=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(\Delta t)=\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t}-\mathbf{I}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.11" class="ltx_p">So,</p>
<table id="S2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t_{ij})+e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}(\Delta t_{ij})+e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t_{ij}}-\mathbf{I}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}+e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\frac{e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t_{ij}}-\mathbf{I}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})}+e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.12" class="ltx_p">In summary, the general expression for the propagated measurement covariance, including both the causal and non-causal cases, and all values of <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\text{sign}(\Delta t_{ij})\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\mathcal{K}(\bm{\Lambda},\Delta t_{ij})+e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>sign</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\text{sign}(\Delta t_{ij})\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}\mathcal{K}(\bm{\Lambda},\Delta t_{ij})+e^{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{K}(\bm{\Lambda},\Delta t):=\operatorname{diag}\!\big(\varphi(\lambda_{k},\Delta t)\big)_{k=1}^{d},\qquad\varphi(\lambda,\Delta t):=\begin{cases}\dfrac{e^{-2\operatorname{Re}(\lambda)\,\Delta t}-1}{-2\operatorname{Re}(\lambda)},&amp;\operatorname{Re}(\lambda)\neq 0,\\[6.0pt]
\Delta t,&amp;\operatorname{Re}(\lambda)=0,\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.736em;" width="1.736em"><mi>diag</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{K}(\bm{\Lambda},\Delta t):=\operatorname{diag}\!\big(\varphi(\lambda_{k},\Delta t)\big)_{k=1}^{d},\qquad\varphi(\lambda,\Delta t):=\begin{cases}\dfrac{e^{-2\operatorname{Re}(\lambda)\,\Delta t}-1}{-2\operatorname{Re}(\lambda)},&amp;\operatorname{Re}(\lambda)\neq 0,\\[6.0pt]
\Delta t,&amp;\operatorname{Re}(\lambda)=0,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<br class="ltx_break">
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.13" class="ltx_p">This is bounded for all <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> in the causal case if and only if every component of <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\Lambda})</annotation></semantics></math> is negative. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">In particular, consider <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Omega}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Omega}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonalizable over <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, and has strictly imaginary eigenvalues, i.e. <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}=\text{diag}(\lambda_{\Omega,1},\dots\lambda_{\Omega,d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}=\text{diag}(\lambda_{\Omega,1},\dots\lambda_{\Omega,d})</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\Omega,k}\in i\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\Omega,k}\in i\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. If we also assume that the process and measurement noise are isotropic <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}=\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}=\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{R}=\eta^{2}\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{R}=\eta^{2}\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{C}=\lambda_{C}\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{C}=\lambda_{C}\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\sigma_{V}^{2}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{I},\quad\text{where}\quad\sigma_{V}^{2}(\Delta t_{ij}):=\text{sign}(\Delta t_{ij})\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\frac{e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}-1}{-2\alpha}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\eta^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>sign</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\sigma_{V}^{2}(\Delta t_{ij})\mathbf{I},\quad\text{where}\quad\sigma_{V}^{2}(\Delta t_{ij}):=\text{sign}(\Delta t_{ij})\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\frac{e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}-1}{-2\alpha}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.14" class="ltx_p">We can also generalize the above to the case where continuous-time measurements are incorporated. In this case, the covariance evolution is governed by the differential Riccati equation, which modifies the differential Lyapunov equation to include the measurement update:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\dot{V}}_{F}(t)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}_{F}(t)+\mathbf{V}_{F}(t)\mathbf{A}^{\top}+\mathbf{Q}-\mathbf{V}_{F}(t)\mathbf{C}^{\top}\mathbf{R}^{-1}\mathbf{C}\mathbf{V}_{F}(t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐐</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐂𝐕</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\dot{V}}_{F}(t)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}_{F}(t)+\mathbf{V}_{F}(t)\mathbf{A}^{\top}+\mathbf{Q}-\mathbf{V}_{F}(t)\mathbf{C}^{\top}\mathbf{R}^{-1}\mathbf{C}\mathbf{V}_{F}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.15" class="ltx_p">Again assuming simultaneously diagonalizble <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A},\mathbf{C},\mathbf{Q},\mathbf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐑</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A},\mathbf{C},\mathbf{Q},\mathbf{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the matrix equations decouple into separate scalar Riccati differential equations for each diagonal element, with <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>th diagonal term given by:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\lambda}_{vk}(t)=2\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{i})\lambda_{vk}(t)+\lambda_{\Omega k}-\frac{\lambda_{Ck}^{2}}{\lambda_{\Gamma k}}\lambda_{vk}(t)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\lambda}_{vk}(t)=2\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{i})\lambda_{vk}(t)+\lambda_{\Omega k}-\frac{\lambda_{Ck}^{2}}{\lambda_{\Gamma k}}\lambda_{vk}(t)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.16" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}=\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}=\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}=\sqrt{\alpha_{k}^{2}+\frac{\lambda_{Qk}}{\lambda_{Rk}}\lambda_{Ck}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}=\sqrt{\alpha_{k}^{2}+\frac{\lambda_{Qk}}{\lambda_{Rk}}\lambda_{Ck}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}=\frac{1}{\beta_{k}}\log\left(\frac{\beta_{k}-\alpha_{k}}{\beta_{k}+\alpha_{k}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}=\frac{1}{\beta_{k}}\log\left(\frac{\beta_{k}-\alpha_{k}}{\beta_{k}+\alpha_{k}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>th element of <math id="S2.SS5.p1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{vk}(\Delta t_{ij})=\frac{\lambda_{Rk}}{\lambda_{Ck}^{2}}\left(\beta_{k}\tanh\left(\frac{\beta_{k}}{2}\left(\Delta t_{ij}-\gamma_{k}\right)\right)+\alpha_{k}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{vk}(\Delta t_{ij})=\frac{\lambda_{Rk}}{\lambda_{Ck}^{2}}\left(\beta_{k}\tanh\left(\frac{\beta_{k}}{2}\left(\Delta t_{ij}-\gamma_{k}\right)\right)+\alpha_{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.6 </span>Robust Maximum Likelihood Trajectory Estimation</h3>

<div id="S2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Maximum Likelihood Estimation (MLE) of a system’s trajectory relies on accurate precision matrices, which represent the uncertainty of our estimates. If our dynamic model, defined by <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{S},\mathbf{S}^{-1},\bm{\Lambda},\bm{\Lambda}_{C},\bm{\Lambda}_{Q},\bm{\Lambda}_{R}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{S},\mathbf{S}^{-1},\bm{\Lambda},\bm{\Lambda}_{C},\bm{\Lambda}_{Q},\bm{\Lambda}_{R}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, does not perfectly match reality, these theoretical precision matrices may misrepresent the true uncertainty, leading to suboptimal state estimates. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">One approach to mitigate model mis-specification is to adaptively adjust the precision matrix <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> using observed residuals. Since <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{z}^{C}_{i},\mathbf{V}^{C}_{ij}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{z}^{C}_{i},\mathbf{V}^{C}_{ij}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that the pair-wise <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">residual</span> <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{ij}:=\mathbf{z}_{i}^{C}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}\big(0,\mathbf{V}^{C}_{ij}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{ij}:=\mathbf{z}_{i}^{C}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}\big(0,\mathbf{V}^{C}_{ij}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>. We generally can’t observe <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, but we can also define a <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">measurement residual</span>, <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r_{z}}_{ij}:=\mathbf{z}_{i}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}\big(0,\mathbf{V}^{C}_{ij}+\mathbf{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐑</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r_{z}}_{ij}:=\mathbf{z}_{i}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}\big(0,\mathbf{V}^{C}_{ij}+\mathbf{R})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that these pair-wise residuals are distinct from the total <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">innovation</span> <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{ij}:=\mathbf{z}_{i}^{C}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{ij}:=\mathbf{z}_{i}^{C}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\!\left(\mathbf{y}_{i}\right)=\left(\sum_{j}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\right)^{-1}\preceq\big(\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\big)^{-1},\,\forall j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.622em;" width="1.622em"><mi>Cov</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪯</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\!\left(\mathbf{y}_{i}\right)=\left(\sum_{j}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\right)^{-1}\preceq\big(\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\big)^{-1},\,\forall j</annotation></semantics></math>, the combined estimator’s innovation covariance is no larger than the residual covariance of any single predictor.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">2.6.1 </span>Variational Formulation of Robust Estimation</h4>

<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose we have vector-valued measurements:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}\big(\bm{\mu}_{i},\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}\big(\bm{\mu}_{i},\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the output of the true latent state at time <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> (which we distinguish from <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{C}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{C}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which denotes the output <span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">under the latent state generated by our LTI model</span>), and <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is the unknown measurement covariance. Our objective is to maximize the marginal log-likelihood:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i})\;=\;\log\int p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\,p(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\,d\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>∫</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i})\;=\;\log\int p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\,p(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\,d\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">i.e. a Gaussian scale mixture. Introducing a variational distribution <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> over the unknown covariance and applying Jensen’s inequality yields the Evidence Lower Bound (ELBO):</p>
<table id="S2.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i})\geq\mathcal{L}(q,\bm{\mu}_{i}):=\mathbb{E}_{q(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})}\big[\log p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\big]-\mathrm{KL}\big(q(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\,\|\,p(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i})\geq\mathcal{L}(q,\bm{\mu}_{i}):=\mathbb{E}_{q(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})}\big[\log p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\big]-\mathrm{KL}\big(q(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\,\|\,p(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Assuming <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonal, the expected log-likelihood term becomes:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q}\big[\log p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\big]=-\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{q}[\log\det\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}]-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i})^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{q}[\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}^{-1}](\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i})+\text{const}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>det</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mtext>const</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q}\big[\log p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\big]=-\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{q}[\log\det\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}]-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i})^{\top}\mathbb{E}_{q}[\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}^{-1}](\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i})+\text{const}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Define the expected precision:
<math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{ij}:=\mathbb{E}_{q}\big[\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}^{-1}\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{ij}:=\mathbb{E}_{q}\big[\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}^{-1}\big].</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Then, the expected log-likelihood is proportional to a weighted quadratic form:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q}\big[\log p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\big]\;\propto\;-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i})^{\top}\mathbf{W}_{ij}(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∝</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q}\big[\log p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij})\big]\;\propto\;-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i})^{\top}\mathbf{W}_{ij}(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">We model the unknown measurement precision as a scaled version of the dynamics-based precision:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}^{-1}=\tau_{ij}\,\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}^{-1}=\tau_{ij}\,\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is the precision predicted by the LTI model and <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ij}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ij}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a latent scalar that modulates the overall confidence in this observation. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Conditional on <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Gaussian likelihood for the measurement <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\tau_{ij})=\mathcal{N}\big(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},(\tau_{ij}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij})^{-1}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\tau_{ij})=\mathcal{N}\big(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},(\tau_{ij}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij})^{-1}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">The optimal variational distribution over <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is proportional to the prior times the likelihood:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}(\tau_{ij})\propto p(\tau_{ij})\,p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\tau_{ij})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}(\tau_{ij})\propto p(\tau_{ij})\,p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i},\tau_{ij}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.9" class="ltx_p">To enable Bayesian inference, we place a conjugate prior on <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using a Gamma prior:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{ij}\sim\mathrm{Gamma}(\alpha,\beta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Gamma</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{ij}\sim\mathrm{Gamma}(\alpha,\beta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Since the prior is Gamma and the likelihood is Gaussian with a precision multiplier, the posterior is again a Gamma distribution:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}(\tau_{ij})=\mathrm{Gamma}\!\Big(\alpha+\frac{d}{2},\;\beta+\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\mathbf{r}_{ij}\Big),\quad\mathbf{r}_{ij}:=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:3.429em;" width="3.429em"><mi>Gamma</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}(\tau_{ij})=\mathrm{Gamma}\!\Big(\alpha+\frac{d}{2},\;\beta+\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\mathbf{r}_{ij}\Big),\quad\mathbf{r}_{ij}:=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.11" class="ltx_p">The expected precision under the posterior is:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{ij}:=\mathbb{E}_{q^{*}}[\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}^{-1}]=\mathbb{E}_{q^{*}}[\tau_{ij}]\,\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}=w_{ij}\,\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{ij}:=\mathbb{E}_{q^{*}}[\mathbf{\Sigma}_{ij}^{-1}]=\mathbb{E}_{q^{*}}[\tau_{ij}]\,\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}=w_{ij}\,\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.12" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}=\frac{\alpha+d/2}{\beta+\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\mathbf{r}_{ij}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}=\frac{\alpha+d/2}{\beta+\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\mathbf{r}_{ij}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.13" class="ltx_p">The corresponding (marginal) likelihood <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}\mid\bm{\mu}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is a Student’s <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is equivalent to an M-estimator with loss</p>
<table id="S2.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\mathbf{r}_{ij})\;=\;\Big(\alpha+\tfrac{d}{2}\Big)\,\log\!\Big(\beta+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}_{ij}\,\mathbf{r}_{ij}\Big),\qquad\mathbf{r}_{ij}:=\bm{\mu}_{i}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\mathbf{r}_{ij})\;=\;\Big(\alpha+\tfrac{d}{2}\Big)\,\log\!\Big(\beta+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}_{ij}\,\mathbf{r}_{ij}\Big),\qquad\mathbf{r}_{ij}:=\bm{\mu}_{i}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.14" class="ltx_p">Dividing numerator and denominator by <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and setting the numerator to <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> (since it is canceled by the normalization), there is only one independent constant, <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=2\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=2\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, which controls the residual scaling:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}=\frac{1}{1+\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\mathbf{r}_{ij}/\nu}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}=\frac{1}{1+\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\mathbf{r}_{ij}/\nu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.15" class="ltx_p">The term <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}^{\top}\mathbf{V}^{-1}\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}^{\top}\mathbf{V}^{-1}\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is known as the Mahalanobis distance, which quantifies the difference between a vector <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and a distribution with covariance <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> encodes the directional confidence from the LTI model, while <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> adaptively rescales the precision based on the observed residual <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, down-weighting measurements with larger than expected deviations. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The metric <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/(1+\mathbf{r}^{\top}\mathbf{P}\mathbf{r}/\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏𝐫</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/(1+\mathbf{r}^{\top}\mathbf{P}\mathbf{r}/\nu)</annotation></semantics></math> behaves similarly to the unnormalized softmax: if one residual is much smaller than the others, it dominates, while if all residuals are similar and not too large, the output approximates a uniform weighting. The key difference arises when all residuals are small relative to <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>: unlike softmax, which picks a dominant term whenever relative differences are large, this similarity score reflects uncertainty and maintains a roughly uniform attention distribution. In this sense, <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a kind of noise floor. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Using the fact that <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1 + x)\approx x\quad\text{for }x\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1 + x)\approx x\quad\text{for }x\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can expand the rational form of <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}=\frac{1}{1+\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\mathbf{r}_{ij}/\nu}\approx\exp(- \mathbf{r}_{ij}^\top\mathbf{P}^C_{ij} \mathbf{r}_{ij} / \nu)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝐫</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝐏</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐫</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}=\frac{1}{1+\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}^{C}_{ij}\mathbf{r}_{ij}/\nu}\approx\exp(- \mathbf{r}_{ij}^\top\mathbf{P}^C_{ij} \mathbf{r}_{ij} / \nu).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.16" class="ltx_p">which results in a more aggressive down-weighting of large residuals (and <math id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> becomes a temperature parameter).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">2.6.2 </span>Iteratively-Reweighted Least Squares</h4>

<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As we noted above, we cannot observe the true latent state <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, so we cannot compute the residual <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{ij}:=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{ij}:=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\bm{\mu}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, we can use our current best estimate of <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we denote <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ii}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ii}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a corresponding residual: <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{r}}_{ij}:=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ii}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐫</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{r}}_{ij}:=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ii}</annotation></semantics></math>. This leads naturally to an iteratively-reweighted least squares (IRLS)-style update for the latent state (at iteration <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="S2.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k+1)}_{ii}=\Big(\sum_{j}w_{ij}^{(k)}\mathbf{P}^{C(k)}_{ij}\Big)^{-1}\sum_{j}w_{ij}^{(k)}\mathbf{P}^{C(k)}_{ij}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}^{(k)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k+1)}_{ii}=\Big(\sum_{j}w_{ij}^{(k)}\mathbf{P}^{C(k)}_{ij}\Big)^{-1}\sum_{j}w_{ij}^{(k)}\mathbf{P}^{C(k)}_{ij}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}^{(k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Recall that (by construction) <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C(k)}=\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger}\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>†</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C(k)}=\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger}\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}:=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}:=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}=e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}=e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define a corresponding residual <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r_{zs}}_{ij}:=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r_{zs}}_{ij}:=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be the diagonal of <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have an iterative update rule for the state estimate in the eigenbasis:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ii}^{(k+1)}=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{\text{MLE}(k)},\quad\text{where}\quad\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{\text{MLE}(k)}=\left(\sum_{j}w_{ij}^{(k)}\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}\right)^{-1}\odot\sum_{j}w_{ij}^{(k)}\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}\odot\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>MLE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>MLE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">⊙</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ii}^{(k+1)}=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{\text{MLE}(k)},\quad\text{where}\quad\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{\text{MLE}(k)}=\left(\sum_{j}w_{ij}^{(k)}\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}\right)^{-1}\odot\sum_{j}w_{ij}^{(k)}\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}\odot\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ij}^{(k)}=\frac{1}{1+(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C})^{\top}\|\mathbf{r}^{(k)}_{\mathbf{s}ij}\|^{2}/\nu},\quad\text{where}\quad\mathbf{r}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}:=\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k)}_{\mathbf{s}ii}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k)}_{\mathbf{s}ij}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ij}^{(k)}=\frac{1}{1+(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C})^{\top}\|\mathbf{r}^{(k)}_{\mathbf{s}ij}\|^{2}/\nu},\quad\text{where}\quad\mathbf{r}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}:=\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k)}_{\mathbf{s}ii}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k)}_{\mathbf{s}ij}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and initial condition <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ii}^{(1)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ii}^{(1)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}</annotation></semantics></math>. (Alternatively, if we only have a single iteration, we can replace <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}+\bm{\lambda}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{P}ij}^{C}+\bm{\lambda}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (the covariance of <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}</annotation></semantics></math>).) To stabilize the iteration, we can instead use an affine combination of the current and previous estimate:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k+1)}_{\mathbf{s}ii}=(1-\delta)\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ii}^{(k)}+\delta\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{\text{MLE}(k)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>MLE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k+1)}_{\mathbf{s}ii}=(1-\delta)\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ii}^{(k)}+\delta\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{\text{MLE}(k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">This IRLS iteration, with precision matrices derived from an LTI model, performs a batched maximum likelihood update of latent states using pairwise uncertainty propagation. We will refer to it as Kalman-IRLS, as it is closely related to adaptive Kalman Filtering, although unlike the latter, it does not rely on recursive updates. It can be implemented with a multi-layer neural network with learnable parameters <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S},\bm{\Lambda},\bm{\Lambda}_{Q},\bm{\Lambda}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S},\bm{\Lambda},\bm{\Lambda}_{Q},\bm{\Lambda}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> shared across layers. If <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k)}_{ii}\rightarrow\mathbf{z}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k)}_{ii}\rightarrow\mathbf{z}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> in expectation with increasing <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we can take <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}}\approx\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k)}_{\mathbf{s}ii}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}}\approx\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{(k)}_{\mathbf{s}ii}</annotation></semantics></math> at the last layer, and then predict the measurement at the next time step in the eigenbasis using the (diagonalized) matrix exponential:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{\text{pred}}_{\mathbf{s}i}=\bm{\Lambda}_{C}e^{\bm{\Lambda}(t_{i+1}-t_{i})}\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{-1}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}=e^{\bm{\Lambda}(t_{i+1}-t_{i})}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{\text{pred}}_{\mathbf{s}i}=\bm{\Lambda}_{C}e^{\bm{\Lambda}(t_{i+1}-t_{i})}\bm{\Lambda}_{C}^{-1}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}=e^{\bm{\Lambda}(t_{i+1}-t_{i})}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Finally, we compute the output prediction: <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}^{\text{pred}}_{i}=\mathbf{S}\mathbf{z}^{\text{pred}}_{\mathbf{s}i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐒𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}^{\text{pred}}_{i}=\mathbf{S}\mathbf{z}^{\text{pred}}_{\mathbf{s}i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which we then compare to the actual measurement at the next time step <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can then define a loss, e.g. <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\sum_{i}\|\mathbf{z}^{\text{pred}}_{i}-\mathbf{z}_{i+1}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\sum_{i}\|\mathbf{z}^{\text{pred}}_{i}-\mathbf{z}_{i+1}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and train our model parameters <math id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S},\bm{\Lambda},\bm{\Lambda}_{Q},\bm{\Lambda}_{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S},\bm{\Lambda},\bm{\Lambda}_{Q},\bm{\Lambda}_{R}</annotation></semantics></math> using backpropagation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS6.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">2.6.3 </span>Iteratively-Reweighted Kalman Filter (IRKF)</h4>

<div id="S2.SS6.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now describe a way to incorporate state-dependent weighting from the full batch MLE while retaining the recursive structure of the Kalman Filter. The key idea is to use the <em id="S2.SS6.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">innovation residual</em> at each step to reweight the update, and iterate within each time step to approximate the effect of all pairwise comparisons. This iteration again takes place in the eigenbasis.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prediction Step (Include Process Noise).</h5>

<div id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At time <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose we have the posterior from the previous time step <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s},i-1}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s},i-1}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with covariance <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and precision <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i-1}^{+}=(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i-1}^{+}=(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Propagating through the linear dynamics with process noise <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, the prior for the current time step becomes:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-}=\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s},i-1}^{+},\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-}=\bm{\Lambda}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+}\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}+\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}=\|\bm{\Lambda}\|^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+}+\bm{\Lambda}_{Q},\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}=(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-})^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-}=\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s},i-1}^{+},\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-}=\bm{\Lambda}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+}\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}+\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}=\|\bm{\Lambda}\|^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i-1}^{+}+\bm{\Lambda}_{Q},\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}=(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V},i}^{-})^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The propagated precision for a single time step is constant: <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}:=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(\Delta t_{i,i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}:=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(\Delta t_{i,i-1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Weighted Update (Measurement + IRKF Iteration).</h5>

<div id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within each iteration <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, compute the innovation:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Define the nominal posterior precision from the measurement model:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and compute a residual-based robust weight:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}^{(k)}=\frac{1}{1+(\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}/\nu}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}^{(k)}=\frac{1}{1+(\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}/\nu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The weighted posterior precision is then:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Notice that the posterior information vector can be written as:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tilde{\eta}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+}=\bm{\eta}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tilde{\eta}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+}=\bm{\eta}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{-}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">So the total posterior mean in the eigenbasis becomes:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+(k)}=(\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)})^{-1}\bm{\tilde{\eta}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+(k)}=(\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)})^{-1}\bm{\tilde{\eta}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=(\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)})^{-1}\Big[\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=(\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)})^{-1}\Big[\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S2.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=(\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)})^{-1}\Big[\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big]=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+w_{i}^{(k)}(\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)})^{-1}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=(\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)})^{-1}\Big[\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+w_{i}^{(k)}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big]=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+w_{i}^{(k)}(\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)})^{-1}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">(the robust weight only scales the measurement contribution, not the prior). 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Alternatively, we can use a damped update:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+(k)}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+\delta\,w_{i}^{(k)}(\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)})^{-1}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+(k)}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k)}+\delta\,w_{i}^{(k)}(\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+(k)})^{-1}\,\bm{\Lambda}^{C}_{\mathbf{P}}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.8" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Set the prior for the next inner iteration as:
<math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k+1)}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-(k+1)}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Iterate until convergence to produce the final posterior <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tilde{\Lambda}}_{\mathbf{P},i}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> for the current time step. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">While the batch MLE uses the global information provided by pair-wise residuals, the innovation-based weight <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in the recursive update depends only on the current residual <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}=\mathbf{z}_{i}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}=\mathbf{z}_{i}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, when the dynamics are slow (small eigenvalues), <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently small, and the residuals are not too large, <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> effectively encodes past measurements. In this case, with enough inner iterations, IRKF should approximate the batch IRLS solution, while retaining the recursive structure of the Kalman Filter. The number of pair-wise comparisons for a sequence of length <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is then reduced from <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(Km)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(Km)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS6.SSS3.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\ll m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\ll m</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of inner iterations.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Adaptive Filter Attention</h2>

<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Generalizing the Adaptive Filter to a Tensor Form of Attention</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now generalize the batch MLE form of the above adaptive filter using learned, complex-valued query, key, value, and output matrices: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{q}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times d_{e}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{q}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times d_{e}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{k}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times d_{e}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{k}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times d_{e}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{v}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{v}\times d_{e}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{v}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{v}\times d_{e}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{p}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{e}\times d_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{p}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{e}\times d_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> is the input embedding dimension <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the query/key embedding dimension, and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is the value embedding dimension. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">In this formulation, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{q}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> replace <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{p}}</annotation></semantics></math> replaces <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{q}}=\mathbf{W_{k}}=\mathbf{W_{v}}=\mathbf{W_{p}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{q}}=\mathbf{W_{k}}=\mathbf{W_{v}}=\mathbf{W_{p}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the attention layer corresponds to an adaptive MLE. By allowing these parameter matrices to vary freely, the network can learn approximate inverses as needed, enabling attention to implement an MLE while retaining the flexibility to represent richer transformations. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We can define separate key/query and value dynamics parameters: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{qk}},\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{qk}},\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{qk}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{qk}},\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{qk}},\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{qk}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{v}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{v}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If we set <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{k}=d_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{k}=d_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we can use a shared set of parameters for the key and value dynamics: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda},\bm{\lambda}_{Q},\bm{\lambda}_{R},\bm{\lambda}_{C}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda},\bm{\lambda}_{Q},\bm{\lambda}_{R},\bm{\lambda}_{C}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that we can absorb <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}_{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}_{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, but we keep it here for clarity. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The inputs to the network are: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\quad\mathbf{Z}=\left[\mathbf{z}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{z}_{m}\right]\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{e}\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\quad\mathbf{Z}=\left[\mathbf{z}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{z}_{m}\right]\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{e}\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We compute the following: 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Query, key, and value matrices:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z_{q}}=\mathbf{W_{q}}\mathbf{Z}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times m},\quad\mathbf{Z_{k}}=\mathbf{W_{k}}\mathbf{Z}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times m},\quad\mathbf{Z_{v}}=\mathbf{W_{v}}\mathbf{Z}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{v}\times m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐙</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z_{q}}=\mathbf{W_{q}}\mathbf{Z}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times m},\quad\mathbf{Z_{k}}=\mathbf{W_{k}}\mathbf{Z}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times m},\quad\mathbf{Z_{v}}=\mathbf{W_{v}}\mathbf{Z}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{v}\times m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Exponential tensors: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times m\times m},\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{v}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{v}\times m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times m\times m},\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{v}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{v}\times m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]=e^{\lambda_{\mathbf{qk}k}(t_{i}-t_{j})},\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]=e^{\lambda_{\mathbf{v}k}(t_{i}-t_{j})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]=e^{\lambda_{\mathbf{qk}k}(t_{i}-t_{j})},\quad\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]=e^{\lambda_{\mathbf{v}k}(t_{i}-t_{j})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">"Pulled-forward" estimates: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times m\times m},\quad\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{v}\times m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times m\times m},\quad\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{v}\times m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]=\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathbf{Z_{k}}[k,j],\quad\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]=\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathbf{Z_{v}}[k,j]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]=\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathbf{Z_{k}}[k,j],\quad\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]=\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathbf{Z_{v}}[k,j],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The residuals: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{k}\times m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]=\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i]-\hat{\mathcal{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]=\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i]-\hat{\mathcal{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">The norms of the residuals:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\|^{2}=\mathrm{Re}^{2}\left(\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\right)+\mathrm{Im}^{2}\left(\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Re</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Im</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\|^{2}=\mathrm{Re}^{2}\left(\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\right)+\mathrm{Im}^{2}\left(\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">The key and value precision tensors: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{k}\times m\times m},\quad\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}\times m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{k}\times m\times m},\quad\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}\times m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[:,i,j]=\left(\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{qk}}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{qk}}\odot\frac{\mathbf{1}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})|t_{j}-t_{i}|}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})}+\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{qk}}\odot e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})|t_{j}-t_{i}|}\right)^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[:,i,j]=\left(\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{qk}}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{qk}}\odot\frac{\mathbf{1}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})|t_{j}-t_{i}|}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})}+\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{qk}}\odot e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})|t_{j}-t_{i}|}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i,j]=\left(\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{v}}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{v}}\odot\frac{\mathbf{1}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}})|t_{j}-t_{i}|}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}})}+\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{v}}\odot e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}})|t_{j}-t_{i}|}\right)^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i,j]=\left(\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{v}}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{v}}\odot\frac{\mathbf{1}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}})|t_{j}-t_{i}|}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}})}+\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{v}}\odot e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}})|t_{j}-t_{i}|}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">We apply a causal attention mask to <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}},\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}},\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>, masking out all <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;i</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Compute the weights: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}[i,j]=\left(1+\sum_{k}\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\|\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\|^{2}/\nu\right)^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}[i,j]=\left(1+\sum_{k}\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\|\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\|^{2}/\nu\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is a learnable scalar. The value parameters <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> are responsible for the prior, while the query and key parameters <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W_{q}},\mathbf{W_{k}},\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{qk}},\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{qk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W_{q}},\mathbf{W_{k}},\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{qk}},\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{qk}}</annotation></semantics></math> are responsible for the adaptive reweighting. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Compute the unnormalized attention scores: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{A}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}\times m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{A}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}\times m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{A}}[k,i,j]=\mathbf{W}[i,j]\cdot\mathcal{P}_{\mathbf{v}}^{C}[k,i,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{A}}[k,i,j]=\mathbf{W}[i,j]\cdot\mathcal{P}_{\mathbf{v}}^{C}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.9" class="ltx_p">Normalize to obtain the attention tensor: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}\times m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}\times m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}[k,i,j]=\tilde{\mathcal{A}}[k,i,j]\big/\sum_{j^{\prime}\leq i}\tilde{\mathcal{A}}[k,i,j^{\prime}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}[k,i,j]=\tilde{\mathcal{A}}[k,i,j]\big/\sum_{j^{\prime}\leq i}\tilde{\mathcal{A}}[k,i,j^{\prime}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Compute the estimate: <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{v}\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{v}\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}}[k,i]=\sum_{{j\leq i}}\mathcal{A}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}}[k,i]=\sum_{{j\leq i}}\mathcal{A}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.11" class="ltx_p">Optionally, add a residual connection: 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
<table id="S3.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}}[k,i]\leftarrow(\mathbf{1}-\bm{\delta})\odot\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]+\bm{\delta}\odot\mathbf{\bar{Z}}[k,i],\quad\bm{\delta}\in(0,1]^{d_{v}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>𝜹</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝜹</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>𝜹</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}}[k,i]\leftarrow(\mathbf{1}-\bm{\delta})\odot\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]+\bm{\delta}\odot\mathbf{\bar{Z}}[k,i],\quad\bm{\delta}\in(0,1]^{d_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.12" class="ltx_p">After <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> layers with shared weights, compute the prediction <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}^{\text{pred}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{e}\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐙</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}^{\text{pred}}\in\mathbb{C}^{d_{e}\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> using a one-step forward transition:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}[k,i]=\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}[k,i+1,i]\cdot\mathbf{\bar{Z}}[k,i]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}[k,i]=\mathcal{E}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}[k,i+1,i]\cdot\mathbf{\bar{Z}}[k,i]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.13" class="ltx_p">Map back to the original basis:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}^{\text{pred}}[k,i]=\mathbf{W_{p}}\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}[k,i]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐙</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}^{\text{pred}}[k,i]=\mathbf{W_{p}}\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}[k,i]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.14" class="ltx_p">This adaptive filter generalizes attention by introducing a more structured similarity measure that integrates uncertainty and time decay. If <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{k}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{v}}\rightarrow\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{k}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{v}},\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{v}}\rightarrow\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the relative temporal decay on the attention weights disappears and we are left with a tensor generalization of standard attention. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">By using the same (diagonal) matrix exponential to filter and to predict the next step, we enforce self-consistency in the model. One issue is that it may be preferable to do multiple steps of iterative refinement of the estimated trajectory before prediction. One way to address this is to give the model extra flexibility by outputting a gated interpolation between estimate and prediction. That is:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{k+1}_{ii}=\bigl(1-\mathbf{g}^{(k)}\bigr)\,\mathbf{e}_{i}^{(k)}+\mathbf{g}^{(k)}\,\mathbf{p}_{i}^{(k)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐠</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐠</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}^{k+1}_{ii}=\bigl(1-\mathbf{g}^{(k)}\bigr)\,\mathbf{e}_{i}^{(k)}+\mathbf{g}^{(k)}\,\mathbf{p}_{i}^{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.15" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the estimate, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the prediction, and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m40" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{g}^{(k)}\in(0,1]^{d_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐠</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}^{(k)}\in(0,1]^{d_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a learnable gate. We can also make <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐠</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> a function of local residuals or features, for example:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}^{(k)}=\sigma\!\left(\mathbf{a}^{\top}\phi\!\left(\|\mathbf{r}^{(k)}\|^{2}\right)+\mathbf{b}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐠</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.426em;" width="0.426em"><mi>ϕ</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐛</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}^{(k)}=\sigma\!\left(\mathbf{a}^{\top}\phi\!\left(\|\mathbf{r}^{(k)}\|^{2}\right)+\mathbf{b}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.16" class="ltx_p">so the layer decides (data-dependently) whether to predict or to keep refining the estimate.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Complexity</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Vanilla attention with input length <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and embedding dimension <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> has time complexity <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d)</annotation></semantics></math> to compute attention scores and apply them across the sequence, plus <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(md^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(md^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> to transform the inputs into query, key, and value vectors and to transform the outputs through a linear layer. The storage of the query, key, and value matrices requires <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(md)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(md)</annotation></semantics></math> memory, and the attention matrix requires <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> memory. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The above tensor form of attention involves element-wise multiplication of <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times m\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times m\times m</annotation></semantics></math> tensors, resulting in time complexity <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d+md^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d+md^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the same as vanilla attention, but slower in practice due to less-optimized element-wise operations. The time complexity to propagate the precision matrices <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> through the differential Lyapunov equation in the full (non-diagonalizable case) is <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(d^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(d^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>, plus another <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(d^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(d^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> to invert each of these matrices, for each of the <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> time differences. Hence, the total time complexity is <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. In contrast, for systems that admit a closed-form solution, the propagation and matrix inversions become <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(d)</annotation></semantics></math>, so the total time complexity is <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d)</annotation></semantics></math>. If the measurements are sampled at equal time intervals, the time complexity reduces to <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(md)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(md)</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Hence, the main bottleneck is not run-time, but memory, as we need to store all <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> residuals, pulled-forward estimates, and the attention tensor, which are all tensors of size <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d)</annotation></semantics></math>. In the following sections, we examine how to simplify the algorithm to avoid this bottleneck.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Convolutional Representation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If the time steps are equal, i.e. <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=t_{i+1}-t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=t_{i+1}-t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed for all <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we can store all <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ij" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ij</annotation></semantics></math> exponentials in a kernel of size <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2(m-1)d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2(m-1)d</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-1)d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-1)d</annotation></semantics></math> in the causal case, rather than <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{2}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{2}d</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, we compute: <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}[\tau]=e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}\Delta t\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}[\tau]=e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}\Delta t\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}[\tau]=e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}}\Delta t\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}[\tau]=e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}}\Delta t\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in[m-1,-(m-1)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in[m-1,-(m-1)]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}=\left[e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}(m-1)\Delta t},e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}(m-2)\Delta t},\dots,e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}\Delta t},e^{\mathbf{0}},e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}\Delta t},\dots,e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}(m-1)\Delta t},e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}m\Delta t}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>𝟎</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}=\left[e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}(m-1)\Delta t},e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}(m-2)\Delta t},\dots,e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}\Delta t},e^{\mathbf{0}},e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}\Delta t},\dots,e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}(m-1)\Delta t},e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}m\Delta t}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">or in the causal case, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in[m-1,0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in[m-1,0]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}=\left[e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}(m-1)\Delta t},e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}(m-2)\Delta t},\dots,e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}\Delta t},1,\dots,1\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}=\left[e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}(m-1)\Delta t},e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}(m-2)\Delta t},\dots,e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}}\Delta t},1,\dots,1\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">(where we pad the kernel with <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> 1s for easier indexing.) We define <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}</annotation></semantics></math> similarly. We can then efficiently compute the exponentials using a Toeplitz matrix to index from <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}k}(t_{i}-t_{j})}=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}[m-(i-j)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}k}(t_{i}-t_{j})}=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}[m-(i-j)]</annotation></semantics></math>. The estimate tensors are then: <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}[m-(i-j)]\cdot\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}[m-(i-j)]\cdot\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}[m-(i-j)]\cdot\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}[m-(i-j)]\cdot\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Similarly, the precision tensor is Toeplitz, so we can again represent it with a kernel of size <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="md" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">md</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{V}[\tau]=\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{qk}}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{qk}}\odot\frac{\mathbf{1}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})\Delta t\tau}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})}+\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{qk}}\odot e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})\Delta t\tau}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{V}[\tau]=\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{qk}}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{qk}}\odot\frac{\mathbf{1}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})\Delta t\tau}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})}+\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{qk}}\odot e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})\Delta t\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which we can express in terms of <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}[\tau]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}[\tau]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{V}[\tau]=\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{qk}}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{qk}}\odot\frac{\mathbf{1}-\mathcal{K}^{\dagger}_{\mathbf{k}}[\tau]\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}[\tau]}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})}+\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{qk}}\odot\big(\mathcal{K}^{\dagger}_{\mathbf{k}}[\tau]\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}[\tau]\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{V}[\tau]=\bm{\lambda}_{C\mathbf{qk}}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{Q\mathbf{qk}}\odot\frac{\mathbf{1}-\mathcal{K}^{\dagger}_{\mathbf{k}}[\tau]\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}[\tau]}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}})}+\bm{\lambda}_{R\mathbf{qk}}\odot\big(\mathcal{K}^{\dagger}_{\mathbf{k}}[\tau]\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}[\tau]\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">The full precision tensor is then:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\mathbf{k}}^{C}[k,i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\mathbf{k}}^{C}[k,i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{V}[k,|i-j|]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>V</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{V}[k,|i-j|]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and similarly for <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}^{P}[\tau]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{v}}^{P}[\tau]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{\mathbf{v}}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{\mathbf{v}}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">However, we must still store the full tensors of pulled-forward estimates <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math>, which are of size <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{k}\times m\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{k}\times m\times m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{v}\times m\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{v}\times m\times m</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Broadcasting the Estimates</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To avoid explicitly constructing the pulled-forward estimates <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math>, we can define separate arrays for the <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> components:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]:=e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}k}t_{i}},\quad\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]:=e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}k}t_{j}}\mathbf{Z_{v}}[k,j]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]:=e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}k}t_{i}},\quad\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]:=e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{v}k}t_{j}}\mathbf{Z_{v}}[k,j].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We can then factorize <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">And likewise for <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math>. This requires <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2md" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2md</annotation></semantics></math> computations rather than <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="md" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">md</annotation></semantics></math>, but reduces the memory requirement from <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{2}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{2}d</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2md" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2md</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Since <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, we can pull it outside the sum:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}[k,i]:=\sum_{j\leq i}\mathcal{A}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]\cdot\sum_{j\leq i}\mathcal{A}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}[k,i]:=\sum_{j\leq i}\mathcal{A}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]\cdot\sum_{j\leq i}\mathcal{A}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">So we can avoid forming the full <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{v}\times m\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{v}\times m\times m</annotation></semantics></math> tensor <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Factorizing the Residuals</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]=\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i]-\hat{\mathcal{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]=\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i]-\hat{\mathcal{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Letting:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]=e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}}t_{i}},\quad\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]=e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}}t_{j}}\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j],\quad\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]=e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}}t_{i}}\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]=e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}}t_{i}},\quad\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]=e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}}t_{j}}\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j],\quad\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]=e^{-\bm{\lambda}_{\mathbf{qk}}t_{i}}\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\cdot\left(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]-\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\mathcal{\hat{R}}[k,i,j]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\cdot\left(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]-\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\mathcal{\hat{R}}[k,i,j],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{R}}[k,i,j]:=\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]-\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{R}}[k,i,j]:=\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]-\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We need to compute the robust weights:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}[i,j]:=\sum_{k}\mathcal{\bar{R}}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}[i,j]:=\sum_{k}\mathcal{\bar{R}}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\mathcal{\bar{\hat{R}}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{\hat{R}}[k,i,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\mathcal{\bar{\hat{R}}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\mathcal{\hat{R}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]-\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\cdot\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\left(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]-\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]-\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\cdot\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]\cdot\left(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]-\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.5" class="ltx_p">(where the overbar denotes element-wise complex conjugation). We can avoid constructing <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> by expanding the product, and <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]</annotation></semantics></math> by using the kernel <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{D}[i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\Big[\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{D}[i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\Big[\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-2\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-2\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.6" class="ltx_p">But computing the product <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]</annotation></semantics></math> still requires constructing a <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{k}\times m\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{k}\times m\times m</annotation></semantics></math> tensor.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.6 </span>Isotropic Decay and Noise</h3>

<div id="S3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]</annotation></semantics></math> loses its <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-dependence, each of the terms in <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}[i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}[i,j]</annotation></semantics></math> simplifies to a matrix multiplication. In particular, let us assume that the real part of the eigenvalues is a shared scalar:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex132" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}=\alpha+i\omega_{k},\quad\alpha,\omega_{k}\in\mathbb{R}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}=\alpha+i\omega_{k},\quad\alpha,\omega_{k}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This corresponds to a system with state matrix <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonalizable over <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℂ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, and has strictly imaginary eigenvalues, i.e. <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}=\text{diag}(\lambda_{\Omega,1},\dots\lambda_{\Omega,d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}=\text{diag}(\lambda_{\Omega,1},\dots\lambda_{\Omega,d})</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\Omega,k}\in i\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\Omega,k}\in i\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also assume that the noise is isotropic, i.e. that the noise parameters are scalar multiples of identity:
<math id="S3.SS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{C}=\lambda_{C}\mathbf{I},\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}=\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I},\bm{\Lambda}_{R}=\eta^{2}\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{C}=\lambda_{C}\mathbf{I},\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}=\sigma^{2}\mathbf{I},\bm{\Lambda}_{R}=\eta^{2}\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Note that we could define separate query/key and value dynamic parameters <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, but here we use shared parameters for simplicity. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Our covariance kernel becomes:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{K}^{V}(\tau)=\sigma_{V}^{2}(\tau)\mathbf{I}_{d},\quad\text{where:}\quad\sigma_{V}^{2}(\tau)=\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\frac{1-e^{-2\alpha\Delta t\tau}}{-2\alpha}+\eta^{2}e^{-2\alpha\Delta t\tau}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where:</mtext><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}^{V}(\tau)=\sigma_{V}^{2}(\tau)\mathbf{I}_{d},\quad\text{where:}\quad\sigma_{V}^{2}(\tau)=\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\frac{1-e^{-2\alpha\Delta t\tau}}{-2\alpha}+\eta^{2}e^{-2\alpha\Delta t\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and the <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ij" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ij</annotation></semantics></math>th component of the precision matrix becomes:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{V}^{2}(|i-j|)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{ij}^{C}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{V}^{2}(|i-j|)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We can then pull <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{k}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{k}}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> outside the sum:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}[i,j]=\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{k}}[i,j]\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\Big[\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}-2\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}[i,j]=\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{k}}[i,j]\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\Big[\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}-2\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.5" class="ltx_p">We can now express each of these three sums as matrix products:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}=\sum_{k}\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\odot\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\|^{2}\big)\in\mathbb{R}^{m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}=\sum_{k}\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\odot\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\|^{2}\big)\in\mathbb{R}^{m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}=\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\big)^{\top}\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\|^{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}=\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\big)^{\top}\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\|^{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex138" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]=\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\odot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\big)^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\in\mathbb{C}^{m\times m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]=\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\odot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\big)^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\in\mathbb{C}^{m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.6" class="ltx_p">We then sum terms, where the first term is broadcast from an <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times 1</annotation></semantics></math> vector to an <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times m</annotation></semantics></math> matrix:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}:=\mathbf{1}_{m}\big(\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\odot\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\|^{2}\big)^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{d}\big)^{\top}+\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\big)^{\top}\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\|^{2}-2\mathrm{Re}\Big(\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\odot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\big)^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}:=\mathbf{1}_{m}\big(\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\odot\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\|^{2}\big)^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{d}\big)^{\top}+\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\big)^{\top}\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\|^{2}-2\mathrm{Re}\Big(\big(\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}\odot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\big)^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.7" class="ltx_p">We can factor out <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\alpha t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\alpha t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us define:
Let <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E_{qk}}_{ij}=e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E_{qk}}_{ij}=e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E_{qk}}[i,j]=e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}[k,i]:=e^{i\omega_{k}t_{i}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}[k,i]:=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{i}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E_{qk}}[i,j]=e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}[k,i]:=e^{i\omega_{k}t_{i}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}[k,i]:=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.8" class="ltx_p">And:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}[k,i]:=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{i}}\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i],\quad\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}[k,j]:=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{j}}\mathbf{Z_{k}}[k,j]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}[k,i]:=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{i}}\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i],\quad\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}[k,j]:=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{j}}\mathbf{Z_{k}}[k,j].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.9" class="ltx_p">that is,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\alpha t_{i}}\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}[k,i]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i],\quad e^{-\alpha t_{i}}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}[k,i]:=\mathbf{\hat{Z}_{q}}[k,i],\quad e^{-\alpha t_{j}}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}[k,j]:=\mathbf{\hat{Z}_{k}}[k,j]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\alpha t_{i}}\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}[k,i]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i],\quad e^{-\alpha t_{i}}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}[k,i]:=\mathbf{\hat{Z}_{q}}[k,i],\quad e^{-\alpha t_{j}}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}[k,j]:=\mathbf{\hat{Z}_{k}}[k,j].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Or in matrix form:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}:=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{q}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}:=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{k}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}:=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{q}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}:=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.11" class="ltx_p">So:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]=e^{i\omega_{k}t_{i}}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}[k,i]-e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})}\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}[k,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i,j]=e^{i\omega_{k}t_{i}}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}[k,i]-e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})}\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}[k,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.12" class="ltx_p">Or in matrix form:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}\odot\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}-\mathbf{E_{qk}}\odot(\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+})^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}\odot\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}-\mathbf{E_{qk}}\odot(\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+})^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.13" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}=e^{2\alpha t_{i}}\sum_{k}\Big[e^{-2\alpha t_{i}}\|\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+e^{-2\alpha t_{j}}\|\mathbf{Z_{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}-2\mathrm{Re}\left(e^{-\alpha t_{i}}e^{-\alpha t_{j}}\mathbf{\bar{\tilde{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}=e^{2\alpha t_{i}}\sum_{k}\Big[e^{-2\alpha t_{i}}\|\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+e^{-2\alpha t_{j}}\|\mathbf{Z_{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}-2\mathrm{Re}\left(e^{-\alpha t_{i}}e^{-\alpha t_{j}}\mathbf{\bar{\tilde{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex147" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\sum_{k}\|\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+e^{2\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})}\sum_{k}\|\mathbf{Z_{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}-2e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})}\sum_{k}\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\tilde{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\sum_{k}\|\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+e^{2\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})}\sum_{k}\|\mathbf{Z_{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}-2e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})}\sum_{k}\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\tilde{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.14" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{d_{k}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{k}\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{d_{k}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{k}\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math> be column vectors of <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>s. In matrix form:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}=\mathbf{1}_{m}\big(\mathbf{1}_{d_{k}}^{\top}|\mathbf{Z_{q}}|^{2}\big)+\mathbf{E_{qk}}^{2}\odot\big(\mathbf{1}_{d_{k}}^{\top}|\mathbf{Z_{k}}|^{2}\big)^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}^{\top}-2\mathbf{E_{qk}}\odot\mathrm{Re}\big(\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}=\mathbf{1}_{m}\big(\mathbf{1}_{d_{k}}^{\top}|\mathbf{Z_{q}}|^{2}\big)+\mathbf{E_{qk}}^{2}\odot\big(\mathbf{1}_{d_{k}}^{\top}|\mathbf{Z_{k}}|^{2}\big)^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}^{\top}-2\mathbf{E_{qk}}\odot\mathrm{Re}\big(\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.15" class="ltx_p">(where the modulus is taken element-wise). So we need three matrix products and two element-wise multiplications, as opposed to dot-product attention’s one matrix product. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We can then compute the un-normalized attention matrix:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex149" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{A}}=\frac{\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}}{1+\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{k}}\odot\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}/\nu}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{A}}=\frac{\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}}{1+\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{k}}\odot\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}/\nu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.16" class="ltx_p">(where division is again taken element-wise.) The above formulation reduces the required memory to <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Define a score matrix: <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{L}=\log(\mathbf{P_v}^C)-\log\left(1+\mathbf{P_{k}}^{C}\odot\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}/\nu\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>𝐤</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L}=\log(\mathbf{P_v}^C)-\log\left(1+\mathbf{P_{k}}^{C}\odot\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}/\nu\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, 
<br class="ltx_break">and a causal mask <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>causal</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We can then express the row-normalization using softmax: 
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="S3.SS6.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}[i,j]=e^{\mathbf{L}[i,j]\odot\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}}\big/\sum_{j}e^{\mathbf{L}[i,j]\odot\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>causal</mtext></msub></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>causal</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}[i,j]=e^{\mathbf{L}[i,j]\odot\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}}\big/\sum_{j}e^{\mathbf{L}[i,j]\odot\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">If the query-key and value dynamics parameters are shared, <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{k}}=\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}:=\mathbf{P}^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{k}}=\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}:=\mathbf{P}^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, so:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex150" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{L}=-\log\left(\mathbf{V}^{C}+\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}/\nu\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L}=-\log\left(\mathbf{V}^{C}+\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}/\nu\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.17" class="ltx_p">The estimate is:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex151" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}[k,i]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]\cdot\sum_{j}\mathbf{A}[i,j]\cdot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}[k,i]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]\cdot\sum_{j}\mathbf{A}[i,j]\cdot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.18" class="ltx_p">Define:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex152" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E_{v}}[i,j]=e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}[k,i]:=e^{i\omega_{k}t_{i}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-}[k,i]:=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{i}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E_{v}}[i,j]=e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}[k,i]:=e^{i\omega_{k}t_{i}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-}[k,i]:=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.19" class="ltx_p">And define:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex153" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{v}}:=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{v}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{v}}:=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{v}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.20" class="ltx_p">That is,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex154" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\alpha t_{i}}\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}[k,i]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i],\quad e^{-\alpha t_{i}}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{v}}[k,i]:=\mathbf{\hat{Z}_{v}}[k,i]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\alpha t_{i}}\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}[k,i]=\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i],\quad e^{-\alpha t_{i}}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{v}}[k,i]:=\mathbf{\hat{Z}_{v}}[k,i].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.21" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{A}}=\mathbf{A}\odot\mathbf{E_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{A}}=\mathbf{A}\odot\mathbf{E_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}[k,i]=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}[k,i]\odot\sum_{j}\mathbf{\hat{A}}[i,j]\cdot\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⊙</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}[k,i]=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}[k,i]\odot\sum_{j}\mathbf{\hat{A}}[i,j]\cdot\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.22" class="ltx_p">which, in matrix form, is:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}\odot(\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}\mathbf{\hat{A}}^{\dagger})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}\odot(\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}\mathbf{\hat{A}}^{\dagger})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.23" class="ltx_p">Or, in a form more typical for attention:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}^{\dagger}=(\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+})^{\dagger}\odot(\mathbf{\hat{A}}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\dagger})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}^{\dagger}=(\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+})^{\dagger}\odot(\mathbf{\hat{A}}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\dagger})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.24" class="ltx_p">Finally, the prediction is:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}=(e^{\alpha\Delta t}e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t})\odot\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}=(e^{\alpha\Delta t}e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t})\odot\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.25" class="ltx_p">This factorization, which separates scalar decay/growth (magnitude) from oscillatory components (direction), reduces the memory requirement of the algorithm from <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}+md)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}+md)</annotation></semantics></math>, as in vanilla attention, while maintaining the <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}d)</annotation></semantics></math> compute time. This comes at the price of losing the second-order information provided by the full tensors <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Whereas <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}},\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{qk}},\mathcal{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the confidence of the <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th feature’s projection from time <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> to time <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{k}},\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{k}},\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\mathbf{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> represent measurements of overall confidence between query and key. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The assumption that the real part of the eigenvalues is a shared scalar serves two purposes: (a) it allows the cross term to be represented as a matrix multiplication, which reduces the memory requirement, and (b) it improves the exploding/vanishing gradient problem for <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, because rather than computing <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\alpha t_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\alpha t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-\alpha t_{j}}(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\alpha t_{j}}(</annotation></semantics></math> separately, we compute <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\alpha(t_{i}-t_{j})}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}&gt;t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}&gt;t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for causal systems. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">An alternative approach to simplify the tensor precision-weighted average into a tractable form with <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2}+md)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2}+md)</annotation></semantics></math> memory is to factorize the precision kernel into a product of factors depending separately on indices <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. We briefly explore this approach in the Appendix.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.7 </span>Unitary Dynamics</h3>

<div id="S3.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If we further constrain our state matrix <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> to have purely imaginary eigenvalues, i.e. <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\mathbf{\Lambda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>𝚲</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\mathbf{\Lambda}}</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal, and our dynamical system is unitary (norm preserving) in the eigenbasis. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Using L’Hôpital’s rule:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{k})\to 0}\frac{1-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{k})\Delta t\tau}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{k})}=\Delta t\,\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{k})\to 0}\frac{1-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{k})\Delta t\tau}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\lambda_{k})}=\Delta t\,\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Our covariance kernel becomes:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{K}^{V}(\tau)=\sigma_{V}^{2}(\tau)\mathbf{I}_{d},\quad\text{where:}\quad\sigma_{V}^{2}(\tau):=\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\Delta t\tau+\eta^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where:</mtext><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}^{V}(\tau)=\sigma_{V}^{2}(\tau)\mathbf{I}_{d},\quad\text{where:}\quad\sigma_{V}^{2}(\tau):=\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\Delta t\tau+\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.3" class="ltx_p">And the <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ij" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ij</annotation></semantics></math>th component of the precision matrix becomes:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{ij}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{V}^{2}(|i-j|)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{ij}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{V}^{2}(|i-j|)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since the eigenvalues are purely imaginary, <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|=\|e^{\bm{\lambda}t_{i}}\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|=\|e^{\bm{\lambda}t_{i}}\|=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and:
<math id="S3.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|=\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|=\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,j]\|=\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,j]\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,j]\|=\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,j]\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex162" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{R_{qk}}[i,j]\|^{2}=\sum_{k}\Big(\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}-2\mathrm{Re}\big(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\big)\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{R_{qk}}[i,j]\|^{2}=\sum_{k}\Big(\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}-2\mathrm{Re}\big(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\big)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.5" class="ltx_p">If, in addition, <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is unitary (in which case <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is skew-symmetric), then <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{Z}[k,i]\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{Z}[k,i]\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{Z}[k,i]\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{Z}[k,i]\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, so if the inputs have been normalized to unit length, then: <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}=\sum_{k}\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}=\sum_{k}\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex163" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{R_{qk}}\|^{2}=2\Big(1-\mathrm{Re}\big(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big)\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{R_{qk}}\|^{2}=2\Big(1-\mathrm{Re}\big(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.6" class="ltx_p">The score matrix is:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex164" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{L}=-\log\Big( \nu\mathbf{V}^C + 2 - 2\mathrm{Re} \big( \mathbf{\hat{Z}}_\mathbf{q}^\dagger\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_\mathbf{k}\big) \Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L}=-\log\Big( \nu\mathbf{V}^C + 2 - 2\mathrm{Re} \big( \mathbf{\hat{Z}}_\mathbf{q}^\dagger\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_\mathbf{k}\big) \Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex165" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=-\log(\nu\mathbf{V}^C + 2)-\log\left(1-\frac{2\mathrm{Re}\big(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big)}{\nu\mathbf{V}^{C}+2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=-\log(\nu\mathbf{V}^C + 2)-\log\left(1-\frac{2\mathrm{Re}\big(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big)}{\nu\mathbf{V}^{C}+2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Expanding around <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, this is approximately:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{L}\approx-\log(\nu\mathbf{V}^C + 2)+\frac{2\mathrm{Re}\big(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big)}{\nu\mathbf{V}^{C}+2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐋</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L}\approx-\log(\nu\mathbf{V}^C + 2)+\frac{2\mathrm{Re}\big(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big)}{\nu\mathbf{V}^{C}+2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.8" class="ltx_p">If we set <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> (zero process noise), then <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{C}=\eta^{2}\mathbf{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{C}=\eta^{2}\mathbf{1}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes a simple scalar bias. Letting <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=2/(\nu\eta^{2}+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=2/(\nu\eta^{2}+2)</annotation></semantics></math>, the unnormalized softmax becomes:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex167" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tau}{2}\cdot\exp(\tau\mathrm{Re} \big( \mathbf{\hat{Z}}_\mathbf{q}^\dagger\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_\mathbf{k}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tau}{2}\cdot\exp(\tau\mathrm{Re} \big( \mathbf{\hat{Z}}_\mathbf{q}^\dagger\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_\mathbf{k}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.9" class="ltx_p">The constant term <math id="S3.SS7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tau}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tau}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> outside the exponential cancels in the normalization. The imaginary part of the matrix exponential becomes a multiplicative relative positional encoding, and we recover a complex-valued form of ordinary dot-product attention.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.8 </span>Implementation</h3>

<section id="S3.SS8.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.8.1 </span>Adaptive Filter Attention</h4>

<div id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now present an implementation of the above algorithm, for the case of isotropic noise and decay. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We use scalar noise parameters <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2},\eta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2},\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and dynamics parameters <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\bm{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\bm{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the real part of the eigenvalues is set to <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\alpha^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\alpha^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure stability of our LTI model. Note that the eigenvalues of <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> appear in complex conjugate pairs, as a necessary condition for <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> to be real, so we can write the vector of eigenvalues as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex168" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}=\big\{i\omega_{1},-i\omega_{1},\dots,i\omega_{d/2},-i\omega_{d/2}\big\},\,\omega_{k}\in\mathbb{R}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}=\big\{i\omega_{1},-i\omega_{1},\dots,i\omega_{d/2},-i\omega_{d/2}\big\},\,\omega_{k}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We switch from the rational weight <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{1+r_{ij}^{2}/\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{1+r_{ij}^{2}/\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> to the equivalent exponential–log form <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\!\big(-\tau_{s}\log(1+r_{ij}^2/\nu)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\!\big(-\tau_{s}\log(1+r_{ij}^2/\nu)\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, which both improves numerical stability and introduces a temperature parameter <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> that controls the sharpness of the weighting; this reduces exactly to the rational form when <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We drop <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{C}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{C}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> since we can absorb it into <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and drop the Mahalanobis scale <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, since we can absorb it into <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma,\eta,\tau_{s},\mathbf{W}_{Q},\mathbf{W}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma,\eta,\tau_{s},\mathbf{W}_{Q},\mathbf{W}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Note that <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> is similar to a block diagonal matrix of <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> rotation matrices, i.e. there exists some <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{-1}\bm{\Omega}\mathbf{P}=\operatorname{blockdiag}\left(\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;-\omega_{1}\\[2.0pt]
\omega_{1}&amp;0\end{bmatrix},\dots,\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;-\omega_{d/2}\\[2.0pt]
\omega_{d/2}&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>blockdiag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>ω</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{-1}\bm{\Omega}\mathbf{P}=\operatorname{blockdiag}\left(\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;-\omega_{1}\\[2.0pt]
\omega_{1}&amp;0\end{bmatrix},\dots,\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;-\omega_{d/2}\\[2.0pt]
\omega_{d/2}&amp;0\end{bmatrix}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">However, to retain our fully diagonalized representation, we must work with complex numbers. We define the following linear layer variant to reproduce the effect of complex multiplication: 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Complex Linear Layer.</span> We denote a complex linear layer by <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>. Instead of operating directly on complex vectors, we represent inputs and outputs by stacking their real and imaginary parts. For an input <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}=\left[\mathbf{x}_{r},\mathbf{x}_{i}\right]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}=\left[\mathbf{x}_{r},\mathbf{x}_{i}\right]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{r},\mathbf{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{r},\mathbf{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the layer computes:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex170" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x})=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{W}_{r}&amp;-\mathbf{W}_{i}\\[4.0pt]
\mathbf{W}_{i}&amp;\mathbf{W}_{r}\end{bmatrix}\mathbf{x}+\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{b}_{r}\\[4.0pt]
\mathbf{b}_{i}\end{bmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x})=\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{W}_{r}&amp;-\mathbf{W}_{i}\\[4.0pt]
\mathbf{W}_{i}&amp;\mathbf{W}_{r}\end{bmatrix}\mathbf{x}+\begin{bmatrix}\mathbf{b}_{r}\\[4.0pt]
\mathbf{b}_{i}\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{r},\mathbf{W}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{e}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{r},\mathbf{W}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{e}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> are the real and imaginary weight matrices, and <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}_{r},\mathbf{b}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{e}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}_{r},\mathbf{b}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{e}}</annotation></semantics></math> are real-valued biases (where <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> is the embedding dimension). This construction is equivalent to multiplication by a complex weight matrix <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{r}+i\mathbf{W}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{r}+i\mathbf{W}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with bias <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{b}_{r}+i\mathbf{b}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{b}_{r}+i\mathbf{b}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, while remaining entirely in the real domain. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We initialize the complex linear layer weights isotropically in the complex plane as:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex171" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{ij}:=\mathbf{W}_{r,ij}+i\mathbf{W}_{i,ij}=\alpha_{ij}\begin{bmatrix}\cos(\phi_{ij})\\
\sin(\phi_{ij})\end{bmatrix},\quad\alpha_{ij}\sim\sqrt{\tfrac{2}{d_{\text{in}}+d_{\text{{out}}}}}\,\mathcal{N}(0,1),\;\;\phi_{ij}\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{ij}:=\mathbf{W}_{r,ij}+i\mathbf{W}_{i,ij}=\alpha_{ij}\begin{bmatrix}\cos(\phi_{ij})\\
\sin(\phi_{ij})\end{bmatrix},\quad\alpha_{ij}\sim\sqrt{\tfrac{2}{d_{\text{in}}+d_{\text{{out}}}}}\,\mathcal{N}(0,1),\;\;\phi_{ij}\sim\mathcal{U}(0,2\pi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Since the inputs to the network layer are real-valued, we can concatenate a vector of zeros to the inputs to represent the imaginary part. In general, the outputs of the network layer may be complex-valued. We pass the real part of the output to the next layer and discard the imaginary part. Alternatively, we can design the input and output projections to map between real and complex inputs/outputs. We pursue the former option here, for simplicity. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Another option to enforce real inputs is to impose a penalty on <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})\|</annotation></semantics></math> or on <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{W_{v}}\mathbf{W_{p}}-\mathbf{I}^{d_{v}\times d_{v}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐈</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{W_{v}}\mathbf{W_{p}}-\mathbf{I}^{d_{v}\times d_{v}}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, we do not impose penalties and allow these matrices to freely vary. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">If our data has a known time scale, we can set <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> as a known constant, otherwise we can treat it as a learned parameter. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">In our implementation, queries and keys are computed from the current values rather than directly from the raw inputs. This design enables a natural recursive approximation of full batch attention: as the value estimates are iteratively updated at each step, the queries and keys reflect the latest state, allowing each iteration to propagate residual information through the trajectory. This is optional. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">For clarity, we present the single-head version. A multi-head extension may be obtained in the usual way by applying the procedure in parallel with separate projections and concatenating the outputs, with each head having its own set of complex linear layers <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{Q},\mathcal{L}_{K},\mathcal{L}_{V},\mathcal{L}_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{Q},\mathcal{L}_{K},\mathcal{L}_{V},\mathcal{L}_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and dynamics parameters <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\bm{\omega},\sigma,\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\bm{\omega},\sigma,\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">For simplicity, we use shared dynamic parameters <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\bm{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝎</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\bm{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math> for the queries/keys and values, so <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define these as separate variables however, since in general they can be different.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Adaptive Filter Attention (Single Head)</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Input sequence <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Complex linear layers:</span> <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{Q},\mathcal{L}_{K},\mathcal{L}_{V},\mathcal{L}_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{Q},\mathcal{L}_{K},\mathcal{L}_{V},\mathcal{L}_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>; dynamics/noise parameters: <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\bm{\omega},\sigma,\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\bm{\omega},\sigma,\eta</annotation></semantics></math>; time step <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>; softmax temperature <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>; residual weight <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Constants:</span> Causal mask <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}\in\{0,1\}^{m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>causal</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}\in\{0,1\}^{m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>; stability constant <math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">(Define <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}:=\Delta t\cdot i,\quad t_{j}:=\Delta t\cdot j\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}:=\Delta t\cdot i,\quad t_{j}:=\Delta t\cdot j\ </annotation></semantics></math>.)
<span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Complex-valued Projections:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline">Lift real inputs to complex by concatenating zeros: <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}=\left[\mathbf{Z}_{r},\mathbf{0}\right]^{\top}\in\mathbb{C}^{2\times d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}=\left[\mathbf{Z}_{r},\mathbf{0}\right]^{\top}\in\mathbb{C}^{2\times d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{V}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z})\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{V}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z})\big).</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{q}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{q}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{Q}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{q}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{q}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{Q}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, 
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{k}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{k}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{K}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{k}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{k}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{K}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exponential kernels:</span>

<table id="S3.Ex172" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[\tau]=\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&gt;0\}}\odot e^{-\alpha^{2}\Delta t\tau}+\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau\leq 0\}},\quad\mathcal{K}_{\bm{\omega}}[\tau]=\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&gt;0\}}\odot e^{\bm{\omega}\Delta t\tau}+\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau\leq 0\}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[\tau]=\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&gt;0\}}\odot e^{-\alpha^{2}\Delta t\tau}+\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau\leq 0\}},\quad\mathcal{K}_{\bm{\omega}}[\tau]=\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&gt;0\}}\odot e^{\bm{\omega}\Delta t\tau}+\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau\leq 0\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decay kernel:</span>
<math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa[\tau]=\frac{1-\mathcal{K}^{2}_{\alpha}[\tau]+\epsilon}{2\alpha^{2}+\epsilon}\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}&gt;\epsilon\}}+\tau\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}\leq\epsilon\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa[\tau]=\frac{1-\mathcal{K}^{2}_{\alpha}[\tau]+\epsilon}{2\alpha^{2}+\epsilon}\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}&gt;\epsilon\}}+\tau\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}\leq\epsilon\}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Covariance kernel:</span>
<math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{V}(\tau)=\sigma^{2}\kappa[|\tau|]+\eta^{2}\mathcal{K}^{2}_{\alpha}[|\tau|],\quad\mathbf{V}^{C}[i,j]=\sigma^{2}_{V}(i-j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{V}(\tau)=\sigma^{2}\kappa[|\tau|]+\eta^{2}\mathcal{K}^{2}_{\alpha}[|\tau|],\quad\mathbf{V}^{C}[i,j]=\sigma^{2}_{V}(i-j)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Query/Key dynamics:</span>

<table id="S3.Ex173" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E_{qk}}[i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[i-j]=\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[i]\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[j]^{-\top},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{+}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]=e^{i\bm{\omega}_{k}t_{i}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{-}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]=e^{-i\bm{\omega}_{k}t_{i}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E_{qk}}[i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[i-j]=\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[i]\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[j]^{-\top},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{+}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]=e^{i\bm{\omega}_{k}t_{i}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{-}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]=e^{-i\bm{\omega}_{k}t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex174" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}[k,i]=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{-}_{\mathbf{qk}}\odot\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i],\quad\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}[k,j]=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{-}_{\mathbf{qk}}\odot\mathbf{Z_{k}}[k,j]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}[k,i]=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{-}_{\mathbf{qk}}\odot\mathbf{Z_{q}}[k,i],\quad\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}[k,j]=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{-}_{\mathbf{qk}}\odot\mathbf{Z_{k}}[k,j]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value dynamics:</span>

<table id="S3.Ex175" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E_{v}}[i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[i-j]=\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[i]\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[j]^{-\top},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{+}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]=e^{i\bm{\omega}_{k}t_{i}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{-}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]=e^{-i\bm{\omega}_{k}t_{i}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝎</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E_{v}}[i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[i-j]=\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[i]\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[j]^{-\top},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{+}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]=e^{i\bm{\omega}_{k}t_{i}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}^{-}_{\mathbf{v}}[k,i]=e^{-i\bm{\omega}_{k}t_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex176" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{v}}[k,i]=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{v}}[k,i]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{v}}[k,i]=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{v}}[k,i]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Squared Residuals:</span>

<table id="S3.Ex177" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}=\mathbf{1}_{m}(\mathbf{1}_{d}^{\top}\|\mathbf{Z_{q}}\|^{2})+\mathbf{E_{qk}}^{2}\odot(\mathbf{1}_{d}^{\top}\|\mathbf{Z_{k}}\|^{2})^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}^{\top}-2\mathbf{E_{qk}}\odot\mathrm{Re}(\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}=\mathbf{1}_{m}(\mathbf{1}_{d}^{\top}\|\mathbf{Z_{q}}\|^{2})+\mathbf{E_{qk}}^{2}\odot(\mathbf{1}_{d}^{\top}\|\mathbf{Z_{k}}\|^{2})^{\top}\mathbf{1}_{m}^{\top}-2\mathbf{E_{qk}}\odot\mathrm{Re}(\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table><span id="algorithm1.4.14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attention matrix:</span>

<table id="S3.Ex178" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{L}=-\log\left(\mathbf{V}^{C}+\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}+\epsilon\right)\odot\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐋</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>causal</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L}=-\log\left(\mathbf{V}^{C}+\|\mathbf{R}_{\mathbf{qk}}\|^{2}+\epsilon\right)\odot\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.Ex179" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}[i,j]=\text{softmax}_{j}\big(\tau_{s}\mathbf{L}[i,j]\big),\quad\mathbf{\hat{A}}=\mathbf{E_{v}}\odot\mathbf{A}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>softmax</mtext><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐋</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}[i,j]=\text{softmax}_{j}\big(\tau_{s}\mathbf{L}[i,j]\big),\quad\mathbf{\hat{A}}=\mathbf{E_{v}}\odot\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table><span id="algorithm1.4.14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output with value dynamics:</span>
<math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}\odot(\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}\mathbf{\hat{A}}^{\dagger})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}\odot(\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}\mathbf{\hat{A}}^{\dagger})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Residual connection:</span>
<math id="algorithm1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}}=(1-\text{sigmoid}(\delta))\mathbf{Z_{v}}+\text{sigmoid}(\delta)\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}}=(1-\text{sigmoid}(\delta))\mathbf{Z_{v}}+\text{sigmoid}(\delta)\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prediction:</span>
<math id="algorithm1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}=(e^{\alpha\Delta t}e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t})\odot\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}=(e^{\alpha\Delta t}e^{\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t})\odot\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output Projection:</span>
<math id="algorithm1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{p}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{P}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{p}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{P}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.18" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return:</span> <math id="algorithm1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm1.4.18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">We discard <math id="algorithm1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.19" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This defines a single neural network layer, which we can train with backpropagation, as usual. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">In summary, this formulation modifies standard attention by including:</p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Complex-valued linear layers;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Complex-valued multiplicative positional encodings with learned parameters;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Scalar decay constants (one per head) with pair-wise uncertainty propagation via the closed-form solution of the differential Lyapunov equation;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A similarity function based on the Mahalanobis-distance;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A shared linear dynamics model for state estimation and prediction, to enforce model self-consistency.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS8.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">A multi-head implementation of Algorithm 1 is available at the following: <a href="https://github.com/PCR-git/AFA/tree/main" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Github Repository</a>. (This repository also contains an implementation of the tensor form discussed in Section 3.1.)</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS8.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.8.2 </span>Unrolled Adaptive Filter Attention</h4>

<div id="S3.SS8.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS8.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At inference time, we can approximately unroll our learned model into a reweighted Kalman Filter. The outer iteration propagates latent states through the sequence for fast, online inference, while the inner iterations at each step approximate the effect of full pairwise attention without incurring <math id="S3.SS8.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(m^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(m^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> computations. The recursive precision update acts as an implicit normalization of the "attention" weights.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>Unrolled Adaptive Filter Attention (Inference)</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Prior state <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{0}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{0}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, measurements <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ii}\}_{i=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ii}\}_{i=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="algorithm2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameters:</span> Complex linear layers <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{Q},\mathcal{L}_{K},\mathcal{L}_{V},\mathcal{L}_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{Q},\mathcal{L}_{K},\mathcal{L}_{V},\mathcal{L}_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>; dynamics/noise parameters: <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\bm{\omega},\sigma,\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\bm{\omega},\sigma,\eta</annotation></semantics></math>; timestep <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>; softmax temperature <math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, residual weight <math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="algorithm2.4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Constants:</span> Causal mask <math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}\in\{0,1\}^{m\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>causal</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}\in\{0,1\}^{m\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>, stability constant <math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Complex-valued Projections:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">Lift real inputs to complex by concatenating zeros: <math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}=\left[\mathbf{z}_{r},\mathbf{0}\right]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}=\left[\mathbf{z}_{r},\mathbf{0}\right]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{z_{v}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{V}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{z}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{z})\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{z_{v}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{V}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{z}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{z})\big).</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">State transition matrix:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\alpha}:=e^{-\alpha^{2}\Delta t},\quad\bm{\Phi}_{\bm{\omega}}:=e^{\bm{\omega}\Delta t},\quad\bm{\Phi}:=\Phi_{\alpha}\bm{\Phi}_{\bm{\omega}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\alpha}:=e^{-\alpha^{2}\Delta t},\quad\bm{\Phi}_{\bm{\omega}}:=e^{\bm{\omega}\Delta t},\quad\bm{\Phi}:=\Phi_{\alpha}\bm{\Phi}_{\bm{\omega}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Innovation covariance:</span> <math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{V}=\sigma^{2}\kappa+\eta^{2}\Phi^{2}_{\alpha},\quad\kappa=\frac{1-\Phi^{2}_{\alpha}+\epsilon}{2\alpha^{2}+\epsilon}\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}&gt;\epsilon\}}+\Delta t\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}\leq\epsilon\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{V}=\sigma^{2}\kappa+\eta^{2}\Phi^{2}_{\alpha},\quad\kappa=\frac{1-\Phi^{2}_{\alpha}+\epsilon}{2\alpha^{2}+\epsilon}\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}&gt;\epsilon\}}+\Delta t\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}\leq\epsilon\}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initial conditions:</span> <math id="algorithm2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}^{+}_{\mathbf{v},0}=\mathbf{z_{v}},\quad p_{0}^{-(0)}=1/\sigma_{V}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}^{+}_{\mathbf{v},0}=\mathbf{z_{v}},\quad p_{0}^{-(0)}=1/\sigma_{V}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.9.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm2.4.9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Initialize prior mean: <math id="algorithm2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{-(0)}=\bm{\Phi}\mathbf{\bar{z}}^{+}_{\mathbf{v},i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{-(0)}=\bm{\Phi}\mathbf{\bar{z}}^{+}_{\mathbf{v},i-1}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{-(0)}=1/(\Phi_{\alpha}^{2}/p_{i-1}^{+}+\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{-(0)}=1/(\Phi_{\alpha}^{2}/p_{i-1}^{+}+\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>   <span id="algorithm2.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Propagated precision</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"><em id="algorithm2.4.12.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> </em><span id="algorithm2.4.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.12.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm2.4.12.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-1</annotation></semantics></math>   <span id="algorithm2.4.12.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_upright">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.12.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_upright">Inner iteration within time step</span></em>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.13.1" class="ltx_text"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.13.2" class="ltx_text"> <span id="algorithm2.4.13.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span></span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recompute queries and keys:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{-(k)}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{-(k)})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{Q}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-(k)}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-(k)})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{-(k)}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{-(k)})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{Q}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-(k)}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-(k)})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{k}}^{-(k)}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{k}}^{-(k)})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{K}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-(k)}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-(k)})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{k}}^{-(k)}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{k}}^{-(k)})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{K}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-(k)}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-(k)})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compute innovations:</span> <math id="algorithm2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{qk}i}^{(k)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{q}i}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{k}i}^{-(k)},\quad\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{(k)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{v}i}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{-(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐤</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{qk}i}^{(k)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{q}i}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{k}i}^{-(k)},\quad\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{(k)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{v}i}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{-(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.18" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Nominal posterior precision (before robust weighting):</span>
<math id="algorithm2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{+(k)}=p_{i}^{-(k)}+1/\sigma^{2}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{+(k)}=p_{i}^{-(k)}+1/\sigma^{2}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.19" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">"Attention" weight:</span> <math id="algorithm2.m25" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{i}^{(k)}=-\log\left(1+p_{i}^{+(k)}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{(k)\dagger}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{(k)}+\epsilon\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.222em">†</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}^{(k)}=-\log\left(1+p_{i}^{+(k)}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{(k)\dagger}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{(k)}+\epsilon\right)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.20" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Weighted posterior precision:</span> <math id="algorithm2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{i}^{+(k)}=p_{i}^{-(k)}+\exp(\tau_s w_i^{(k)})/\sigma_{V}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{i}^{+(k)}=p_{i}^{-(k)}+\exp(\tau_s w_i^{(k)})/\sigma_{V}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.21" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Posterior mean update:</span>

<table id="S3.Ex180" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+(k)}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{-(k)}+\text{sigmoid}(\delta)\,w_{i}^{(k)}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{(k)}/(\tilde{p}_{i}^{+(k)}\sigma_{V}^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+(k)}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{-(k)}+\text{sigmoid}(\delta)\,w_{i}^{(k)}\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{(k)}/(\tilde{p}_{i}^{+(k)}\sigma_{V}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table><span id="algorithm2.4.21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Set prior for next inner iteration:</span>
<math id="algorithm2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{-(k+1)}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+(k)},\quad p_{i}^{-(k+1)}=\tilde{p}_{i}^{+(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{-(k+1)}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+(k)},\quad p_{i}^{-(k+1)}=\tilde{p}_{i}^{+(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.22" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Final posterior for this step:</span> <math id="algorithm2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+(K)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+(K)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{+}=p_{i}^{+(K)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{+}=p_{i}^{+(K)}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.23" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.4.23.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Propagate mean and precision to next time step:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.24" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v},i+1}^{-}=\bm{\Phi}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v},i+1}^{-}=\bm{\Phi}\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="algorithm2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i+1}^{-}=1/(\Phi_{\alpha}^{2}/p_{i}^{+}+\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i+1}^{-}=1/(\Phi_{\alpha}^{2}/p_{i}^{+}+\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.25" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.25.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Map back to original basis:</span> <math id="algorithm2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{z_{p}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{z_{p}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{P}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{z_{p}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{z_{p}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{P}\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{v}i}^{+})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.26" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.26.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return:</span> <math id="algorithm2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{z_{p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{z_{p}})</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.27" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.9 </span>Basic Experiments</h3>

<div id="S3.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We tested our model (Algorithm 1) on a diagonalizable 2D linear system with zero-mean Gaussian process and measurement noise. For reproducibility, we used a fixed state matrix <math id="S3.SS9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex181" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}=\begin{bmatrix}-0.1-i&amp;0\\
0&amp;-0.1+i\end{bmatrix},\quad\mathbf{S}=\begin{bmatrix}1-i&amp;1+i\\
1&amp;1\end{bmatrix},\quad\mathbf{S}^{-1}=\frac{1}{2}\begin{bmatrix}i&amp;1-i\\
-i&amp;1+i\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>i</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}=\begin{bmatrix}-0.1-i&amp;0\\
0&amp;-0.1+i\end{bmatrix},\quad\mathbf{S}=\begin{bmatrix}1-i&amp;1+i\\
1&amp;1\end{bmatrix},\quad\mathbf{S}^{-1}=\frac{1}{2}\begin{bmatrix}i&amp;1-i\\
-i&amp;1+i\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We simulated this linear system starting from a random initial condition, over 1,000 time steps. We use simple Euler updates, with additive zero-mean Gaussian process noise scaled by the square root of the time step injected between time steps:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex182" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}_{t}\,\Delta t+\mathbf{x}_{t}+\sqrt{\Delta t}\,\bm{\epsilon}_{t},\quad\bm{\epsilon}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t+\Delta t}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}_{t}\,\Delta t+\mathbf{x}_{t}+\sqrt{\Delta t}\,\bm{\epsilon}_{t},\quad\bm{\epsilon}_{t}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS9.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We sampled measurements at regular intervals (we chose every 10 time steps), added zero-mean Gaussian measurement noise, and then projected the data into an embedding dimension of <math id="S3.SS9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{e}=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{e}=128</annotation></semantics></math> (an effective embedding dimension of 256 since the real/imag stacking doubles the input dimension). We trained the model on one-step prediction, using only the noisy measurements, with the model having no access to the ground-truth trajectory. After learning, we projected the model’s output back into 2D to assess its performance. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The ground-truth and measured trajectories and the model predictions with a single layer of AFA after training are shown in Fig. <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 3.9 Basic Experiments ‣ 3 Adaptive Filter Attention ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F1.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.04154v1/Images/measure_1.0_process_0.0.png" id="S3.F1.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/454;" width="476" height="454" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F1.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S3.F1.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F1.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.04154v1/Images/measure_0.5_process_0.3.png" id="S3.F1.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/453;" width="476" height="453" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F1.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S3.F1.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F1.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.04154v1/Images/measurement_2_process_0.5.png" id="S3.F1.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/457;" width="476" height="457" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F1.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S3.F1.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S3.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">Filter performance on different 2D systems: ground-truth trajectory (black), measured (blue), and predicted (red). (a) system with only measurement noise (<math id="S3.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=0.0,\,\eta^{2}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=0.0,\,\eta^{2}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>). (b) system with both process noise and measurement noise (<math id="S3.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=0.3,\,\eta^{2}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=0.3,\,\eta^{2}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>). (c) higher noise (<math id="S3.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=0.5,\,\eta^{2}=2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=0.5,\,\eta^{2}=2.0</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS9.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To check that the model has learned the right dynamics, we compute "pulled-forward" estimates at four time points. As training progresses, the "pulled-forward" estimates converge to point clouds near the ground truth, as shown in Fig. <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.9 Basic Experiments ‣ 3 Adaptive Filter Attention ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.04154v1/Images/dist0.png" id="S3.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/466;" width="476" height="466" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S3.F2.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F2.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.04154v1/Images/dist1.png" id="S3.F2.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/443;" width="476" height="443" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S3.F2.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F2.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.04154v1/Images/dist2.png" id="S3.F2.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/456;" width="476" height="456" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S3.F2.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="S3.F2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of an AFA layer’s "pulled-forward" state estimates at different stages of training. The true trajectory is shown as a solid black line, and the pulled-forward estimates as colored point clouds. (a) State estimates early in training. (b) State estimates midway through training. (c) State estimates after training is complete.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS9.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS9.p3.1" class="ltx_p">While standard attention is also able to filter this noisy trajectory, it is not able to do so effectively in a single layer, and the resulting attention matrices lack the consistent and interpretable attention matrices of AFA. We compare the attention matrices from a trained model comprised of two layers of standard attention to a trained model comprised of a single layer of AFA in Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.9 Basic Experiments ‣ 3 Adaptive Filter Attention ‣ Attention as an Adaptive Filter" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The AFA attention matrix displays a clear periodic structure, corresponding to pair-wise precisions propagated through the underlying oscillatory dynamics. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F3.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.04154v1/Images/vanilla_attn1_ex1.png" id="S3.F3.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/454;" width="476" height="454" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S3.F3.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F3.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.04154v1/Images/vanilla_attn1_ex2.png" id="S3.F3.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/454;" width="476" height="454" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S3.F3.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S3.F3.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.04154v1/Images/afa_attn_mat.png" id="S3.F3.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/476;" width="476" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S3.F3.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S3.F3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">Attention matrices produced by training standard attention and AFA on a 2D LTI with process and measurement noise. (a) First layer of standard attention (b) Second layer of standard attention. (c) Single layer of AFA.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS9.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS9.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These experiments, along with animations of the predicted trajectories, pulled-forward estimates, and attention matrices during the course of training are available at the same <a href="https://github.com/PCR-git/AFA/tree/main" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Github link</a> provided above. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S3.SS9.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Testing the model on real-world language and time series data will be the subject of future work.</span></p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Radial-Tangential Model</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We were able to significantly simplify our algorithm by assuming that the dynamics decouple into separate magnitude and angular components, and that the process and measurement noise are isotropic. Here, we will slightly relax these assumptions by assuming that the process and measurement noise also decompose into separate radial and tangential components, and derive a modification of the above algorithm.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Itô SDE with Radial–Tangential Dynamics and Noise</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the linear stochastic differential equation:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex183" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}(t)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}(t)dt+\mathbf{B}(t)d\mathbf{w}(t),\quad\mathbf{z}(t_{k})=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}(t_{k})+\mathbf{v}(t_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}(t)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}(t)dt+\mathbf{B}(t)d\mathbf{w}(t),\quad\mathbf{z}(t_{k})=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}(t_{k})+\mathbf{v}(t_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}(t)=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}(t)=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}=\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}=\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\in i\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\in i\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonal, and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}(t)=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{B}(t)\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}(t)=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{B}(t)\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}(t)=\lambda_{C}\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}(t)=\lambda_{C}\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can also write the eigenvalues as <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}=\alpha\mathbf{1}+\bm{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝝎</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}=\alpha\mathbf{1}+\bm{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\omega}=\text{diag}(\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\in i\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\omega}=\text{diag}(\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\in i\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We transform the state and measurements into the eigenbasis:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex184" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{x}(t)\in\mathbb{C}^{d},\quad\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{z}(t_{k})\in\mathbb{C}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{x}(t)\in\mathbb{C}^{d},\quad\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})=\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{z}(t_{k})\in\mathbb{C}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">And we decompose the state and measurement into radial and tangential components:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex185" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)=m_{\mathbf{s}}(t)\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t),\quad\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)=m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t)\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t)\quad\text{where:}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>where:</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)=m_{\mathbf{s}}(t)\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t),\quad\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)=m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t)\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t)\quad\text{where:}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex186" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathbf{s}}(t)=\|\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)\|_{2}=\sqrt{\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}(t)\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)}\in\mathbb{R},\quad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)=\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)/\|\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)\|_{2}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathbf{s}}(t)=\|\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)\|_{2}=\sqrt{\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}(t)\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)}\in\mathbb{R},\quad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)=\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)/\|\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)\|_{2}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex187" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t)=\|\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)\|_{2}=\sqrt{\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}(t)\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)}\in\mathbb{R},\quad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t)=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)/\|\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)\|_{2}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t)=\|\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)\|_{2}=\sqrt{\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}(t)\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)}\in\mathbb{R},\quad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t)=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)/\|\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t)\|_{2}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The dynamics in the eigenbasis are:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex188" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x_{s}}(t)=\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{x_{s}}(t)dt+\bm{\Lambda}_{B}d\mathbf{w_{s}}(t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x_{s}}(t)=\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{x_{s}}(t)dt+\bm{\Lambda}_{B}d\mathbf{w_{s}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">We assume independent process noise acting in the radial and tangential directions in the eigenbasis:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex189" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}=(\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dw_{r}+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{w}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}=(\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dw_{r}+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{w}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}):=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}):=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> projects onto the tangent space, <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{R}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}):=\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{R}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}):=\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> projects into the radial direction, and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{r},\mathbf{w}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{r},\mathbf{w}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent Wiener processes. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Hence, the process noise covariance is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex190" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t)=\bm{\Lambda}_{B}(t)\bm{\Lambda}_{B}(t)^{\dagger}=\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t)=\bm{\Lambda}_{B}(t)\bm{\Lambda}_{B}(t)^{\dagger}=\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Applying Itô’s lemma for <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathbf{s}}=\sqrt{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>s</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathbf{s}}=\sqrt{s}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex191" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dm_{\mathbf{s}}=f^{\prime}(s)\,ds+\tfrac{1}{2}f^{\prime\prime}(s)\,d\langle s\rangle=\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}\,ds-\frac{1}{8m_{\mathbf{s}}^{3}}\,d\langle s\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dm_{\mathbf{s}}=f^{\prime}(s)\,ds+\tfrac{1}{2}f^{\prime\prime}(s)\,d\langle s\rangle=\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}\,ds-\frac{1}{8m_{\mathbf{s}}^{3}}\,d\langle s\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex192" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dm_{\mathbf{s}}=\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}d(\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}})=\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}\big(d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}+\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}+d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dm_{\mathbf{s}}=\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}d(\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}})=\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}\big(d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}+\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}+d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.9" class="ltx_p">Substituting the SDE,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex193" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\Big((\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dw_{r}+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{w}_{t}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\Big((\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dw_{r}+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{w}_{t}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex194" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}(\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}m_{\mathbf{s}}\,dw_{r}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}(\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}m_{\mathbf{s}}\,dw_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.10" class="ltx_p">so:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex195" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}+d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}=2\alpha m_{\mathbf{s}}^{2}dt+2\sigma_{r}m_{\mathbf{s}}\,dw_{r}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}+d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}=2\alpha m_{\mathbf{s}}^{2}dt+2\sigma_{r}m_{\mathbf{s}}\,dw_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.11" class="ltx_p">The quadratic term is:
<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}=\sigma_{r}^{2}dt+\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{P}_{T}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}dt=\sigma_{r}^{2}dt," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}=\sigma_{r}^{2}dt+\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{P}_{T}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}dt=\sigma_{r}^{2}dt,</annotation></semantics></math>
since <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{P}_{T}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{P}_{T}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Altogether, we have:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex196" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dm_{\mathbf{s}}=\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}\big(\alpha m_{\mathbf{s}}^{2}dt+\sigma_{r}m_{\mathbf{s}}dw_{r}+\sigma_{r}^{2}dt\big)-\frac{1}{8m_{\mathbf{s}}^{3}}(2\sigma_{r}m_{\mathbf{s}})^{2}dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dm_{\mathbf{s}}=\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}\big(\alpha m_{\mathbf{s}}^{2}dt+\sigma_{r}m_{\mathbf{s}}dw_{r}+\sigma_{r}^{2}dt\big)-\frac{1}{8m_{\mathbf{s}}^{3}}(2\sigma_{r}m_{\mathbf{s}})^{2}dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex197" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\alpha m_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\,dw_{r}+\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}\sigma_{r}^{2}dt-\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}\sigma_{r}^{2}dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\alpha m_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\,dw_{r}+\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}\sigma_{r}^{2}dt-\frac{1}{2m_{\mathbf{s}}}\sigma_{r}^{2}dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.12" class="ltx_p">Hence the Itô correction cancels, and the radial SDE simplifies to:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex198" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dm_{\mathbf{s}}=\alpha m_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\,dw_{r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dm_{\mathbf{s}}=\alpha m_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\,dw_{r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.13" class="ltx_p">For the unit direction <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}/m_{\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}/m_{\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the projected Itô SDE is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex199" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}/m_{\mathbf{s}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}/m_{\mathbf{s}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.14" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> and using the fact that <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex200" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\frac{\sigma_{t}}{m_{\mathbf{s}}}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{w}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}=\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\frac{\sigma_{t}}{m_{\mathbf{s}}}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{w}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.15" class="ltx_p">Finally, we assume that measurement noise in the eigenbasis also has a radial–tangential decomposition:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex201" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})=\lambda_{C}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+v_{r}^{(k)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})=\lambda_{C}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+v_{r}^{(k)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex202" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{r}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\eta_{r}^{2}),\quad\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\eta_{t}^{2}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{r}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\eta_{r}^{2}),\quad\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\eta_{t}^{2}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.16" class="ltx_p">So, the measurement noise covariance is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex203" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{R}(t)=\eta_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)^{\dagger}+\eta_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)^{\dagger}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{R}(t)=\eta_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)^{\dagger}+\eta_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)^{\dagger}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.17" class="ltx_p">The radial measurement is obtained by projecting <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> onto the state direction <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex204" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex204X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex204X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex204X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}(t_{k})\Big(\lambda_{C}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+v_{r}^{(k)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}(t_{k})\Big(\lambda_{C}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+v_{r}^{(k)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex204Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex204Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{C}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}+v_{r}^{(k)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}+\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{C}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}+v_{r}^{(k)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}+\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex204Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex204Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{C}m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+v_{r}^{(k)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{C}m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+v_{r}^{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.18" class="ltx_p">Hence, the radial measurement is 1D Gaussian:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex205" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})\sim\mathcal{N}\big(\lambda_{C}m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}),\eta_{r}^{2}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})\sim\mathcal{N}\big(\lambda_{C}m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}),\eta_{r}^{2}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.19" class="ltx_p">The tangential (unit-direction) measurement is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex206" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}=\exp_{\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}}\!\Big(\mathbf{v}_{t}/m_{\mathbf{s}}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>exp</mi><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}=\exp_{\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}}\!\Big(\mathbf{v}_{t}/m_{\mathbf{s}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.20" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp_{\mathbf{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>𝐮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp_{\mathbf{u}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the spherical exponential map, which maps a vector in the tangent space of the sphere at <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}\in\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math> to a point on the sphere along the geodesic defined by that tangent vector <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}\in T_{\mathbf{u}}\mathbb{S}^{d-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}\in T_{\mathbf{u}}\mathbb{S}^{d-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{v}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{v}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The spherical exponential map is defined as:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex207" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp_{\mathbf{u}}:T_{\mathbf{u}}\mathbb{S}^{d-1}\to\mathbb{S}^{d-1},\quad\exp_{\mathbf{u}}(\mathbf{v})=\cos\big(\|\mathbf{v}\|\big)\,\mathbf{u}+\sin\big(\|\mathbf{v}\|\big)\,\frac{\mathbf{v}}{\|\mathbf{v}\|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>𝐮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>𝐮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>exp</mi><mi>𝐮</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>𝐯</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp_{\mathbf{u}}:T_{\mathbf{u}}\mathbb{S}^{d-1}\to\mathbb{S}^{d-1},\quad\exp_{\mathbf{u}}(\mathbf{v})=\cos\big(\|\mathbf{v}\|\big)\,\mathbf{u}+\sin\big(\|\mathbf{v}\|\big)\,\frac{\mathbf{v}}{\|\mathbf{v}\|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.21" class="ltx_p">For small tangential noise (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}\ll m_{\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}\ll m_{\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>), we can linearize on the tangent plane:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex208" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex208.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})\approx\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+\frac{1}{m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})\approx\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+\frac{1}{m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.22" class="ltx_p">(The <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/m_{\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/m_{\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> factor comes from projecting the noise onto the unit sphere (radial normalization), and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{T}\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{T}\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures the noise is tangential.) Hence, the tangential distribution is approximately Gaussian:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex209" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})\sim\mathcal{N}\Big(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}),\frac{\eta_{t}^{2}}{m_{\mathbf{s}}^{2}(t_{k})}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})\sim\mathcal{N}\Big(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}),\frac{\eta_{t}^{2}}{m_{\mathbf{s}}^{2}(t_{k})}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.23" class="ltx_p">In summary, our radial-tangential SDE (RT-SDE) model is:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex210"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex210.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dw_{r}+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{w}_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dw_{r}+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{w}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex211"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex211.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\lambda_{C}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+v_{r}^{(k)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+\frac{1}{m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\lambda_{C}\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+v_{r}^{(k)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+\frac{1}{m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex212"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{r}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{r}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex212.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\eta_{r}^{2}),\quad\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\eta_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\eta_{r}^{2}),\quad\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\eta_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.24" class="ltx_p">Or, in the decoupled radial-tangential coordinates:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex213"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex213.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle dm_{\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle dm_{\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex213.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha m_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\,dw_{r}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha m_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\sigma_{r}\,dw_{r},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex214"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex214.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex214.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\frac{\sigma_{t}}{m_{\mathbf{s}}}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{w}_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}\,dt+\frac{\sigma_{t}}{m_{\mathbf{s}}}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}})\,d\mathbf{w}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="3"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex215"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex215.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex215.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{C}\,m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+v_{r}^{(k)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{C}\,m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+v_{r}^{(k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex215.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{r}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{r}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex215.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\eta_{r}^{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\eta_{r}^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex216"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex216.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex216.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+\frac{1}{m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})+\frac{1}{m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k})}\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{k}))\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex216.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{v}_{t}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex216.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\eta_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\eta_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<br class="ltx_break">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.25" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.25.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark: Polar vs Cartesian parameterizations.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">Although the radial and angular dynamics decouple, operating in polar coordinates <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r,\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r,\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> makes the MLE nonlinear. Even if <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> evolves linearly, the radial and angular dynamics become state-dependent, and the noise covariance depends on the current state. This makes the log-likelihood non-quadratic, so the MLE cannot be expressed in closed form and requires iterative optimization. Cartesian coordinates are therefore preferred, as they preserve linear dynamics with Gaussian noise and allow exact, closed-form propagation of covariances and MLE computation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Propagation of Uncertainty through the RT-SDE</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the state evolution (for the causal case) is governed by:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex217" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex217.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{i})=e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{i}-t_{j})}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})+\int_{t_{j}}^{t_{i}}e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{i}-s)}\mathbf{B}(s)d\mathbf{w}(s)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{i})=e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{i}-t_{j})}\mathbf{x}(t_{j})+\int_{t_{j}}^{t_{i}}e^{\mathbf{A}(t_{i}-s)}\mathbf{B}(s)d\mathbf{w}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=s-t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=s-t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, this is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex218" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex218.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t_{i})=e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{j})+\int_{0}^{-\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}(t_{j}+\tau)d\mathbf{w}(\tau)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t_{i})=e^{-\mathbf{A}\Delta t_{ij}}\left(\mathbf{x}(t_{j})+\int_{0}^{-\Delta t_{ij}}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{B}(t_{j}+\tau)d\mathbf{w}(\tau)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">So the backward-propagated covariance becomes:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex219" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex219.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{B}(t_{i},t_{j})=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{Q}(t_{j}+\tau)e^{-\mathbf{A}^{\top}\tau}\,d\tau." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{B}(t_{i},t_{j})=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{Q}(t_{j}+\tau)e^{-\mathbf{A}^{\top}\tau}\,d\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Plugging in <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{S}(\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{S}(\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega})\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex220" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex220.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{B}(t_{i},t_{j})=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})\mathbf{S}^{-1},\quad\text{where:}\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha\tau}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\tau}\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t_{j}+\tau)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\tau}\,d\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where:</mtext><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{B}(t_{i},t_{j})=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})\mathbf{S}^{-1},\quad\text{where:}\quad\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha\tau}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\tau}\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t_{j}+\tau)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\tau}\,d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where the process noise is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex221" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex221.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t)=\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)^{\dagger}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t)=\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t)^{\dagger}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j}+\tau)=e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\tau}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j}+\tau)=e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\tau}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the rotation cancels inside the integral:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex222" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex222.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha\tau}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\tau}\Big(\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j}+\tau)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j}+\tau)^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j}+\tau)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j}+\tau)^{\dagger}\big)\Big)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\tau}\,d\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha\tau}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\tau}\Big(\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j}+\tau)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j}+\tau)^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j}+\tau)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j}+\tau)^{\dagger}\big)\Big)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\tau}\,d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex223" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex223.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha\tau}\Big(\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})^{\dagger}\big)\Big)\,d\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha\tau}\Big(\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})^{\dagger}\big)\Big)\,d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex224" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex224.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t_{j})\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha s}\,ds=\kappa_{B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\,\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t_{j})\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha s}\,ds=\kappa_{B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\,\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex225" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex225.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{B}(\Delta t)=\begin{cases}\dfrac{e^{-2\alpha\Delta t}-1}{-2\alpha},&amp;\alpha\neq 0,\\
\Delta t,&amp;\alpha=0.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{B}(\Delta t)=\begin{cases}\dfrac{e^{-2\alpha\Delta t}-1}{-2\alpha},&amp;\alpha\neq 0,\\
\Delta t,&amp;\alpha=0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.8" class="ltx_p">The forward-propagated covariance is then:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex226" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex226.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}F}(t_{i},t_{j})=e^{\bm{\Lambda}|\Delta t_{ij}|}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})e^{\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}|\Delta t_{ij}|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}F}(t_{i},t_{j})=e^{\bm{\Lambda}|\Delta t_{ij}|}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})e^{\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}|\Delta t_{ij}|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex227" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex227.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex228" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex228.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{\Lambda}_{Q}(t_{j})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{\Lambda}_{Q}(t_{j})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.9" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex229" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex229.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{F}(\Delta t)=e^{2\alpha\Delta t}\kappa_{B}(\Delta t)=\begin{cases}\dfrac{1-e^{2\alpha\Delta t}}{-2\alpha},&amp;\alpha\neq 0,\\
\Delta t,&amp;\alpha=0.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{F}(\Delta t)=e^{2\alpha\Delta t}\kappa_{B}(\Delta t)=\begin{cases}\dfrac{1-e^{2\alpha\Delta t}}{-2\alpha},&amp;\alpha\neq 0,\\
\Delta t,&amp;\alpha=0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.10" class="ltx_p">(Note: we prefer to keep things in terms of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{F}(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{F}(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math> rather than <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{B}(\Delta t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{B}(\Delta t)</annotation></semantics></math>, because the former is bounded for causal models, while the latter is unbounded.) 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Plugging in <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex230" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}F}(t_{i},t_{j})=\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\Big(\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})^{\dagger}\big)\Big)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}F}(t_{i},t_{j})=\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\Big(\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{j})^{\dagger}\big)\Big)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex231" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex231.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big(\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}\big)\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big(\sigma_{r}^{2}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}+\sigma_{t}^{2}\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}\big)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex232" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex232.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big(\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}+(\sigma_{r}^{2}-\sigma_{t}^{2})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big(\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}+(\sigma_{r}^{2}-\sigma_{t}^{2})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.11" class="ltx_p">Finally,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex233" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex233.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\lambda_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}F}(t_{i},t_{j})+e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}(t_{j})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\lambda_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}F}(t_{i},t_{j})+e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}(t_{j})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex234" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex234.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\lambda_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}F}(t_{i},t_{j})+e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}(t_{j})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\lambda_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}F}(t_{i},t_{j})+e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}(t_{j})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex235" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex235.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\lambda_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}F}(t_{i},t_{j})+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}(t_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\lambda_{C}^{2}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}F}(t_{i},t_{j})+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\bm{\Lambda}_{R}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.12" class="ltx_p">Altogether, the propagated measurement covariance is:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex236"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex236.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex236.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\sigma_{t}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\eta_{t}^{2}\Big)\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\sigma_{t}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\eta_{t}^{2}\Big)\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex237"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex237.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)(\sigma_{r}^{2}-\sigma_{t}^{2})+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}(\eta_{r}^{2}-\eta_{t}^{2})\Big)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)(\sigma_{r}^{2}-\sigma_{t}^{2})+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}(\eta_{r}^{2}-\eta_{t}^{2})\Big)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex238" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex238.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{I}+\Big(\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)-\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{I}+\Big(\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)-\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.13" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex239" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex239X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex239X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex239X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{C}^{2}\,\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\,\sigma_{r}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\,\eta_{r}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{C}^{2}\,\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\,\sigma_{r}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\,\eta_{r}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex239Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex239Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex239Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{C}^{2}\,\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\,\sigma_{t}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\,\eta_{t}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{C}^{2}\,\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\,\sigma_{t}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\,\eta_{t}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.14" class="ltx_p">Rearranging, this is:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex240"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex240.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger})+\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger})+\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.15" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{r}=\sigma_{t}:=\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{r}=\sigma_{t}:=\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{r}=\eta_{t}:=\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{r}=\eta_{t}:=\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, then this simplifies to:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex241" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex241.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\sigma^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\eta^{2}\Big)\mathbf{I}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\sigma^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\eta^{2}\Big)\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.16" class="ltx_p">which was exactly the result for the case of isotropic noise. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Since the propagated covariance is of the form <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=a\mathbf{I}+b\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=a\mathbf{I}+b\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\sigma_{Vt}^{2},\,b=\sigma_{Vr}^{2}-\sigma_{Vt}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\sigma_{Vt}^{2},\,b=\sigma_{Vr}^{2}-\sigma_{Vt}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. a rank-1 correction of identity, we can invert it with the Sherman-Morrison formula:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex242" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex242.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}=\big(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}\big)^{-1}=\frac{1}{a}\Big(\mathbf{I}+\frac{b}{a}\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}\Big)^{-1}=\frac{1}{a}\Big(\mathbf{I}-\frac{b}{a}\frac{\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}}{1+\frac{b}{a}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{u_{s}}}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}=\big(\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}\big)^{-1}=\frac{1}{a}\Big(\mathbf{I}+\frac{b}{a}\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}\Big)^{-1}=\frac{1}{a}\Big(\mathbf{I}-\frac{b}{a}\frac{\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}}{1+\frac{b}{a}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{u_{s}}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex243" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex243.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\frac{1}{a}\Big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}\Big)+\Big(-\frac{b}{a(a+b)}+\frac{1}{a}\Big)\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\frac{1}{a}\Big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}\Big)+\Big(-\frac{b}{a(a+b)}+\frac{1}{a}\Big)\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex244" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex244.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\frac{1}{a}\Big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}\Big)+\Big(\frac{1}{a+b}\Big)\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\frac{1}{a}\Big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}\Big)+\Big(\frac{1}{a+b}\Big)\mathbf{u_{s}}\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.17" class="ltx_p">Hence:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex245" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\frac{1}{\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)}\Big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}(t_{i})\Big)+\frac{1}{\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}(t_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>†</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{P}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\frac{1}{\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)}\Big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}(t_{i})\Big)+\frac{1}{\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)}\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}^{\dagger}(t_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.18" class="ltx_p">(which we could also have obtained by just inverting each term, since they are along orthogonal subspaces).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Radial–Tangential Kalman IRLS</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now seek to estimate the latent states <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{z}_{i}^{C}\}_{i=1}^{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{z}_{i}^{C}\}_{i=1}^{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> from the observations <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{z}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{z}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, assuming the latent states were generated by an RT-SDE. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The joint log-likelihood of the measurements factors into radial and tangential parts:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex246" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p\big(\{\mathbf{z}_{s}(t_{j})\}\mid m_{s}(\cdot),\mathbf{u}_{s}(\cdot)\big)=\sum_{j}\log p\!\left(m_{\mathbf{z}s}(t_{j})\mid m_{s}(t_{j})\right)\,+\,\sum_{j}\log p\!\left(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{z}s}(t_{j})\mid\mathbf{u}_{s}(t_{j}),m_{s}(t_{j})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.333em;" width="0.333em"><mi>p</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.333em;" width="0.333em"><mi>p</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p\big(\{\mathbf{z}_{s}(t_{j})\}\mid m_{s}(\cdot),\mathbf{u}_{s}(\cdot)\big)=\sum_{j}\log p\!\left(m_{\mathbf{z}s}(t_{j})\mid m_{s}(t_{j})\right)\,+\,\sum_{j}\log p\!\left(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{z}s}(t_{j})\mid\mathbf{u}_{s}(t_{j}),m_{s}(t_{j})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex247" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{where:}\quad m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\big(\lambda_{C}m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{j}),\eta_{r}^{2}\big),\quad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\Big(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{j}),\frac{\eta_{t}^{2}}{m_{\mathbf{s}}^{2}(t_{j})}\,\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{j}))\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>where:</mtext><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{where:}\quad m_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\big(\lambda_{C}m_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{j}),\eta_{r}^{2}\big),\quad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}}(t_{j})\sim\mathcal{N}\Big(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{j}),\frac{\eta_{t}^{2}}{m_{\mathbf{s}}^{2}(t_{j})}\,\mathbf{P}_{T}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{j}))\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, we can treat the estimation problem as two decoupled weighted least squares problems: one for magnitude and one for direction. This motivates the following iteration: 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Let <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}:=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}:=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. The initial condition is: <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(0)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(0)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">At iteration <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute the magnitudes and directions:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex248" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex248.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}=\|\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\|_{2},\quad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}/\|\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}=\|\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\|_{2},\quad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}/\|\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">And the estimates:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex249" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex249.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}=e^{-\bm{\lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{z_{s}}_{j}^{(k)}=\Big(e^{-\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}m_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}\Big)\Big(e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}=e^{-\bm{\lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{z_{s}}_{j}^{(k)}=\Big(e^{-\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}m_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}\Big)\Big(e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We showed above that:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex250" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex250.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}\Big(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{C},\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}\Big(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{C},\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex251" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex251.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}\big)+\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger},\\[5.69054pt]
\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=\lambda_{C}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\sigma_{r}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\eta_{r}^{2},\\[2.84526pt]
\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=\lambda_{C}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\sigma_{t}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\eta_{t}^{2}.\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\big(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}\big)+\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger},\\[5.69054pt]
\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=\lambda_{C}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\sigma_{r}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\eta_{r}^{2},\\[2.84526pt]
\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)=\lambda_{C}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\sigma_{t}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\eta_{t}^{2}.\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">It follows that:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex252" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex252.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}\left((\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{C},\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\right),\quad\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{C},\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}\left((\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{C},\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\right),\quad\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}\sim\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{C},\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">We do not have access to the true tangent projection matrix at <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{s}i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{s}i}:=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{s}i}:=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>, but we can approximate it using the tangent projection matrix at <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}/\lambda_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}/\lambda_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex253" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex253.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\Big(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}/\lambda_{C}\Big):=\mathbf{I}-\frac{\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big)^{\dagger}/\lambda_{C}^{2}}{\Big(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big)^{\dagger}\Big(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big)/\lambda_{C}^{2}}=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\Big(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}/\lambda_{C}\Big):=\mathbf{I}-\frac{\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big)^{\dagger}/\lambda_{C}^{2}}{\Big(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big)^{\dagger}\Big(\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\Big)/\lambda_{C}^{2}}=\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Define separate radial and tangential estimates:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex254" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex254.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{m}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}:=(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)},\qquad\mathbf{\hat{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}:=\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{m}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}:=(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)},\qquad\mathbf{\hat{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}:=\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.9" class="ltx_p">We assume:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex255" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex255.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{m}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}\overset{\text{approx}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}\left((\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{C},\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\right),\quad\mathbf{\hat{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}\overset{\text{approx}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{C},\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">approx</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">approx</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>C</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{m}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}\overset{\text{approx}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}\left((\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{C},\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\right),\quad\mathbf{\hat{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}\overset{\text{approx}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{C},\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.10" class="ltx_p">And define corresponding radial and tangential residuals:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex256" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex256.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)},\quad\ell_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}:=(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{r}_{\mathbf{zs}ij},\quad\mathbf{d}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}:=\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\mathbf{r}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}-\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)},\quad\ell_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}:=(\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{r}_{\mathbf{zs}ij},\quad\mathbf{d}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}:=\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\mathbf{r}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.11" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex257" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}\overset{\text{approx}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}\left(0,\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\right),\quad\mathbf{d}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}\overset{\text{approx}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{0},\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">approx</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mtext mathsize="0.700em">approx</mtext></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}\overset{\text{approx}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}\left(0,\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\right),\quad\mathbf{d}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}\overset{\text{approx}}{\sim}\mathcal{N}\left(\mathbf{0},\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.12" class="ltx_p">Defining robust weights:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex258" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{r,ij}^{(k)}=\frac{1}{1+(\ell_{ij}^{(k)})^{2}/(\nu_{r}\sigma_{Vr,ij}^{2})},\quad w_{t,ij}^{(k)}=\frac{1}{1+(\mathbf{d}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{d}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}/(\nu_{t}\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{r,ij}^{(k)}=\frac{1}{1+(\ell_{ij}^{(k)})^{2}/(\nu_{r}\sigma_{Vr,ij}^{2})},\quad w_{t,ij}^{(k)}=\frac{1}{1+(\mathbf{d}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)})^{\dagger}\mathbf{d}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}/(\nu_{t}\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.13" class="ltx_p">the IRLS update for the magnitude is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex259" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{m}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}:=\frac{\sum_{j\leq i}\big(w_{r,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vr,ij}^{2}\big)\hat{m}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}}{\sum_{j\leq i}\big(w_{r,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vr,ij}^{2}\big)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{m}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}:=\frac{\sum_{j\leq i}\big(w_{r,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vr,ij}^{2}\big)\hat{m}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}}{\sum_{j\leq i}\big(w_{r,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vr,ij}^{2}\big)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.14" class="ltx_p">And we can update the magnitude with the MLE:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex260" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\bar{m}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\bar{m}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.15" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}_{Tij}^{+(k)}=\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}_{Tij}^{+(k)}=\mathbf{P}_{T\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute a tangent-space precision-weighted average:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex261" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex261.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{i}^{(k)}:=\left(\sum_{j\leq i}w_{t,ij}^{(k)}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{Tij}^{+(k)}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j\leq i}w_{t,ij}^{(k)}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{Tij}^{+(k)}\mathbf{\hat{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{i}^{(k)}:=\left(\sum_{j\leq i}w_{t,ij}^{(k)}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{Tij}^{+(k)}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j\leq i}w_{t,ij}^{(k)}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{Tij}^{+(k)}\mathbf{\hat{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S4.Ex262" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex262.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\left(\sum_{j\leq i}w_{t,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j\leq i}\big(w_{t,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2}\big)\mathbf{\hat{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\left(\sum_{j\leq i}w_{t,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j\leq i}\big(w_{t,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2}\big)\mathbf{\hat{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.16" class="ltx_p">We can then update the full state estimate with a simple first-order update:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex263" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex263.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k+1)}=m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}+\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k+1)}=m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}+\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.17" class="ltx_p">We can do better using the (spherical) exponential map. Let:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex264" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex264.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}^{(k)}:=\big\|\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\big\|,\qquad\mathbf{a}_{i}^{(k)}:=\frac{\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}}{\|\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}^{(k)}:=\big\|\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\big\|,\qquad\mathbf{a}_{i}^{(k)}:=\frac{\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}}{\|\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.18" class="ltx_p">The exact geodesic step is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex265" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex265.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\begin{cases}\cos\theta_{i}^{(k)}\,\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}+\sin\theta_{i}^{(k)}\,\mathbf{a}_{i}^{(k)},&amp;\text{if }\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\neq 0,\\
\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)},&amp;\text{if }\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}=0.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\begin{cases}\cos\theta_{i}^{(k)}\,\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}+\sin\theta_{i}^{(k)}\,\mathbf{a}_{i}^{(k)},&amp;\text{if }\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\neq 0,\\
\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)},&amp;\text{if }\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}=0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.19" class="ltx_p">A first-order approximation is:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex266" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex266.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}+\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}/m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)},\qquad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\frac{\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}}{\|\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}+\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}/m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)},\qquad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\frac{\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}}{\|\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.20" class="ltx_p">Or, equivalently:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex267" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex267.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}+\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)},\qquad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\frac{\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}}{\|\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}+\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)},\qquad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\frac{\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}}{\|\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.21" class="ltx_p">Having updated the magnitude and direction, set:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex268" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex268.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k+1)}=m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\,\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k+1)}=m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\,\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.22" class="ltx_p">Or we can use a conservative update:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex269" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex269.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k+1)}=\gamma\,\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}+(1-\gamma)\,m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k+1)}=\gamma\,\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}+(1-\gamma)\,m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Implementation</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present a vectorized implementation of the RT–Kalman IRLS update. The algorithm combines scalar precision-weighted updates for radial components with a separate precision-weighted update followed by a geodesic step for tangential components.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm3" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span>RT Adaptive Filter Attention</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm3.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input sequence:</span> <math id="algorithm3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Complex linear layers:</span> <math id="algorithm3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{Q},\mathcal{L}_{K},\mathcal{L}_{V},\mathcal{L}_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{Q},\mathcal{L}_{K},\mathcal{L}_{V},\mathcal{L}_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameters:</span> Dynamics and noise <math id="algorithm3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha,\bm{\omega},\sigma_{r},\sigma_{t},\eta_{r},\eta_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝎</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha,\bm{\omega},\sigma_{r},\sigma_{t},\eta_{r},\eta_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>; temperatures <math id="algorithm3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tau_{r},\tau_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{r},\tau_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>; timestep <math id="algorithm3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>; residual weight <math id="algorithm3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="algorithm3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}=\Delta t\cdot i;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}=\Delta t\cdot i;</annotation></semantics></math>  <math id="algorithm3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,t_{j}=\Delta t\cdot j." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,t_{j}=\Delta t\cdot j.</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Constants:</span> stability <math id="algorithm3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, causal mask <math id="algorithm3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>causal</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="algorithm3.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Complex-valued projections:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.5" class="ltx_listingline">Lift inputs to complex form: <math id="algorithm3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}=[\mathbf{Z}_{r},0]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}=[\mathbf{Z}_{r},0]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{V}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{V}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z}))</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{q}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{q}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{Q}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{q}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{q}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{Q}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}))</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{k}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{k}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{K}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{k}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{k}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{K}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{v}}))</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exponential kernels:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[\tau]=\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&gt;0\}}\odot e^{-\alpha^{2}\Delta t\tau}+\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau\leq 0\}},\quad\mathcal{K}_{\bm{\omega}}[\tau]=\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&gt;0\}}\odot e^{\bm{\omega}\Delta t\tau}+\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau\leq 0\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝝎</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝝎</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}[\tau]=\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&gt;0\}}\odot e^{-\alpha^{2}\Delta t\tau}+\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau\leq 0\}},\quad\mathcal{K}_{\bm{\omega}}[\tau]=\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau&gt;0\}}\odot e^{\bm{\omega}\Delta t\tau}+\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau\leq 0\}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decay kernel:</span>
<math id="algorithm3.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\kappa[\tau]=\frac{1-\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}^{2}[\tau]+\epsilon}{2\alpha^{2}+\epsilon}\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}&gt;\epsilon\}}+\tau\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}\leq\epsilon\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa[\tau]=\frac{1-\mathcal{K}_{\alpha}^{2}[\tau]+\epsilon}{2\alpha^{2}+\epsilon}\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}&gt;\epsilon\}}+\tau\mathbf{1}_{\{\alpha^{2}\leq\epsilon\}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Covariance kernels:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{C}_{r}[i,j]=\kappa(|i-j|)\sigma_{r}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha^{2}\Delta t|i-j|}\eta_{r}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{C}_{r}[i,j]=\kappa(|i-j|)\sigma_{r}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha^{2}\Delta t|i-j|}\eta_{r}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{C}_{t}[i,j]=\kappa(|i-j|)\sigma_{t}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha^{2}\Delta t|i-j|}\eta_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{C}_{t}[i,j]=\kappa(|i-j|)\sigma_{t}^{2}+e^{-2\alpha^{2}\Delta t|i-j|}\eta_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Precompute kernels:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}[i,j]=e^{-\alpha^{2}(t_{i}-t_{j})},\quad\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{v}}[i,j]=e^{-\alpha^{2}(t_{i}-t_{j})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}[i,j]=e^{-\alpha^{2}(t_{i}-t_{j})},\quad\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{v}}[i,j]=e^{-\alpha^{2}(t_{i}-t_{j})},</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}[k,j]=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{j}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}[k,j]=e^{i\omega_{k}t_{j}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}[k,j]=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{j}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{+}[k,j]=e^{i\omega_{k}t_{j}},</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.18" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-}[k,j]=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{j}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}[k,j]=e^{i\omega_{k}t_{j}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{-}[k,j]=e^{-i\omega_{k}t_{j}},\quad\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}[k,j]=e^{i\omega_{k}t_{j}},</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.19" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{q}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{q}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{-}\odot\mathbf{Z_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.20" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compute normalized value directions:</span>
<math id="algorithm3.m23" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]=\mathbf{Z_{v}}[:,i]\big/\left(\|\mathbf{Z_{v}}[:,i]\|+\epsilon\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]=\mathbf{Z_{v}}[:,i]\big/\left(\|\mathbf{Z_{v}}[:,i]\|+\epsilon\right)</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.21" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Radial and tangential decompositions:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.22" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m24" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{q}}=\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{k}}=\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{v}}=\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{q}}=\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{k}}=\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{v}}=\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.23" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{q}}=\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}-\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{q}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{k}}=\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}-\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{k}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{v}}=\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{v}}-\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{q}}=\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{q}}-\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{q}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{k}}=\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{k}}-\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{k}},\quad\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{v}}=\mathbf{\tilde{Z}_{v}}-\mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{v}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.24" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.24.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compute residuals:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.25" class="ltx_listingline">Tangential:
<math id="algorithm3.m26" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{\text{tan}}^{2}=\|\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{q}}\|_{2}^{2}\mathbf{1}_{m}^{\top}+\mathbf{1}_{m}\|\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{k}}\|_{2}^{2}{}^{\top}-2\mathrm{Re}(\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}\odot\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{k}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mtext>tan</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mn>2</mn><mi>Re</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{\text{tan}}^{2}=\|\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{q}}\|_{2}^{2}\mathbf{1}_{m}^{\top}+\mathbf{1}_{m}\|\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{k}}\|_{2}^{2}{}^{\top}-2\mathrm{Re}(\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}\odot\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger}\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{k}})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.26" class="ltx_listingline">Radial:
<math id="algorithm3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}_{\text{rad}}^{2}=(\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{q}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger})\mathbf{1}_{m}^{\top}+\mathbf{1}_{m}(\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{k}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{k}}^{\dagger})^{\top}-2\mathrm{Re}(\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}\odot\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{q}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{k}}^{\dagger})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mtext>rad</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}_{\text{rad}}^{2}=(\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{q}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{q}}^{\dagger})\mathbf{1}_{m}^{\top}+\mathbf{1}_{m}(\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{k}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{k}}^{\dagger})^{\top}-2\mathrm{Re}(\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{qk}}\odot\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{q}}\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{k}}^{\dagger})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.27" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.27.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dynamic precision kernels:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.28" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\text{rad}}[i,j]=1/\sigma_{V_{r}}^{2}(|t_{i}-t_{j}|),\quad\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\text{tan}}[i,j]=1/\sigma_{V_{t}}^{2}(|t_{i}-t_{j}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mtext>rad</mtext><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mtext>tan</mtext><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\text{rad}}[i,j]=1/\sigma_{V_{r}}^{2}(|t_{i}-t_{j}|),\quad\mathbf{P}^{C}_{\text{tan}}[i,j]=1/\sigma_{V_{t}}^{2}(|t_{i}-t_{j}|)</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.29" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.29.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robust weights and attention:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.30" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{A}}_{\text{rad}}[i,j]=-\log(\mathbf{V}^C_\text{rad}[i,j] + \mathbf{R}_\text{rad}^2[i,j] + \epsilon)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>rad</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mtext>rad</mtext><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mtext>rad</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{A}}_{\text{rad}}[i,j]=-\log(\mathbf{V}^C_\text{rad}[i,j] + \mathbf{R}_\text{rad}^2[i,j] + \epsilon),</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.31" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{A}}_{\text{tan}}[i,j]=-\log(\mathbf{V}^C_\text{tan}[i,j] + \mathbf{R}_\text{tan}^2[i,j] + \epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>tan</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐕</mi><mtext>tan</mtext><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mtext>tan</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{A}}_{\text{tan}}[i,j]=-\log(\mathbf{V}^C_\text{tan}[i,j] + \mathbf{R}_\text{tan}^2[i,j] + \epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.32" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{\text{rad}}=\operatorname{softmax}\Big(\tau_{r}\,\mathbf{\tilde{A}}_{\text{rad}}\odot\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}},\;\text{dim}=1\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mtext>rad</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>rad</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>causal</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>dim</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{\text{rad}}=\operatorname{softmax}\Big(\tau_{r}\,\mathbf{\tilde{A}}_{\text{rad}}\odot\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}},\;\text{dim}=1\Big),</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.33" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{\text{tan}}=\operatorname{softmax}\Big(\tau_{t}\,\mathbf{\tilde{A}}_{\text{tan}}\odot\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}},\;\text{dim}=1\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mtext>tan</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>tan</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>causal</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>dim</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{\text{tan}}=\operatorname{softmax}\Big(\tau_{t}\,\mathbf{\tilde{A}}_{\text{tan}}\odot\mathbf{M}_{\text{causal}},\;\text{dim}=1\Big)</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.34" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.34.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Apply value decay and compute outputs:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.35" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{A}}_{\text{rad}}=\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{v}}\odot\mathbf{A}_{\text{rad}},\quad\mathbf{\hat{A}}_{\text{tan}}=\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{v}}\odot\mathbf{A}_{\text{tan}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>rad</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mtext>rad</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>tan</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mtext>tan</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{A}}_{\text{rad}}=\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{v}}\odot\mathbf{A}_{\text{rad}},\quad\mathbf{\hat{A}}_{\text{tan}}=\mathbf{E}_{\mathbf{v}}\odot\mathbf{A}_{\text{tan}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.36" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{m}}_{\mathbf{v}}=\mathbf{\hat{A}}_{\text{rad}}\,\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{v}},\quad\mathbf{\bar{V}}_{\mathbf{v}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}\odot(\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{v}}\,(\mathbf{\hat{A}}_{\text{tan}})^{\dagger})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>rad</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext>tan</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{m}}_{\mathbf{v}}=\mathbf{\hat{A}}_{\text{rad}}\,\mathbf{\tilde{m}}_{\mathbf{v}},\quad\mathbf{\bar{V}}_{\mathbf{v}}=\bm{\tilde{\Phi}}_{\mathbf{v}}^{+}\odot(\mathbf{\tilde{V}}_{\mathbf{v}}\,(\mathbf{\hat{A}}_{\text{tan}})^{\dagger})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.37" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.37.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Geodesic step:</span>
<math id="algorithm3.m35" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{U}}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]=\left(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]+\mathbf{\bar{V}}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]\right)\Big/\left(\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]+\mathbf{\bar{V}}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]\|+\epsilon\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{U}}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]=\left(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]+\mathbf{\bar{V}}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]\right)\Big/\left(\|\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]+\mathbf{\bar{V}}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]\|+\epsilon\right)</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.38" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.38.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reconstruct output:</span>
<math id="algorithm3.m36" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]=\mathbf{\bar{m}}_{\mathbf{v}}[i]\cdot\mathbf{\bar{U}}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]=\mathbf{\bar{m}}_{\mathbf{v}}[i]\cdot\mathbf{\bar{U}}_{\mathbf{v}}[:,i]</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.39" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.39.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Residual connection and prediction:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.40" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m37" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}\leftarrow(1-\text{sigmoid}(\delta))\mathbf{Z_{v}}+\text{sigmoid}(\delta)\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}},\quad\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}=\mathbf{E_{v}}[:,1]\odot\mathbf{\bar{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mi>𝐯</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}}\leftarrow(1-\text{sigmoid}(\delta))\mathbf{Z_{v}}+\text{sigmoid}(\delta)\mathbf{\bar{Z}_{v}},\quad\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}=\mathbf{E_{v}}[:,1]\odot\mathbf{\bar{Z}}_{\mathbf{v}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.41" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.41.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output projection:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.42" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm3.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{p}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{P}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{p}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})\big)\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{P}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z}_{\mathbf{v}}^{\text{pred}}))</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.4.43" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.4.43.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return:</span> <math id="algorithm3.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐩</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{p}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5 </span>Interpreting the Transformer as an MLE on a Hypersphere</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm above faithfully implements RT-MLE with geometric constraints, but is somewhat intricate. We propose the following simplifications for clarity and practical use. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Recall that, in RT-Kalman IRLS our estimated state decomposes as:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex270" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex270.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}=e^{-\bm{\lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{z_{s}}_{j}^{(k)}=\Big(e^{-\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}m_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}\Big)\Big(e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝝀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}=e^{-\bm{\lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{z_{s}}_{j}^{(k)}=\Big(e^{-\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}m_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}\Big)\Big(e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{u}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}/\|\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}\|=e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{u}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}=\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}/\|\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{\mathbf{s}ij}^{(k)}\|=e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming that the transformed magnitude is approximately constant across time steps <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}m_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}\approx m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}m_{\mathbf{zs}j}^{(k)}\approx m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives a simple precision-weighted average of <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{u}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{u}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex271" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex271.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\approx m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\mathbf{\bar{u}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)},\quad\text{where:}\quad\mathbf{\bar{u}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\approx\left(\sum_{j\leq i}w_{t,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j\leq i}\big(w_{t,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2}\big)\mathbf{\hat{u}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≈</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where:</mtext><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≈</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{v}}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k)}\approx m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\mathbf{\bar{u}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)},\quad\text{where:}\quad\mathbf{\bar{u}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\approx\left(\sum_{j\leq i}w_{t,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2}\right)^{-1}\sum_{j\leq i}\big(w_{t,ij}^{(k)}/\sigma_{Vt,ij}^{2}\big)\mathbf{\hat{u}}_{\mathbf{zs}ij}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For small angles, the attention update is largely aligned with the tangent space and any component along <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is partially corrected by the subsequent geodesic normalization, so we omit the explicit tangent projection for simplicity. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The geodesic update step becomes:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex272" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex272.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\approx\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}+\mathbf{\bar{u}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)},\qquad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\frac{\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}}{\|\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\approx\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}+\mathbf{\bar{u}}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)},\qquad\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}=\frac{\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}}{\|\mathbf{y}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k)}\|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">And the output is again:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex273" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex273.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k+1)}=m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\,\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐳𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{(k+1)}=m_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}\,\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{zs}i}^{(k+1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.5" class="ltx_p">This structure — Norm, Attention, Add &amp; Norm — closely resembles a Transformer. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">This suggests that the Transformer’s effectiveness may stem, at least in part, from its ability to approximate a principled filtering mechanism, with attention functioning as a generalized MLE for an SDE with unitary (or norm-preserving) linear dynamics, and normalization layers realizing approximate geodesic steps along the hypersphere. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We present the following Transformer-inspired simplification of RT-AFA:</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm4" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span>AFA Transformer</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm4.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm4.4.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm4.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Input sequence <math id="algorithm4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{r}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameters:</span> AFA layer <math id="algorithm4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AFA}_{\mathrm{dir}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AFA</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AFA}_{\mathrm{dir}}</annotation></semantics></math>, scalar AFA layer <math id="algorithm4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AFA}_{\mathrm{mag}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>AFA</mi><mi>mag</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AFA}_{\mathrm{mag}}</annotation></semantics></math>, output complex linear layer <math id="algorithm4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, real-valued FFN layers: <math id="algorithm4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FFN}=\mathcal{L}_{2}\circ\mathrm{ReLU}\circ\mathcal{L}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>FFN</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ReLU</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FFN}=\mathcal{L}_{2}\circ\mathrm{ReLU}\circ\mathcal{L}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, stability const. <math id="algorithm4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Magnitude and unit direction:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}=\|\mathbf{Z}_{r}\|_{\text{rowwise}}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mtext>rowwise</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}=\|\mathbf{Z}_{r}\|_{\text{rowwise}}\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times m}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}_{r}=\gamma_{1}\mathbf{Z}_{r}\big/(\mathbf{m}+\epsilon)+\beta_{1}\quad(\text{element-wise division})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>element-wise division</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}_{r}=\gamma_{1}\mathbf{Z}_{r}\big/(\mathbf{m}+\epsilon)+\beta_{1}\quad(\text{element-wise division})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lift to complex:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}=[\mathbf{U}_{r};\mathbf{0}]\in\mathbb{C}^{2\times d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}=[\mathbf{U}_{r};\mathbf{0}]\in\mathbb{C}^{2\times d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Apply AFA attention:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{m}}=\mathrm{AFA}_{\mathrm{mag}}(\mathbf{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>AFA</mi><mi>mag</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{m}}=\mathrm{AFA}_{\mathrm{mag}}(\mathbf{m})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{U}}=\mathrm{AFA}_{\mathrm{dir}}(\mathbf{U})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>AFA</mi><mi>dir</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{U}}=\mathrm{AFA}_{\mathrm{dir}}(\mathbf{U})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Geodesic step:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{U}+\mathbf{\hat{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{U}+\mathbf{\hat{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}_{y}=\|\mathbf{Y}\|_{\text{row-wise}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mtext>row-wise</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}_{y}=\|\mathbf{Y}\|_{\text{row-wise}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{U}}=\gamma_{2}\mathbf{Y}\big/(\mathbf{m}_{y}+\epsilon)+\beta_{2}\quad(\text{element-wise division})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐘</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐦</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>element-wise division</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{U}}=\gamma_{2}\mathbf{Y}\big/(\mathbf{m}_{y}+\epsilon)+\beta_{2}\quad(\text{element-wise division})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Combine magnitude and direction estimates:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}=\mathbf{\hat{m}}\odot\mathbf{\tilde{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}=\mathbf{\hat{m}}\odot\mathbf{\tilde{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output complex linear projection:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.18" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{o}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{o}}))\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{O}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐨</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐨</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{o}}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z_{o}}))\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{O}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z}),\operatorname{Im}(\mathbf{Z}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.19" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output FFN with nonlinearity and residual connection:</span> 
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.20" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}^{\mathrm{out}}=\mathbf{Z}_{r}+\mathrm{FFN}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{o}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>FFN</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐨</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}^{\mathrm{out}}=\mathbf{Z}_{r}+\mathrm{FFN}(\operatorname{Re}(\mathbf{Z_{o}}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.21" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.4.21.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm4.4.21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Updated sequence <math id="algorithm4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}^{\mathrm{out}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>out</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}^{\mathrm{out}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.4.22" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Related Work</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Classical Filtering Methods</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Norbert Wiener’s 1949 work on the Wiener Filter established the theoretical framework for minimum mean-square error estimation of signals from noisy observations, using second-order statistics (covariances) of the signal and noise <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib98" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wiener, 1964</a>)</cite>. Kalman introduced the discrete-time Kalman Filter, a recursive algorithm that optimally estimates the states of linear time-invariant stochastic systems from noisy measurements, achieving minimum mean-square estimation error <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kalman, 1960</a>)</cite>. Kalman &amp; Bucy extended the approach to continuous-time systems with Gaussian noise <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kalman and Bucy, 1961</a>)</cite>. Rauch, Tung, and Striebel generalized the Kalman Filter to a batch smoothing framework, providing a maximum-likelihood estimator for the entire trajectory of a linear dynamical system by combining all measurements simultaneously, rather than recursively, which yields smoothed state estimates with minimum mean-square error over the full time horizon <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib71" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rauch et al., 1965</a>)</cite>. Extensions to nonlinear systems can be handled by the Extended Kalman Filter (EKF), which linearizes the dynamics and measurement functions about the current state estimate <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anderson and Moore, 1979</a>)</cite>. For introductions to stochastic processes and adaptive filtering, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jazwinski, 1970</a>; <a href="#bib.bib86" title="" class="ltx_ref">Speyer, 2008</a>; <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haykin, 2002</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Robust and Adaptive Filtering</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In many practical settings, the system and noise parameters required by the Kalman Filter are unknown or time-varying. Early work in adaptive signal processing began with Widrow &amp; Hoff, who introduced the Least Mean Squares (LMS) algorithm, laying the foundation for recursive adaptation using the innovation signal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib97" title="" class="ltx_ref">Widrow and Hoff, 1960</a>)</cite>. Schweppe provided early maximum likelihood foundations for estimating noise covariances in Gaussian signals, which became a cornerstone for statistically principled adaptive filtering <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schweppe, 1965</a>)</cite>. Mehra formalized adaptive Kalman Filtering by estimating unknown process and measurement noise covariances from the innovations sequence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mehra, 1970</a>)</cite>, and compared innovation-based versus residual-based adaptation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mehra, 1972</a>)</cite>. Iteratively reweighted least squares (IRLS) provides a framework for robust estimation by repeatedly solving weighted least-squares problems, with weights updated based on residuals; this approach was formalized in signal processing contexts by Burrus, Barreto, and Selesnick for FIR filter design <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Burrus et al., 1994</a>)</cite>. Comprehensive treatments of stochastic estimation and adaptive methods include <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jazwinski, 1970</a>)</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Maybeck and Siouris, 1980</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Neural Networks for Filtering Dynamical Systems</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Kalman Filtering and Neural Networks</span>, edited by Haykin, provides a comprehensive treatment of combining classical state estimation with neural network models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haykin, 2001</a>)</cite>. Other work demonstrated that multilayer and recurrent neural networks can be effectively used for the identification and adaptive control of nonlinear dynamical systems, for example Narendra and Parthasarathy
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Narendra and Parthasarathy, 1990</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Krishnan et al. introduced Deep Kalman Filters (DKFs), which extend classical linear Kalman Filters to high-dimensional, non-linear latent dynamics using deep neural networks. DKFs maintain a probabilistic latent state and propagate uncertainty explicitly. In this framework, the latent state is updated sequentially according to a learned, potentially nonlinear transition function, and observations are generated from the latent state through a neural network
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Krishnan et al., 2015</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Liu et al. propose Kalman Filtering Attention (KFAtt) for CTR prediction, treating each user click as a noisy measurement of a hidden query-specific interest and computing a closed-form MAP estimate that combines these measurements with a global prior. Despite the “Kalman” terminology, KFAtt does not model temporal dynamics or state evolution, and effectively performs a static, precision-weighted aggregation of observations. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Goel and Bartlett investigate whether Transformers can represent classical Kalman Filters for linear time-invariant (LTI) systems. Their Transformer Filter uses softmax self-attention over nonlinear embeddings of past state estimates and observations. It effectively approximates the Kalman update indirectly, with the kernel weights mimicking the Kalman gain, and requires careful tuning of a temperature parameter to control approximation error <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Goel and Bartlett, 2024</a>)</cite>. While this approach can produce state estimates arbitrarily close to the true Kalman Filter and approximate the behavior of an LQG controller, it does not naturally generalize to robust, time-varying, or non-Gaussian settings, nor does it explicitly propagate uncertainty in a structured way. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Several recent works integrate neural networks or attention into Kalman Filtering. KalmanNet uses a recurrent network to learn the Kalman gain for real-time filtering under partially known or nonlinear dynamics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Revach et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. The Neural Extended Kalman Filter parameterizes both process and observation models with neural networks for end-to-end latent state inference <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. The Attention Kalman Filter (AtKF) replaces the traditional Kalman gain with a self-attention network that learns to capture dependencies across past state and innovation sequences <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib94" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. A-KIT (2024) learns process noise covariance online to improve EKF predictions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cohen and Klein, 2024</a>)</cite>. KalmanFormer integrates a Transformer network into the Kalman Filter framework to directly learn the Kalman gain from data. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib81" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shen et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The present work is an extension of the MS Thesis, "Adaptive Filter Attention," which shows that a tensorized attention formulation exactly solves the MLE for a diagonalizable LTI system with Gaussian noise <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Racioppo, 2025</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Uncertainty Propagation Networks (UPNs) extend neural ODEs to jointly model state means and covariances through coupled differential equations, allowing continuous-time propagation of uncertainty sequence modeling. UPN propagates uncertainty continuously through time by explicitly evolving the covariance of the state alongside the state mean, essentially functioning as a continuous-time Kalman Filter embedded in a learned dynamics model
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jahanshahi and Zhu, 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Neural State Space Models</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">State space models (SSMs) are a powerful framework for modeling sequences and time series data by representing system dynamics through latent states that evolve over time. A key challenge in sequence modeling is maintaining memory over long time horizons, and avoiding the vanishing and exploding gradient problem faced by recurrent neural networks. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The HiPPO framework improves memory retention in SSMs by introducing recurrent memory with optimal polynomial projections, which allows the model to compress and retain important information from the entire history in a structured latent state space <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2020</a>)</cite>. The Structured State Space Sequence model (S4) designs efficient state space layers that scale linearly with sequence length, using structured representations of the system matrices <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Subsequent works such as Mamba further enhance efficiency by introducing selective state space components that dynamically focus computation on relevant parts of the sequence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu and Dao, 2024</a>)</cite>. The S4ND model applies state space models to multidimensional signals such as images and videos, interpreting them as higher-dimensional spatiotemporal signals <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nguyen et al., 2022</a>)</cite> . Goel et al. propose a multi-scale architecture based on S4 designed specifically for raw audio waveform generation, and address instability issues in SSM sequence modeling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Goel et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. Mamba Mixer combines structured state space models with selective token and channel mixing via learned gating, enabling efficient and adaptive modeling of long sequences by focusing on relevant elements and features <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Behrouz et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Finally, simplified variants of state space layers have been proposed to reduce model complexity and improve training stability while retaining the key benefits of state space modeling in sequence tasks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">Smith et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Both S4 and our model exploit a <em id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">diagonal-plus-low-rank</em> (DPLR) structure to reduce the cost of inverting a dense <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\times N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\times N</annotation></semantics></math> matrix, using the Sherman-Morrison formula for efficiency: a diagonal part captures independent modes, and a rank-1 correction captures global interactions. In S4, the DPLR matrix models deterministic state dynamics, determining how past inputs influence future states. In our model, the DPLR structure appears in the noise covariance matrices in a stochastic differential equation (SDE) formulation, which allows us to represent how uncertainty propagates through the dynamics. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Our formulation relies on complex-valued weight matrices. Prior work on complex-valued neural networks includes studies of complex-valued activation functions, parameter initialization strategies, and the use of Wirtinger calculus, which treats complex parameters as pairs of real variables to enable effective gradient computation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">Trabelsi et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Barrachina et al., 2023</a>)</cite>,<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hammad, 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.5 </span>Attention as a Structured State Space Computation</h3>

<div id="S5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The attention mechanism was first introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bahdanau et al., 2016</a>)</cite> to improve neural machine translation by allowing models to dynamically focus on relevant input tokens, and was later generalized into the self-attention architecture of the Transformer by Vaswani et al, which became the foundation for modern large language models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib93" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Attention mechanisms can be interpreted through the lens of structured state space computations. Several recent works have explored these connections and proprosed structured alternatives to standard Transformer attention based on state space models. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Katharopoulos et al. propose a Linear Attention framework that approximates attention weights using kernel feature maps, enabling the Transformer to be expressed in a recurrent form. While this formulation offers computational benefits, it does not explicitly connect the recurrence to an underlying system dynamics model; rather, the recurrent structure serves primarily as an efficient implementation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Katharopoulos et al., 2020</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Dao and Gu establish that a state space model (SSM) transformation is mathematically equivalent to multiplication by an <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-sequentially semiseparable (SSS) matrix. This equivalence means that the recurrence inherent in SSMs can be expressed as a structured matrix multiplication, which directly parallels the matrix form of self-attention in Transformers. In particular, the attention matrix in a Transformer can be interpreted as a low-rank or structured matrix operating along the sequence dimension, making it amenable to the same efficient algorithms developed for SSS matrices. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao and Gu, 2024</a>)</cite>. While this formulation offers computational benefits and is grounded in a linear state-space model, it does not explicitly propagate uncertainty through the sequence or perform adaptive, residual-based reweighting. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Other recent works explore the integration of attention mechanisms with state space models. For example, the Dynamical Systems Framework (DSF) unifies attention, state space models, and recurrent networks under a common recurrent/convolutional form <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sieber et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Bick et al. focus on distilling quadratic self-attention into efficient SSMs, with the goal of matching the performance of Transformers while reducing computation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bick et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.6 </span>Dynamical Systems Perspectives on Attention</h3>

<div id="S5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention mechanisms have been studied through continuous-time and dynamical systems frameworks, modeling hidden states or latent dynamics via ordinary differential equations (ODEs) or stochastic processes to capture temporal dependencies, uncertainty, and adaptivity. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Stochastic Recurrent Networks (STORNs) combine RNNs with time-dependent latent variables and variational inference to model multimodal temporal dynamics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bayer and Osendorfer, 2015</a>)</cite>. Neural ODEs treat hidden states as continuous-time dynamics parameterized by a neural network and solved with an ODE solver <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. Neural Processes (NPs) and Neural ODE Processes (NDPs) extend this framework to learn distributions over functions or ODE trajectories, enabling uncertainty-aware predictions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Garnelo et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Norcliffe et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. Rubanova et al. introduce ODE-RNNs and Latent ODEs, continuous-time models that handle irregularly-sampled time series without discretization or imputation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rubanova et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. Physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) integrate differential equation constraints into neural networks to enforce physically consistent solutions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">Raissi et al., 2017</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Attentive Neural Processes (ANPs) introduce attention over context sets, while Attentive Differential Networks (ADNs) handle irregularly sampled data using continuous-time attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chien and Chen, 2023</a>)</cite>.
ACE-NODE and ANCDE integrate attention into ODE or controlled differential equation frameworks, learning attention dynamics continuously rather than via standard query-key comparisons <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jhin et al., 2021a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jhin et al., 2021b</a>)</cite>. Neural ODE Transformers and Hopfield Networks reinterpret attention as evolving or energy-based dynamical systems <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tong et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ramsauer et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. Continuous-discrete state space models and Structured Inference Networks combine latent continuous dynamics with discrete observations and approximate Bayesian filtering <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ansari et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Krishnan et al., 2016</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Geshkovski et al. model Transformers as interacting particle systems evolving on the unit sphere, and find that self-attention induces nonlinear dynamics leading to clustering of token embeddings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib101" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geshkovski et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Molina interprets Transformers geometrically, showing that LayerNorm constrains hidden states to a hypersphere and attention moves “word particles” along this surface <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Molina, 2023</a>)</cite>. Brody et al. show that LayerNorm shapes Transformer hidden states geometrically—projecting them onto a hyperplane and scaling them—which enhances the expressiveness of attention
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brody et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.7 </span>Diffusion, Score-Based Models, and Neural SDEs</h3>

<div id="S5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Song et al. showed that diffusion models can be formulated as continuous-time stochastic differential equations (SDEs), where learning the time-dependent score allows high-quality sampling via SDE solvers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib85" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2021</a>)</cite>. FIM-SDE estimates drift and diffusion functions from noisy, sparse SDE observations by learning a generalizable mapping from trajectories to underlying dynamical system parameters <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib79" title="" class="ltx_ref">Seifner et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Tzen and Raginsky show that deep latent Gaussian models converge in the infinite-layer limit to Itô SDEs with neural-network-parameterized drift and diffusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib92" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tzen and Raginsky, 2019</a>)</cite>. Wang and Yao combine neural processes with neural SDEs to improve uncertainty estimation on noisy or incomplete data, using attention-based NPs for multidimensional inputs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib96" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang and Yao, 2021</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.8 </span>Structuring Attention with Priors and Positional Biases</h3>

<div id="S5.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The original Transformer lacks built-in modeling of relative or absolute positions, relying instead on added absolute positional encodings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib93" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Several methods have proposed extending self-attention to efficiently incorporate relative position information. For example, Shaw et al. introduce a mechanism to encode relative distances between tokens directly into the attention computation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib80" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shaw et al., 2018</a>)</cite>. Transformer-XL introduces relative positional encodings, enabling the model to generalize to sequences longer than those seen during training <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. Su et al. apply a position-dependent rotation to each dimension of the query and key vectors before computing their dot products. This rotation encodes the relative distance between positions directly into the attention mechanism <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib87" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">A number of works reinterpret sequence modeling as a controlled, time-aware aggregation of past information, where learned or adaptive decay mechanisms regulate the influence of prior inputs over time. These models typically rely on heuristic, learned gating or decay functions for memory control, whereas we derive update weights from robust, data-driven precision estimates grounded in Bayesian filtering. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The Retentive Network (RetNet) introduces a retention mechanism that blends each token’s hidden state with an exponentially decaying summary of previous tokens. RetNet uses multiple attention heads, each having its own learned exponential decay rate, enabling multi-scale memory of different temporal lengths. Attention is applied with decay masks that enforce causality and decay over relative positions, while a gating mechanism modulates the retained summaries to improve expressivity and control the contribution of past information <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib89" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">GateLoop generalizes linear RNNs with data-controlled, time-varying state transition gates and introduces a surrogate attention mechanism where each input contributes via learned, input-dependent decay factors, capturing content and relative position <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Katsch, 2024</a>)</cite>. Gated Linear Attention (GLA) uses data-dependent, time-varying gates to modulate hidden state updates, combining fast, recurrent linear attention with input-adaptive, relative position-aware decay <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib100" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. The Real-Gated Linear Recurrent Unit (RG-LRU) introduces input and recurrence gates into a stable linear recurrent update, avoiding complexity from softmax attention or continuous-time dynamics. Griffin interleaves RG-LRU blocks with lightweight local attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">De et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. The Dynamically Context-Sensitive Time-Decay Attention mechanism learns a time-decay function to adjust attention weights <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib88" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2018</a>)</cite>. This approach focuses on temporal proximity rather than integrating known system dynamics. Performer approximates softmax attention with positive-definite kernel methods to achieve scalable, linear-time self-attention for long sequences <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Choromanski et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Several papers have explored element-wise (in the embedding dimension) attention mechanisms. McCarter investigates replacing scaled dot-product attention with negative-log Euclidean distance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">McCarter, 2023</a>)</cite>. Elliptical Attention replaces the traditional dot-product attention with a Mahalanobis distance-based mechanism <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nielsen et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Feng uses an exponentiated Euclidean distance as a similarity metric <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Feng, 2025</a>)</cite>. Bacochina et al. replace matrix multiplications with learned spatial weight arrays applied directly via element-wise multiplication, focusing attention along rows and columns <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bacochina and de Souza, 2023</a>)</cite>. Wu et al. introduce the DA-Transformer, which reweights attention scores using learnable functions of token distances <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib99" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2021</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.9 </span>Modeling Uncertainty in Neural Networks</h3>

<div id="S5.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Other approaches explicitly model uncertainty in neural networks and attention mechanisms. Foundational works such as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">MacKay, 1992</a>)</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Neal, 1996</a>)</cite> laid the groundwork for modern developments in approximate Bayesian inference in deep learning. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Chung et al. introduce the Variational Recurrent Neural Network (VRNN), which incorporates latent random variables into RNN hidden states to represent and propagate uncertainty in sequential data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chung et al., 2016</a>)</cite>. Fraccaro et al. introduce the stochastic recurrent neural network, a sequential model combining deterministic RNN states with stochastic latent variables, using structured variational inference to propagate uncertainty over time and improve sequence modeling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fraccaro et al., 2016</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The Bayesian Attention Mechanism (BAM) interprets attention weights as joint probabilities over token content and position, showing that positional encoding strategies correspond to specific priors and introducing a generalized Gaussian prior (GGD-BAM) that balances local and long-range dependencies
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bianchessi et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Litman shows that scaled dot-product attention is the exact solution to a one-sided entropic optimal transport problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Litman, 2025</a>)</cite>.
The Correlated Gaussian Process Transformer models self-attention as the cross-covariance between two correlated Gaussian processes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bui et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Ruan and Zhang analyze self-attention as a similarity-based information propagation process converging to a drift-diffusion or heat equation on a manifold <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ruan and Zhang, 2024</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Various approaches embed structured or probabilistic biases directly into attention mechanisms. For example, Probabilistic Transformers model attention as MAP inference in a Gaussian mixture model, with each key/value pair having its own precision parameter, updated via expectation-maximization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Movellan and Gabbur, 2020</a>)</cite>. Uncertainty-Aware Attention introduces input-specific uncertainty modeling through variational inference <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Heo et al., 2018</a>)</cite>. The Attention Gaussian Process (AGP) treats attention weights as probabilistic outputs from a sparse Gaussian process, with variational inference approximating the posterior <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schmidt et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. SLANG uses a diagonal plus low-rank covariance to efficiently estimate uncertainty in deep networks via natural-gradient variational inference <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mishkin et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Other recent probabilistic attention methods introduce uncertainty-aware mechanisms into Transformer-based architectures. These include the Uncertainty-Guided Probabilistic Transformer (UGPT) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, Attention Gaussian Process (AGP)
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schmidt et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, Gaussian Adaptive Attention (GAAM) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ioannides et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, the Correlated Gaussian Process Transformer (CGPT) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bui et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and Kernel-Eigen Pair Sparse Variational Gaussian Processes (KEP-SVGP) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.10 </span>Structured Low-Rank Covariances for Efficient Propagation</h3>

<div id="S5.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Several methods have been developed to efficiently represent and propagate high-dimensional covariance matrices using low-rank plus diagonal approximations in Riccati-like equations. Pnevmatikakis et al. propose a low-rank perturbative approach for Kalman Filtering and smoothing, approximating the state covariance as a small-rank update to the prior <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pnevmatikakis et al., 2014</a>)</cite>. Saibaba et al. represent the covariance as a weighted sum of the process noise and a low-rank term from a generalized eigenvalue problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib75" title="" class="ltx_ref">Saibaba et al., 2015</a>)</cite>. Bonnabel et al. approximate large, time-dependent PSD matrices with low-rank plus diagonal structures, allowing linear-time storage, inversion, and integration in high-dimensional Riccati flows <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bonnabel et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Schmidt et al. (2021) introduce the Rank-Reduced Kalman Filter, projecting the Lyapunov equations onto a low-rank manifold and updating only the covariance column space, reducing complexity from cubic to quadratic (or linear) while recovering the exact filter in the full-rank limit and outperforming ensemble-based approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schmidt et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS11" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.11 </span>Unrolling Optimization Algorithms and Connections to Attention</h3>

<div id="S5.SS11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unrolling iterative optimization algorithms into trainable networks began with frameworks like LISTA, which expresses the ISTA sparse-coding algorithm as a neural network with learned parameters <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gregor and LeCun, 2010</a>)</cite>. Deep Equilibrium Models (DEQs) extend this idea by solving a single equilibrium layer via root-finding, effectively modeling infinite-depth networks with constant memory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. Wang et al. study how attention can also be viewed as an unrolled iterative process: multi-head self-attention corresponds to iterative subspace denoising, compressing inputs into a low-rank manifold <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib95" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Discussion and Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work explores a connection between classical control theory and attention mechanisms by framing attention through the lens of linear dynamical systems and adaptive filtering. We show that attention arises naturally as the solution to a maximum likelihood estimation problem under a linear stochastic differential equation with structured system matrices and noise covariances, and discrete observations. In this view, the attention update implements a parallelized form of adaptive Kalman Filtering: each key-value pair is interpreted as a noisy observation of a latent state, and a precision-weighted Bayesian update aggregates evidence across all observations to refine the state estimate in a parallel manner. To the best of our knowledge, this view of attention as the MLE for a structured linear SDE has not appeared in the literature on attention mechanisms. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Several promising directions remain for future work. It should be straightforward to extend the method to the LQG controller, and the framework could also be adapted to reinforcement learning settings, where the dynamics-aware attention mechanism might provide more sample-efficient policy evaluation and state estimation in partially observed or noisy environments. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The closed-form expression for the propagated precision matrix, which assumes simultaneous diagonalizability, can be computed in <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(md)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(md)</annotation></semantics></math> time, whereas full integration and inversion in the general case requires <math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(md^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(md^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> time. Since our algorithm already involves <math id="S6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(md^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(md^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> matrix multiplications, moderately less efficient integration methods introduce a limited additional overhead. In particular, if we use a diagonalizable-plus-rank-1 state matrix <math id="S6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, covariance propagation can be computed efficiently by expressing the matrix exponential and integrals as a diagonal term plus a rank-1 outer-product correction, reducing complexity to <math id="S6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(md^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(md^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, though losing a fully closed form. We could also consider a generalization using the Jordan canonical form. Alternatively, differentiable numerical solvers for the differential Lyapunov equation, or unrolled iterations of specialized low-rank methods such as Krylov subspace techniques or ADI iterations could potentially be integrated directly into a neural network layer. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">To achieve the statistical accuracy of the full batch estimator while retaining the computational efficiency of a recursive filter, one could explore alternative unrolling strategies. These may include inner-loop iterations within each time step, linearizing weights around a precomputed batch solution, or hybrid schemes that propagate residual-dependent weights more globally across the trajectory. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">In this work, we assume the output matrix <math id="S6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐂</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is square and invertible, so the latent state is fully observable. We can account for partially observed states with projections or pseudo-inverses to map between measurement and latent spaces. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The layer-wise updates in our model perform adaptive denoising, which parallels the iterative refinement in diffusion models. Future work could investigate these connections. Finally, it would be worthwhile to explore whether linking attention to system dynamics and measurement confidence can improve model interpretability.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Background</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Linear Systems</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A continuous-time linear system is defined, in state-space form, as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex274" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex274.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\dot{x}}(t)=\mathbf{A}(t)\mathbf{x}(t)+\mathbf{B}(t)\mathbf{u}(t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\dot{x}}(t)=\mathbf{A}(t)\mathbf{x}(t)+\mathbf{B}(t)\mathbf{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex275" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex275.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}(t)=\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{x}(t)+\mathbf{D}(t)\mathbf{u}(t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}(t)=\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{x}(t)+\mathbf{D}(t)\mathbf{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The signals:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex276" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex276.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{x}(t):[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}^{N},\quad\textbf{u}(t):[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}^{M},\quad\textbf{y}(t):[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">u</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{x}(t):[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}^{N},\quad\textbf{u}(t):[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}^{M},\quad\textbf{y}(t):[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">are known as the <span id="A1.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">state</span>, <span id="A1.SS1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">input</span>, and <span id="A1.SS1.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">output</span>, respectively. In control applications, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is usually a feedback control term. <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}(t),\mathbf{B}(t),\mathbf{C}(t),\mathbf{D}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}(t),\mathbf{B}(t),\mathbf{C}(t),\mathbf{D}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are known as the state matrix, input matrix, output matrix, and direct transition matrix, respectively. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Letting <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{x}(t_{0})=\textbf{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{x}(t_{0})=\textbf{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the unique solution to the above system is given by:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex277" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex277.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{x}(t)=\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})\textbf{x}_{0}+\int_{t_{0}}^{t}\mathbf{\Phi}(t,\tau)\mathbf{B}(\tau)\textbf{u}(\tau)\,d\tau," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">u</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{x}(t)=\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})\textbf{x}_{0}+\int_{t_{0}}^{t}\mathbf{\Phi}(t,\tau)\mathbf{B}(\tau)\textbf{u}(\tau)\,d\tau,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex278" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex278.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{y}(t)=\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})\textbf{x}_{0}+\int_{t_{0}}^{t}\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{\Phi}(t,\tau)\mathbf{B}(\tau)\textbf{u}(\tau)\,d\tau+\mathbf{D}(t)\textbf{u}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">u</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">u</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{y}(t)=\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})\textbf{x}_{0}+\int_{t_{0}}^{t}\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{\Phi}(t,\tau)\mathbf{B}(\tau)\textbf{u}(\tau)\,d\tau+\mathbf{D}(t)\textbf{u}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, the <span id="A1.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">state transition matrix</span>, is the unique solution to</p>
<table id="A1.Ex279" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex279.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})=\mathbf{A}(t)\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})=\mathbf{A}(t)\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">with the initial condition <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ \mathbf{\Phi}(t_{0},t_{0})=\mathbf{I}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ \mathbf{\Phi}(t_{0},t_{0})=\mathbf{I}.</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">A linear time-invariant (LTI) system is one in which the matrices <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A},\mathbf{B},\mathbf{C},\textbf{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">D</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A},\mathbf{B},\mathbf{C},\textbf{D}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed, real-valued matrices, (i.e. not functions of time): <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}\in\mathbb{R}^{P\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}\in\mathbb{R}^{P\times N}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}\in\mathbb{R}^{P\times M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}\in\mathbb{R}^{P\times M}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">An autonomous LTI system <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\dot{x}}(t)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\dot{x}}(t)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is <span id="A1.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">asymptotically stable</span> (i.e. <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> approaches a stable equilibrium point as <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\rightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\rightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math>) if <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is Hurwitz, that is if every eigenvalue of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> has strictly negative real part. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">In an LTI system, the state transition matrix is given by:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex280" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex280.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})=e^{\mathbf{A}(t-t_{0})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Phi}(t,t_{0})=e^{\mathbf{A}(t-t_{0})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where the matrix exponential <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\mathbf{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>𝐌</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\mathbf{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex281" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex281.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\mathbf{M}}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{k!}\mathbf{M}^{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>𝐌</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\mathbf{M}}=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{k!}\mathbf{M}^{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonalizable, i.e. <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for some invertible <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and diagonal <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the matrix exponential can be computed cheaply using: <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\mathbf{A}}=\mathbf{S}e^{\bm{\Lambda}}\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>𝐀</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>𝚲</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\mathbf{A}}=\mathbf{S}e^{\bm{\Lambda}}\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. See also, standard references such as <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Antsaklis, 1997</a>)</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib83" title="" class="ltx_ref">Skogestad and Postlethwaite, 2005</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Stochastic Processes</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Many real-world systems are subject to uncertainty, which can be modeled as stochastic disturbances or process noise.
A continuous-time linear time-invariant system with additive Gaussian noise is described by the Itô stochastic differential equation (SDE):</p>
<table id="A1.Ex282" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex282.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}(t)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}(t)\,dt+\mathbf{B}\,d\mathbf{w}(t),\qquad\mathbf{z}(t_{k})=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}(t_{k})+\mathbf{v}(t_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}(t)=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}(t)\,dt+\mathbf{B}\,d\mathbf{w}(t),\qquad\mathbf{z}(t_{k})=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}(t_{k})+\mathbf{v}(t_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the latent state (or just state),</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}(t_{k})\in\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}(t_{k})\in\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math> is the observation at discrete times <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is the state matrix, and <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> is the input/noise matrix,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐂</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is the measurement matrix,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{w}(t)\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I}\,dt)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{w}(t)\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I}\,dt)</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard Wiener process,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}(t_{k})\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}(t_{k})\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{R})</annotation></semantics></math> is Gaussian measurement noise.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The continuous-time process noise covariance is defined as: <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}:=\mathbf{B}\mathbf{B}^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>𝐁𝐁</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}:=\mathbf{B}\mathbf{B}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discrete-time form.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sampling the SDE at equal intervals <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> yields a linear Gaussian state-space model:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex283" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex283.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}=\mathbf{A}_{d}\mathbf{x}_{i-1}+\bm{\eta}_{i},\qquad\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}_{i}+\mathbf{v}_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝜼</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}=\mathbf{A}_{d}\mathbf{x}_{i-1}+\bm{\eta}_{i},\qquad\mathbf{z}_{i}=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}_{i}+\mathbf{v}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\eta}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{Q}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝜼</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\eta}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{Q}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐑</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{i}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{R})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{d}=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{d}=e^{\mathbf{A}\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{d}=\int_{0}^{\Delta t}e^{\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{Q}\,e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}\tau}\,d\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{d}=\int_{0}^{\Delta t}e^{\mathbf{A}\tau}\mathbf{Q}\,e^{\mathbf{A}^{\top}\tau}\,d\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">This stochastic formulation provides the foundation for linear Gaussian estimation and filtering, including the classical Kalman Filter. Standard references include: <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Antsaklis, 1997</a>; <a href="#bib.bib83" title="" class="ltx_ref">Skogestad and Postlethwaite, 2005</a>; <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jazwinski, 1970</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>The Kalman Filter</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Filtering</span>, or <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">state estimation</span>, is the task of estimating the states <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{x}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{x}_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{x}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{x}_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> from noisy measurements <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{z}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{z}_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{z}_{1},\dots,\mathbf{z}_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The Kalman Filter is the optimal recursive estimator for a linear system with Gaussian noise. It maintains a mean estimate <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and a covariance <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> that quantifies uncertainty, and updates them sequentially as new measurements arrive. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The Kalman Filter alternates between prediction steps (propagating the state forward using the system model) and update steps (correcting the prediction using measurements).</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prediction Step:</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The model dynamics <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> propagate the previous state forward, and process noise <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> increases uncertainty:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex284" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex284.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k|k-1}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k-1},\qquad\mathbf{V}_{k|k-1}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}_{k-1}\mathbf{A}^{\top}+\mathbf{Q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐐</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k|k-1}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k-1},\qquad\mathbf{V}_{k|k-1}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}_{k-1}\mathbf{A}^{\top}+\mathbf{Q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Update Step:</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When a new measurement <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is available, the filter computes a Kalman gain <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> that weights the relative uncertainty in the prediction and the measurement:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex285" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex285.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}_{k}=\mathbf{V}_{k|k-1}\mathbf{C}^{\top}(\mathbf{C}\mathbf{V}_{k|k-1}\mathbf{C}^{\top}+\mathbf{R})^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐑</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}_{k}=\mathbf{V}_{k|k-1}\mathbf{C}^{\top}(\mathbf{C}\mathbf{V}_{k|k-1}\mathbf{C}^{\top}+\mathbf{R})^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The state and covariance are updated to reflect the new information:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex286" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex286.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k}=\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k|k-1}+\mathbf{K}_{k}(\mathbf{z}_{k}-\mathbf{C}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k|k-1}),\quad\mathbf{V}_{k}=(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{K}_{k}\mathbf{C})\mathbf{V}_{k|k-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k}=\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k|k-1}+\mathbf{K}_{k}(\mathbf{z}_{k}-\mathbf{C}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k|k-1}),\quad\mathbf{V}_{k}=(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{K}_{k}\mathbf{C})\mathbf{V}_{k|k-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">When the measurement is very precise (small <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}</annotation></semantics></math>), the gain <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is large, and the estimate relies more on the observation; when the model is more certain, the estimate relies more on the prediction. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We refer to <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k|k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k|k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{k|k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{k|k-1}</annotation></semantics></math> as the <span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">a priori</span> estimates of the state and covariance (i.e. those computed before accounting for the latest measurement), and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> as the <span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">a posteriori</span> estimates (which include the latest measurement). 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The difference between the actual measurement and the predicted measurement,
<math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{k}:=\mathbf{z}_{k}-\mathbf{C}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k|k-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{k}:=\mathbf{z}_{k}-\mathbf{C}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k|k-1},</annotation></semantics></math>
is called the <span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">innovation</span> and represents the new information that the measurement brings relative to the model prediction. The difference between the measurement and the updated estimate, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{k}:=\mathbf{z}_{k}-\mathbf{C}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{k}:=\mathbf{z}_{k}-\mathbf{C}\mathbf{\hat{x}}_{k},</annotation></semantics></math> is called the <span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">residual</span> and quantifies the discrepancy after incorporating the measurement. See also: <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jazwinski, 1970</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anderson and Moore, 1979</a>; <a href="#bib.bib86" title="" class="ltx_ref">Speyer, 2008</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Continuous-time Kalman Filtering.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For continuous-time linear stochastic systems, the Kalman Filter generalizes to the <span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Kalman–Bucy filter</span>. Given</p>
<table id="A1.Ex287" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex287.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}(t)=\mathbf{A}(t)\mathbf{x}(t)\,dt+\mathbf{B}(t)d\mathbf{w}(t),\quad\mathbf{z}(t)=\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{x}(t)+\mathbf{v}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}(t)=\mathbf{A}(t)\mathbf{x}(t)\,dt+\mathbf{B}(t)d\mathbf{w}(t),\quad\mathbf{z}(t)=\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{x}(t)+\mathbf{v}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with process noise covariance <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}(t)=\mathbf{B}(t)\mathbf{B}(t)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}(t)=\mathbf{B}(t)\mathbf{B}(t)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and measurement noise covariance <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐑</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, the state estimate <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> evolves according to:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex288" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex288.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}\mathbf{\hat{x}}(t)=\mathbf{A}(t)\mathbf{\hat{x}}(t)+\mathbf{K}(t)\big(\mathbf{z}(t)-\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{\hat{x}}(t)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}\mathbf{\hat{x}}(t)=\mathbf{A}(t)\mathbf{\hat{x}}(t)+\mathbf{K}(t)\big(\mathbf{z}(t)-\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{\hat{x}}(t)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the continuous-time Kalman gain <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex289" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex289.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}(t)=\mathbf{V}(t)\mathbf{C}(t)^{\top}\mathbf{R}^{-1}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}(t)=\mathbf{V}(t)\mathbf{C}(t)^{\top}\mathbf{R}^{-1}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and the covariance <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the differential Riccati equation:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex290" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex290.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}\mathbf{V}(t)=\mathbf{A}(t)\mathbf{V}(t)+\mathbf{V}(t)\mathbf{A}(t)^{\top}-\mathbf{V}(t)\mathbf{C}(t)^{\top}\mathbf{R}^{-1}(t)\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{V}(t)+\mathbf{Q}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}\mathbf{V}(t)=\mathbf{A}(t)\mathbf{V}(t)+\mathbf{V}(t)\mathbf{A}(t)^{\top}-\mathbf{V}(t)\mathbf{C}(t)^{\top}\mathbf{R}^{-1}(t)\mathbf{C}(t)\mathbf{V}(t)+\mathbf{Q}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Adaptive Filtering</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adaptive filtering is the task of estimating or tracking a signal in real time when the system dynamics or noise statistics are unknown or time-varying. Unlike the Kalman Filter, which assumes known dynamics and noise covariances, adaptive filters adjust their parameters dynamically to minimize the mean squared error (MSE) between the filter output and a desired signal. They are called “adaptive” because the filter adapts to changes in the system or environment, usually in an online fashion.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Iteratively Reweighted Least Squares (IRLS) and Robust Kalman Filtering</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Iteratively Reweighted Least Squares (IRLS) is a general approach for solving weighted least squares problems, particularly when robustness to outliers is desired. Given a set of residuals <math id="A1.SS4.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, IRLS solves:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex291" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex291.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\hat{x}}=\arg\min_{\mathbf{x}}\sum_{i}w_{i}\,\|\mathbf{r}_{i}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\hat{x}}=\arg\min_{\mathbf{x}}\sum_{i}w_{i}\,\|\mathbf{r}_{i}(\mathbf{x})\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the weights <math id="A1.SS4.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are updated iteratively based on the current residuals, often using an influence function <math id="A1.SS4.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\mathbf{r}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\mathbf{r}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> such that: <math id="A1.SS4.SSSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=\psi(\mathbf{r}_{i})/\mathbf{r}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=\psi(\mathbf{r}_{i})/\mathbf{r}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>The Attention Mechanism</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Self-attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib93" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al., 2023</a>)</cite> models pairwise interactions between elements in a sequence of length <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> by computing learned similarity scores between <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional embeddings of each token. Each token is associated with a query, key, and value, stacked as <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}_{Q},\mathbf{X}_{K},\mathbf{X}_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}_{Q},\mathbf{X}_{K},\mathbf{X}_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and linearly projected:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex292" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex292.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}=\mathbf{X}_{Q}\mathbf{W}_{Q},\quad\mathbf{K}=\mathbf{X}_{K}\mathbf{W}_{K},\quad\mathbf{V}=\mathbf{X}_{V}\mathbf{W}_{V}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}=\mathbf{X}_{Q}\mathbf{W}_{Q},\quad\mathbf{K}=\mathbf{X}_{K}\mathbf{W}_{K},\quad\mathbf{V}=\mathbf{X}_{V}\mathbf{W}_{V}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">And the output is a weighted sum:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex293" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex293.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{K}^{\top})\mathbf{V},\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐐𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{K}^{\top})\mathbf{V},\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">A row of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex294" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex294.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{i}=\sum_{j=1}^{m}p_{ij}\mathbf{v}_{j},\quad p_{ij}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{q}_{i}^{\top}\mathbf{k}_{j})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{i}=\sum_{j=1}^{m}p_{ij}\mathbf{v}_{j},\quad p_{ij}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{q}_{i}^{\top}\mathbf{k}_{j}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Attention can be viewed as a special-case of a <span id="A1.SS5.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">precision-weighted average</span>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex295" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex295.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{i}=\Big(\sum_{j}\mathbf{\tilde{P}}_{ij}\Big)^{-1}\sum_{j}\mathbf{\tilde{P}}_{ij}\mathbf{x}_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{i}=\Big(\sum_{j}\mathbf{\tilde{P}}_{ij}\Big)^{-1}\sum_{j}\mathbf{\tilde{P}}_{ij}\mathbf{x}_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where each <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{P}}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{P}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive definite matrix. This tensor formulation allows the model not only to scale each input differently, but also to rotate and stretch it in feature space. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">For example, if we set:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex296" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex296.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{P}}_{ij}=\frac{\mathbf{P}_{ij}}{1+\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}_{ij}\mathbf{r}_{ij}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{P}}_{ij}=\frac{\mathbf{P}_{ij}}{1+\mathbf{r}_{ij}^{\top}\mathbf{P}_{ij}\mathbf{r}_{ij}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.6" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> diagonal and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{ij}=\mathbf{q}_{i}-\mathbf{k}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{ij}=\mathbf{q}_{i}-\mathbf{k}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, the normalization reduces to a simple row-wise form, leading to an element-wise version of attention. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The standard dot-product attention used in Transformers corresponds to:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex297" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex297.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\tilde{P}}_{ij}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{q}_{i}^{\top}\mathbf{k}_{j})\,\mathbf{I}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\tilde{P}}_{ij}=\text{softmax}(\mathbf{q}_{i}^{\top}\mathbf{k}_{j})\,\mathbf{I}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>State Space Models</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In discrete time, a linear time-invariant (LTI) system can be written as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex298" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex298.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{k}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}_{k-1}+\mathbf{B}\mathbf{u}_{k},\quad\mathbf{y}_{k}=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}_{k}+\mathbf{D}\mathbf{u}_{k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐁𝐮</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐃𝐮</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{k}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}_{k-1}+\mathbf{B}\mathbf{u}_{k},\quad\mathbf{y}_{k}=\mathbf{C}\mathbf{x}_{k}+\mathbf{D}\mathbf{u}_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the hidden state, <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> the input, and <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> the output. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The LTI structure allows explicit unrolling of the dynamics:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex299" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex299.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{k}=\mathbf{\bar{C}}\mathbf{\bar{A}}^{k}\mathbf{x}_{0}+\sum_{j=1}^{k}\mathbf{\bar{C}}\mathbf{\bar{A}}^{k-j}\mathbf{\bar{B}}\mathbf{u}_{j}=\sum_{j=0}^{k}\mathbf{\bar{h}}_{j}\mathbf{u}_{k-j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{k}=\mathbf{\bar{C}}\mathbf{\bar{A}}^{k}\mathbf{x}_{0}+\sum_{j=1}^{k}\mathbf{\bar{C}}\mathbf{\bar{A}}^{k-j}\mathbf{\bar{B}}\mathbf{u}_{j}=\sum_{j=0}^{k}\mathbf{\bar{h}}_{j}\mathbf{u}_{k-j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{h}}_{j}=\mathbf{\bar{C}}\mathbf{\bar{A}}^{j}\mathbf{\bar{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{h}}_{j}=\mathbf{\bar{C}}\mathbf{\bar{A}}^{j}\mathbf{\bar{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the impulse response. This shows that the system output can be viewed as a discrete convolution: <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}=\mathbf{\bar{h}}*\mathbf{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐡</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}=\mathbf{\bar{h}}*\mathbf{u}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be computed efficiently in the frequency domain via the Fourier or <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>-transform.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Neural State Space Models</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recurrent models such as SSMs are prone to vanishing or exploding gradients. The HiPPO framework addresses this by constructing the state matrix <math id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> based on orthogonal polynomial projections, such as Legendre polynomials. The resulting HiPPO matrices optimally compress a continuous-time signal into a fixed-dimensional state while preserving information about the past. This ensures that the hidden state maintains a summary of the input sequence over long horizons, alleviating vanishing gradients <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2020</a>)</cite>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Directly computing <math id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> involves repeated multiplications by <math id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The S4 model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al., 2022</a>)</cite> exploits the <math id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>-transform to convert the recurrence into a convolution in the frequency domain:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex300" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex300.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}(z)=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\mathbf{y}_{k}z^{-k}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\mathbf{h}_{i}z^{-i}\sum_{k=i}^{\infty}\mathbf{u}_{k-i}z^{-(k-i)}=\mathcal{\hat{K}}(z)\mathbf{U}(z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝐡</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}(z)=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\mathbf{y}_{k}z^{-k}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\mathbf{h}_{i}z^{-i}\sum_{k=i}^{\infty}\mathbf{u}_{k-i}z^{-(k-i)}=\mathcal{\hat{K}}(z)\mathbf{U}(z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the transfer function is:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex301" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex301.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{K}}(z)=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\mathbf{\bar{C}}\mathbf{\bar{A}}^{i}\mathbf{\bar{B}}z^{-i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{K}}(z)=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\mathbf{\bar{C}}\mathbf{\bar{A}}^{i}\mathbf{\bar{B}}z^{-i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">S4 further exploits the structure of <math id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> for computational efficiency. If <math id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> is diagonal, the transfer function simplifies:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex302" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex302.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{\hat{K}}_{\mathbf{\Lambda}}(z)=c(z)\sum_{i}\frac{\mathbf{C}_{i}\mathbf{B}_{i}}{g(z)-\mathbf{\Lambda}_{i}}=c(z)\cdot k_{z,\mathbf{\Lambda}}(\mathbf{C},\mathbf{B})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝚲</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{\hat{K}}_{\mathbf{\Lambda}}(z)=c(z)\sum_{i}\frac{\mathbf{C}_{i}\mathbf{B}_{i}}{g(z)-\mathbf{\Lambda}_{i}}=c(z)\cdot k_{z,\mathbf{\Lambda}}(\mathbf{C},\mathbf{B}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSSx1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">allowing parallel computation across state dimensions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Diagonal Plus Low-Rank (DPLR) and Normal Plus Low-Rank (NPLR) Structures</h4>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To capture richer dynamics while retaining efficiency, S4 introduces a <span id="A1.SS6.SSSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Diagonal Plus Low-Rank</span> (DPLR) parameterization of the state matrix:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex303" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex303.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\bm{\Lambda}-\mathbf{P}\mathbf{Q}^{\dagger}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐐</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\bm{\Lambda}-\mathbf{P}\mathbf{Q}^{\dagger}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSSx2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This generalizes to <span id="A1.SS6.SSSx2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Normal Plus Low-Rank</span> (NPLR) matrices:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex304" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex304.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{U}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{U}^{\dagger}-\mathbf{P}\mathbf{Q}^{\dagger}=\mathbf{U}(\bm{\Lambda}-\mathbf{\tilde{P}}\mathbf{\tilde{Q}}^{\dagger})\mathbf{U}^{\dagger}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐐</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{U}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{U}^{\dagger}-\mathbf{P}\mathbf{Q}^{\dagger}=\mathbf{U}(\bm{\Lambda}-\mathbf{\tilde{P}}\mathbf{\tilde{Q}}^{\dagger})\mathbf{U}^{\dagger},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSSx2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">showing that any NPLR matrix is unitarily similar to a DPLR matrix. This structure allows the HiPPO matrix to be embedded within S4 efficiently. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The matrix inversion lemma (Sherman–Morrison–Woodbury) enables efficient computation of <math id="A1.SS6.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{\Lambda}-\mathbf{P}\mathbf{Q}^{\dagger})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐏𝐐</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{\Lambda}-\mathbf{P}\mathbf{Q}^{\dagger})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The Mamba models extend S4 by combining NPLR structure with careful numerical techniques to further improve stability and long-range memory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu and Dao, 2024</a>)</cite>. These models achieve performance competitive with Transformers on a variety of sequence modeling tasks.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Material</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Separable Approximation of the Full Precision Kernel</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex305"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex305.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{D}[i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\Big[\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{D}[i,j]=\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\|^{2}+\sum_{k}\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\|^{2}\Big[\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex306"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex306.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-2\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi><mi>P</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-2\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\mathcal{K}_{\mathbf{qk}}^{P}[k,|i-j|]\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If we could factor the precision tensor into separate <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> terms <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}[:,i,j]=c+\mathbf{f}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{g}[k,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}[:,i,j]=c+\mathbf{f}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{g}[k,j]</annotation></semantics></math>, then we could write:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex307"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex307.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{D}[i,j]=c\sum_{k}\big\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\big\|^{2}\Big[\big\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\big\|^{2}+\big\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\big\|^{2}-2\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{D}[i,j]=c\sum_{k}\big\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\big\|^{2}\Big[\big\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\big\|^{2}+\big\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\big\|^{2}-2\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex308"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex308.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{k}\big\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\big\|^{2}\Big[\mathbf{f}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{g}[k,j]\big\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\big\|^{2}+\mathbf{f}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{g}[k,j]\big\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\big\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{k}\big\|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}[k,i]\big\|^{2}\Big[\mathbf{f}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{g}[k,j]\big\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\big\|^{2}+\mathbf{f}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{g}[k,j]\big\|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\big\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex309"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex309.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-2\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{f}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{g}[k,j]\cdot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐟</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-2\mathrm{Re}\left(\mathbf{\bar{\hat{Z}}}_{\mathbf{q}}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{f}[k,i]\cdot\mathbf{g}[k,j]\cdot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}[k,j]\right)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This can now be simplified into a sum of matrix products, which can be cheaply computed without storing a <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times m\times m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times m\times m</annotation></semantics></math> dimensional tensor:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex310"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex310.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{D}=c\Big[\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\big)^{\top}\big|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big|^{2}+\sum_{k}\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\odot\big|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\big|^{2}\big)-2\mathrm{Re}\Big(\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\odot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\big)^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\Big)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{D}=c\Big[\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\big)^{\top}\big|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big|^{2}+\sum_{k}\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\odot\big|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\big|^{2}\big)-2\mathrm{Re}\Big(\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\odot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\big)^{\dagger}\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\Big)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex311"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex311.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\odot\mathbf{f}\big)^{\top}\big(\big|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big|^{2}\odot\mathbf{g}\big)+\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\odot\big|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\big|^{2}\odot\mathbf{f}\big)^{\top}\mathbf{g}-2\mathrm{Re}\Big(\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\odot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\odot\mathbf{f}\big)^{\dagger}\big(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\odot\mathbf{g}\big)\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐟</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐟</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>𝚽</mi><mi>𝐪𝐤</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐪</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐟</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐤</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\odot\mathbf{f}\big)^{\top}\big(\big|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\big|^{2}\odot\mathbf{g}\big)+\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\odot\big|\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\big|^{2}\odot\mathbf{f}\big)^{\top}\mathbf{g}-2\mathrm{Re}\Big(\big(\big|\bm{\Phi}_{\mathbf{qk}}\big|^{2}\odot\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{q}}\odot\mathbf{f}\big)^{\dagger}\big(\mathbf{\hat{Z}}_{\mathbf{k}}\odot\mathbf{g}\big)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Recall that the precision is:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex312" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex312.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}[:,i,j]=\left(\bm{\lambda}_{C}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}\odot\frac{\mathbf{1}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})(t_{i}-t_{j})}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})}+\bm{\lambda}_{\Gamma}\odot e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})(t_{i}-t_{j})}\right)^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}[:,i,j]=\left(\bm{\lambda}_{C}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}\odot\frac{\mathbf{1}-e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})(t_{i}-t_{j})}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})}+\bm{\lambda}_{\Gamma}\odot e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})(t_{i}-t_{j})}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\lambda}_{eff}=\frac{\bm{\lambda}_{C}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\lambda}_{eff}=\frac{\bm{\lambda}_{C}^{2}\odot\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}}{-2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex313" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex313.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}[:,i,j]=\left(\bm{\lambda}_{eff}+(-\bm{\lambda}_{eff}+\bm{\lambda}_{\Gamma})e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})(t_{i}-t_{j})}\right)^{-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}[:,i,j]=\left(\bm{\lambda}_{eff}+(-\bm{\lambda}_{eff}+\bm{\lambda}_{\Gamma})e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})(t_{i}-t_{j})}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex314" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex314.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=\frac{1}{\bm{\lambda}_{eff}}\left(1+\bm{\lambda}_{r}e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})\Delta t}\right)^{-1},\quad\text{where: }\,\bm{\lambda}_{r}=-1+\frac{\bm{\lambda}_{\Gamma}}{\bm{\lambda}_{eff}}&gt;-1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where: </mtext><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\frac{1}{\bm{\lambda}_{eff}}\left(1+\bm{\lambda}_{r}e^{2\mathrm{Re}(\bm{\lambda})\Delta t}\right)^{-1},\quad\text{where: }\,\bm{\lambda}_{r}=-1+\frac{\bm{\lambda}_{\Gamma}}{\bm{\lambda}_{eff}}&gt;-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">We use the separable approximation:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex315" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex315.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+ae^{bx})^{-1}\approx 1-ce^{-dx}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+ae^{bx})^{-1}\approx 1-ce^{-dx},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">with constants chosen to match the value and slope at <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">We obtain the following separable approximation:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex316" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex316.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{C}(\Delta t)\approx\frac{1}{\bm{\lambda}_{eff}}\left(1-\frac{\bm{\lambda}_{r}}{1+\bm{\lambda}_{r}}e^{\frac{2Re(\bm{\lambda})\Delta t}{1+\bm{\lambda}_{r}}}\right)=\frac{1}{\bm{\lambda}_{eff}}\left[1-\left(1-\frac{\bm{\lambda}_{eff}}{\bm{\lambda}_{\Gamma}}\right)e^{-\frac{\bm{\lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}}{\bm{\lambda}_{\Gamma}}\Delta t}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{C}(\Delta t)\approx\frac{1}{\bm{\lambda}_{eff}}\left(1-\frac{\bm{\lambda}_{r}}{1+\bm{\lambda}_{r}}e^{\frac{2Re(\bm{\lambda})\Delta t}{1+\bm{\lambda}_{r}}}\right)=\frac{1}{\bm{\lambda}_{eff}}\left[1-\left(1-\frac{\bm{\lambda}_{eff}}{\bm{\lambda}_{\Gamma}}\right)e^{-\frac{\bm{\lambda}_{C}^{2}\bm{\lambda}_{\Omega}}{\bm{\lambda}_{\Gamma}}\Delta t}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Approximating the Batch MLE with a Recursive Filter</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define a re-weighted Kalman gain:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex317" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex317.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}_{i}:=\frac{e^{\tau_{s}w_{i}}}{\tilde{p}_{i}^{+}\,\sigma_{V}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}_{i}:=\frac{e^{\tau_{s}w_{i}}}{\tilde{p}_{i}^{+}\,\sigma_{V}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The precision and mean updates are:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex318" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex318.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{i}^{+}=p_{i}^{-}+\tilde{K}_{i},\quad\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{+}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}+\tilde{K}_{i}(\mathbf{z}_{i}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-})=\tilde{K}_{i}\mathbf{z}_{i}+(1-\tilde{K}_{i})\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{i}^{+}=p_{i}^{-}+\tilde{K}_{i},\quad\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{+}=\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}+\tilde{K}_{i}(\mathbf{z}_{i}-\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-})=\tilde{K}_{i}\mathbf{z}_{i}+(1-\tilde{K}_{i})\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with the prior propagated through the dynamics:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex319" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex319.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}=\bm{\Phi}\,\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i-1}^{+}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚽</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{-}=\bm{\Phi}\,\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i-1}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Recursive substitution gives a weighted sum of all past observations:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex320" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex320.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{+}=\sum_{j=0}^{i}\left[\tilde{K}_{j}\prod_{k=j+1}^{i}(1-\tilde{K}_{k})\,\bm{\Phi}\right]\mathbf{z}_{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚽</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{+}=\sum_{j=0}^{i}\left[\tilde{K}_{j}\prod_{k=j+1}^{i}(1-\tilde{K}_{k})\,\bm{\Phi}\right]\mathbf{z}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}_{k}\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}_{k}\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> is small, this is approximately:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex321" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex321.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{+}\approx\sum_{j=0}^{i}\tilde{K}_{j}\,e^{\Lambda\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{z}_{j}=\sum_{j=0}^{i}\tilde{K}_{j}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">≈</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\bar{z}}_{i}^{+}\approx\sum_{j=0}^{i}\tilde{K}_{j}\,e^{\Lambda\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{z}_{j}=\sum_{j=0}^{i}\tilde{K}_{j}\mathbf{\hat{z}}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Hence, if:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex322" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex322.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}_{j}\approx\frac{w_{ij}/\sigma_{V}^{2}}{\sum_{j}w_{ij}/\sigma_{V}^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}_{j}\approx\frac{w_{ij}/\sigma_{V}^{2}}{\sum_{j}w_{ij}/\sigma_{V}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">then we recover an approximation of the batch MLE.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Normal plus Rank-1 Noise Covariance</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we explore a generalization of the RT-SDE model by considering a normal-plus-rank-1 structure for <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our goal is to determine whether relaxing the strict radial-tangential decomposition introduces additional expressivity in the propagated covariance or the resulting MLE. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Recall that:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex323" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex323.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j}):=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}(\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}(t_{j}+\tau)\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>†</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j}):=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}(\mathbf{S}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}(t_{j}+\tau)\mathbf{S}^{-\dagger})e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let us now assume that <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> is normal plus rank-1, i.e. <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}=\mathbf{S}\left(\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}+\mathbf{q}\mathbf{q}^{\dagger}\right)\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>𝐪𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}=\mathbf{S}\left(\bm{\Lambda}_{Q}+\mathbf{q}\mathbf{q}^{\dagger}\right)\mathbf{S}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math>. We already derived the diagonal part. The rank-1 part is:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex324" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex324.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}\big(\mathbf{q}\mathbf{q}^{\dagger}\big)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐪𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}\big(\mathbf{q}\mathbf{q}^{\dagger}\big)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex325" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex325.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}\big(e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}\mathbf{q}\big)\big(e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}\mathbf{q}\big)^{\dagger}d\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐪</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}\big(e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}\mathbf{q}\big)\big(e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\tau}\mathbf{q}\big)^{\dagger}d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">If we take: <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}(t_{j}+\tau)=e^{\bm{\Lambda}(\Delta t_{ij}+\tau)}\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}(t_{j}+\tau)=e^{\bm{\Lambda}(\Delta t_{ij}+\tau)}\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> moves with the LTI’s flow, this becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex326" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex326.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}d\tau=e^{\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}|\Delta t_{ij}|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩𝐩</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩𝐩</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}d\tau=e^{\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}|\Delta t_{ij}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">If we assume that <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}=\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}=\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}^{\dagger}=-\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}^{\dagger}=-\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex327" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex327.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha\tau}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\tau}\big(\mathbf{q}\mathbf{q}^{\dagger}\big)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐪𝐪</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha\tau}e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\tau}\big(\mathbf{q}\mathbf{q}^{\dagger}\big)e^{-\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\tau}d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}(t_{j}+\tau)=ae^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}(\Delta t_{ij}+\tau)}\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐩</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}(t_{j}+\tau)=ae^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}(\Delta t_{ij}+\tau)}\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex328" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex328.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ae^{\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha\tau}d\tau=a\frac{e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}-1}{-2\alpha}e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩𝐩</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩𝐩</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ae^{\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\int_{0}^{|\Delta t_{ij}|}e^{-2\alpha\tau}d\tau=a\frac{e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}-1}{-2\alpha}e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Altogether, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex329" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex329.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})=\sigma^{2}\kappa_{B}(\Delta t_{ij})\Big(\mathbf{I}+ae^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩𝐩</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}B}(t_{i},t_{j})=\sigma^{2}\kappa_{B}(\Delta t_{ij})\Big(\mathbf{I}+ae^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Assuming measurement noise with a rank-1 component aligned with the rank-1 component of the process noise, the propagated measurement covariance is:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex330" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex330.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\Big[\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\kappa_{B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big(\mathbf{I}+ae^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)+\eta^{2}\Big(\mathbf{I}+be^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)\Big]e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩𝐩</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩𝐩</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=e^{-\bm{\Lambda}\Delta t_{ij}}\Big[\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\kappa_{B}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big(\mathbf{I}+ae^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)+\eta^{2}\Big(\mathbf{I}+be^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}\Delta t_{ij}}\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}e^{\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)\Big]e^{-\bm{\Lambda}^{\dagger}\Delta t_{ij}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex331" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex331.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big(\mathbf{I}+a\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}\Big)+\eta^{2}e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\Big(\mathbf{I}+b\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩𝐩</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩𝐩</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big(\mathbf{I}+a\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}\Big)+\eta^{2}e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\Big(\mathbf{I}+b\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex332" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex332.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)+\eta^{2}e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)\mathbf{I}+\Big(a\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)+b\eta^{2}e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐩𝐩</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)+\eta^{2}e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)\mathbf{I}+\Big(a\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)+b\eta^{2}e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)\mathbf{p}\mathbf{p}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">In particular, letting <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}=\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐩</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}=\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and setting <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\frac{\sigma_{r}^{2}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\frac{\sigma_{r}^{2}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\frac{\eta_{r}^{2}-\eta_{t}^{2}}{\eta_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\frac{\eta_{r}^{2}-\eta_{t}^{2}}{\eta_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, this becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex333" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex333.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma_{t}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)+\eta_{t}^{2}e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)\mathbf{I}+\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}(\sigma_{r}^{2}-\eta_{t}^{2})\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)+(\eta_{r}^{2}-\eta_{t}^{2})e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>†</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(\Delta t_{ij})=\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}\sigma_{t}^{2}\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)+\eta_{t}^{2}e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)\mathbf{I}+\Big(\lambda_{C}^{2}(\sigma_{r}^{2}-\eta_{t}^{2})\kappa_{F}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)+(\eta_{r}^{2}-\eta_{t}^{2})e^{-2\alpha\Delta t_{ij}}\Big)\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}\mathbf{u}_{\mathbf{s}i}^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex334" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex334.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger})+\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)(\mathbf{I}-\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger})+\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.9" class="ltx_p">Hence, the normal plus rank-1 process noise covariance model reduces exactly to the RT-SDE case: while <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is not restricted to be a unit vector, any scaling of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math> can be absorbed into the radial noise parameters, so the model introduces no additional degrees of freedom beyond RT-SDE. The requirement that <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}</annotation></semantics></math> flow with the LTI dynamics (which is necessary for the integral to be tractable), with <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\alpha\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, constrains the rank-1 component to rotate with the system, forcing the normal-plus-rank-1 noise model to align exactly with the RT-SDE structure.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Expressivity of Radial-Tangential SDEs</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1: Expressivity of Deterministic RT-SDEs.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">Let <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a diagonalizable matrix, with eigendecomposition <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{S}\bm{\Lambda}\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}=\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1},\dots,\lambda_{d})\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}=\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1},\dots,\lambda_{d})\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a sequence of matrices <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{\ell}=\mathbf{S}(\alpha_{\ell}\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega\ell})\mathbf{S}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{\ell}=\mathbf{S}(\alpha_{\ell}\mathbf{I}+\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega\ell})\mathbf{S}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega\ell}=\mathrm{diag}(i\omega_{\ell,1},\dots,i\omega_{\ell,d})\in i\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\Omega\ell}=\mathrm{diag}(i\omega_{\ell,1},\dots,i\omega_{\ell,d})\in i\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a choice of block durations <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex335" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex335.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\|e^{\mathbf{A}t_{k}}-\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}e^{\mathbf{A}_{\ell}\Delta t}\right\|&lt;\epsilon,\quad\forall k=1,\dots,m." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|e^{\mathbf{A}t_{k}}-\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}e^{\mathbf{A}_{\ell}\Delta t}\right\|&lt;\epsilon,\quad\forall k=1,\dots,m.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof Sketch.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Each <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> generates dynamics:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex336" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex336.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\mathbf{A}_{\ell}\Delta t}=\mathbf{S}\,\mathrm{diag}\big(e^{(\alpha_{\ell}+i\omega_{\ell,1})\Delta t},\dots,e^{(\alpha_{\ell}+i\omega_{\ell,d})\Delta t}\big)\mathbf{S}^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\mathbf{A}_{\ell}\Delta t}=\mathbf{S}\,\mathrm{diag}\big(e^{(\alpha_{\ell}+i\omega_{\ell,1})\Delta t},\dots,e^{(\alpha_{\ell}+i\omega_{\ell,d})\Delta t}\big)\mathbf{S}^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Each diagonal entry corresponds to a 1D complex exponential in the eigenbasis. By choosing sufficiently many blocks <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and appropriately selecting <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\ell,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\ell,k}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can approximate:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex337" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex337.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\lambda_{k}t_{j}}\approx\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}e^{(\alpha_{\ell}+i\omega_{\ell,k})\Delta t},\quad\forall k,j," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">≈</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\lambda_{k}t_{j}}\approx\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}e^{(\alpha_{\ell}+i\omega_{\ell,k})\Delta t},\quad\forall k,j,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">to arbitrary precision. Mapping back to the original basis with <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> yields the desired approximation. Hence, for any finite set of times, a product of radial-tangential blocks can approximate the target flow arbitrarily closely. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark:</span>
If we have <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> heads, each producing its own low-dimensional output, stacking them allows combinations of rotations and scalings from different subspaces to mix. The resulting flow in the original <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional space can approximate much richer dynamics than a single high-dimensional LTI with the same number of blocks. The effective number of distinct transformations is roughly the number of heads times the number of layers. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2: Expressivity of RT-SDE Covariance.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">Let <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a symmetric positive definite (SPD) matrix and fix a time <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a number of heads <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and associated RT-SDE parameters:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex338" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex338.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i}),\sigma_{Vr,h}^{2},\sigma_{Vt,h}^{2}\}_{h=1}^{H}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i}),\sigma_{Vr,h}^{2},\sigma_{Vt,h}^{2}\}_{h=1}^{H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">such that the RT-SDE covariance satisfies:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex339" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex339.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|\bm{\Sigma}(t_{i})-\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\big\|&lt;\varepsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|\bm{\Sigma}(t_{i})-\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}\big\|&lt;\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.Ex340" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex340.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}(t_{i})=\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sigma_{Vt,h}^{2}\mathbf{I}+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\beta_{h}\,\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})^{\top},\quad\beta_{h}=\sigma_{Vr,h}^{2}-\sigma_{Vt,h}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}(t_{i})=\sum_{h=1}^{H}\sigma_{Vt,h}^{2}\mathbf{I}+\sum_{h=1}^{H}\beta_{h}\,\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})^{\top},\quad\beta_{h}=\sigma_{Vr,h}^{2}-\sigma_{Vt,h}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<br class="ltx_break">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof Sketch:</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Each head <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> contributes an SPD term of the form:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex341" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex341.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{I}+\big(\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)-\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\big)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚲</mi><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>C</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>𝐬</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}_{\mathbf{V}}^{C}(t_{i},t_{j})=\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\mathbf{I}+\big(\sigma_{Vr}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)-\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\big)\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})\mathbf{u_{s}}(t_{i})^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.8" class="ltx_p">i.e. a rank-1 correction of identity aligned with the current state direction <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}(t_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}(t_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">The total propagated covariance is the sum of the individual head covariances, assuming the uncertainty sources for each head are uncorrelated:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex342" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex342.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}(t_{i})\;=\;\Big(\sum_{h}\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big)\mathbf{I}+\sum_{h}\beta_{h}\,\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})^{\top},\quad\beta_{h}=\sigma_{Vr}^{2}-\sigma_{Vt}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}(t_{i})\;=\;\Big(\sum_{h}\sigma_{Vt}^{2}(|\Delta t_{ij}|)\Big)\mathbf{I}+\sum_{h}\beta_{h}\,\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})^{\top},\quad\beta_{h}=\sigma_{Vr}^{2}-\sigma_{Vt}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.9" class="ltx_p">At a fixed time <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can construct any target SPD matrix <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> using the RT-SDE heads as follows. Let <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\min}=\lambda_{\min}(\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}),\quad\sum_{h}\sigma_{Vt}^{2}=\sigma_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>h</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\min}=\lambda_{\min}(\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}),\quad\sum_{h}\sigma_{Vt}^{2}=\sigma_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that the isotropic contributions sum to the minimal eigenvalue. Consider the spectral decomposition of the shifted matrix:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex343" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex343.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}-\sigma_{\min}\mathbf{I}=\sum_{h}(\lambda_{h}-\sigma_{\min})\,\mathbf{v}_{h}\mathbf{v}_{h}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}-\sigma_{\min}\mathbf{I}=\sum_{h}(\lambda_{h}-\sigma_{\min})\,\mathbf{v}_{h}\mathbf{v}_{h}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.10" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{v}_{h}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{v}_{h}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are the eigenvectors of <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. Setting <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})=\mathbf{v}_{h},\,\beta_{h}=\lambda_{h}-\sigma_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})=\mathbf{v}_{h},\,\beta_{h}=\lambda_{h}-\sigma_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex344" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex344.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h}\sigma_{Vt}^{2}\mathbf{I}+\sum_{h}\beta_{h}\,\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})^{\top}=\sigma_{\min}\mathbf{I}+(\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}-\sigma_{\min}\mathbf{I})=\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h}\sigma_{Vt}^{2}\mathbf{I}+\sum_{h}\beta_{h}\,\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})\mathbf{u}_{h}(t_{i})^{\top}=\sigma_{\min}\mathbf{I}+(\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}-\sigma_{\min}\mathbf{I})=\bm{\Sigma}^{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark:</span> Note that this only holds at a fixed time, since <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{h}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{h}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> evolves according to the underlying LTI dynamics, so we cannot freely choose the propagated covariance at all times independently. Nevertheless, this shows that the RT-SDE model is substantially more flexible than a diagonalizable LTI-SDE with isotropic noise, for which the propagated measurement covariance remains isotropic in the eigenbasis.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
